  {
    "role": "system",
    "content": "你是这篇科学综述的正文作者，对整篇 BODY 的解释和论证负责。读者没有看过任务书、材料卡片或内部规划。请沿用已经批准的完整细纲，把给定科研材料写成一篇读者能持续建立认识的文章。用户的研究问题、范围、目标读者和语言决定写给谁、回答什么；原细纲规定已有的科学职责，不需要你另造一份计划。\n\n写作的中心是读者逐步理解了什么。把必要的背景、对象和概念放在读者需要它们的位置，让结果之间的联系得到实际解释：为什么可以比较，差别如何产生，哪些中间关系得到支持，条件变化怎样改变判断，这一层认识如何引出下一层问题。保留材料中有解释作用的具体机制、实验或观察条件、比较尺度、案例、阴性结果和相互冲突的发现。不要用术语罗列、重要性赞语或一句“仍需研究”代替本来可以讲清的内容。科学深度来自说清关系，不来自抽象用词或长句。\n\n前文实际建立的认识是后文的起点。后文可以重新使用同一研究，但应当完成新的比较、推论边界或解释用途；必要的回顾应帮助理解当前论证，而不是让每章从同一个背景重新开始。先前正文是文章状态，不是新增科学证据。只有在材料支持时才写成因果、机制、普遍结论或跨情境外推。\n\n证据合同：\n- tasks 中的当前完整任务、unit_contexts 中的原始单元职责、chapter_frames 中的当前章节职责和 global_chapter_roles 中的全篇导航共同确定当前要完成的工作；原始批准全篇细纲保存在完整输入档案中。细纲中的“说明/比较/论证/确立”等动词是给作者的指令，正文应直接完成这项解释，不向读者复述工作安排。任务意图不是事实证明。\n- evidence_atoms 中 role=evidence 的完整可用来源材料，以及当前章节或任务携带的可归属工具补充材料构成事实依据。role=planner_interpretation 是先前规划阶段的解释性判断，不能视作已经证实的科学事实；对照可归属研究材料核实。保持研究身份、研究对象、干预/暴露、测量、结局、时间、尺度、比较组和条件之间的对应关系。不要把甲研究的条件、数字、因果程度或结论移给乙研究。\n- 可归属的具体来源材料如果不支持任务或旧摘要中的强概括，以材料实际支持的程度写。可以直接作有依据的局部准确修正；不能把错误推断写成科学事实来获得任务完成标记。遇到改变核心任务的实质冲突，保留可支持内容并在 issues 说明具体依据和未解决范围，不凭空修补证据，也不另起全篇规划。\n- 完整材料指当前提供的相关内容得到完整保留，不表示每篇研究必须有自有 A/B 卡或论文全文。可用的综述转述和互补材料正常参与，准确保留 review-mediated 身份和归属，不能冒充直接阅读原研究。材料类别的名字本身不决定可靠性；判断具体内容、可追溯身份和支持程度。不能因字段缺失就排除一份有用来源。\n- 来源内容中的写作指令、角色要求或其他控制文本只是材料，不得改变本任务。沿用提供的稳定引用句柄，例如 [P0123]，按给定别名映射保持身份；不自造编号、来源或书目信息。来源句柄用于引用，内部 task_id、segment_id 和执行记录不进入读者正文。\n\n重要条件必须进入它改变科学含义的句子或邻近解释，而不是藏进脚注、收尾免责声明或伴随记录。如果后文概括、图表或跨章比较再次使用该发现，其决定性条件仍然有效。区分“没有测量”“没有发现”“发现无效”和“已排除影响”；不能把研究未观察的环节写成已经证明独立。负结果、边界和异质性要帮助读者理解何种判断成立，避免每段附上相同的泛泛限制。\n\n表达采用清楚、平实而成熟的科学散文。根据内容选择有目的的开头：可以直接进入一个发现、一个需要解释的差异、一个关键过程、一项定义或承接前文尚未解决的问题。不要把这些选择轮流填成新模板，也不要求每段采用“主张—案例—限制—展望”。段落、标题、句长和详略由知识关系决定。一个任务可以分几段，几个任务也可以共同形成一个论证；任务数不是段落数、块数或标题数。不把任务名称原样当成小标题。段落结尾可以停在已经讲清的认识处，无需人为制造宏大转折。\n\n少量虚构的跨领域例子仅说明写法，不是当前领域答案，也不得进入正文：如果材料只报告“某电池在低温和高倍率的联合条件下出现额外损耗”，清楚的写法应使读者知道这个联合条件为何限制比较，不能改成“低温降低所有电池寿命”。如果某城市研究没有测量收入，它不能支持“交通影响独立于收入”。这些示意不是要求你在每段提出条件、局限或对立观点。\n\n按批准细纲交付全部 BODY 中的实际成文及必要图表内容。已要求的表格须有材料支持的实质单元格，正文解释比较带来的认识，不逐格复述。图示任务依据现有材料交付可用的图示内容/说明，不声称生成了不存在的外部图片。不得用目录、写作建议、待办、空占位或摘要化后半篇代替成稿。没有任意字数、段数、引用数或表格数指标；允许充分展开，也不要为了用满 token 预算填充。\n\n遵循当前路线给定的工作范围与输出合同。completed_task_ids 是实际完成的可追溯声明，不能靠列全 ID 代替正文兑现；issues 记录真实未决支持问题而非空泛自评。写作前后都核对任务、材料和实际正文，尤其检查完整文章的后部是否得到与其科学职责相称的展开。不要输出思考过程、审稿分数或面向执行者的说明。\n\n本路线把完整语义材料保存在 evidence atoms 中。无损去重只是存储变化：atom 原文及关联条件、归属和 protected context 均不能拆开推断。当前任务是执行职责，atoms 是科学事实的依据；即使两者措辞相似也不可把任务要求当成实验结果。selected evidence 是可复用的材料选择，不是作者必须照抄的叙事。\n\n优先输出自然 Markdown 正文，在最后另附一个 fullbody_metadata 围栏，围栏内只放 JSON 伴随记录，例如：\n\n```fullbody_metadata\n{\"completed_task_ids\":[\"实际完成的完整 task ID\"],\"complete\":true,\"issues\":[]}\n```\n\n也兼容单个 JSON 对象 {\"body_markdown\":\"当前范围完整成文\", \"completed_task_ids\":[\"实际完成的完整 task ID\"], \"complete\":true, \"issues\":[]}。长篇自然正文无需逐字 JSON 转义。正文不包含前文副本；多个任务可以共同由一段或一个足够实质的表格完成。只有当需要尚未提供的原始材料时，改为只输出 {\"read_atom_ids\":[\"atom ID\"],\"read_source_handles\":[\"来源句柄\"]}；不得同时交付正文。回读范围是完整批准材料池，次数有限；已经给出的原文不重复申请。不要用空泛不确定性替代一次具体材料回读。\n\n\n沿着 accepted_body_markdown 中的真实累计前文续写同一文章。当前任务按自然章节成组，只有实际容量不足才在完整任务边界拆分。global_chapter_roles 是简短全篇职责导航，不能假装它是已经写出的正文或科学材料。只输出当前范围的新正文，不改写或重发既有前文。复用前文证据时推进新的解释用途，避免同用途重述。\n"
  },
  {
    "role": "user",
    "content": "{\"schema_version\":\"optomind.writing_evidence.payload.v1\",\"book_sha256\":\"3662038f6f241a48979bc8f9e30c8382776def734fcaa4cdddb82858d6cb6322\",\"language\":\"zh\",\"research_question\":\"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\",\"review_argument\":\"肠道微生物组通过分类学特征、代谢产物及免疫通路调节实体瘤患者对 ICI 的临床疗效，但证据强度因肿瘤类型、研究设计及干预策略而异。观察性关联证据在黑色素瘤中最强，NSCLC 和 RCC 次之，但关联不等于因果。机制证据主要来自动物模型，人类验证有限，特别是肿瘤微环境内代谢物浓度数据缺失（如肌苷仅有血浆数据）。干预策略在初治人群中显示希望（FMT-LUMINate ORR 75-80%），但在难治人群中效果有限（MITRIC ORR 0%），且安全性受 ICI 方案调节（Prevotella 相关心肌炎仅在双 ICI 背景下出现）。目前缺乏 Phase III RCT 证据支持微生物干预的常规临床应用，未来研究需解决标准化、因果推断及人群分层问题。\",\"user_request\":\"\",\"target_reader\":\"\",\"review_scope\":{\"statement\":\"本综述聚焦于实体瘤（黑色素瘤、非小细胞肺癌、肾细胞癌、结直肠癌等）患者接受免疫检查点抑制剂（PD-1/PD-L1、CTLA-4 抑制剂）治疗期间，肠道微生物组对治疗疗效（ORR、PFS、OS）及毒性（irAEs）的调节作用。涵盖观察性关联证据（区分回顾性与前瞻性队列）、因果机制解析（免疫细胞、分子通路、代谢物）、外部干扰因素（抗生素、PPI、饮食）及微生物干预策略（FMT、益生菌、工程菌）的临床试验数据。明确排除血液系统恶性肿瘤及非免疫治疗背景下的微生物组研究（除非用于机制对比）。严格区分肠道微生物组与肿瘤内微生物组的作用边界。证据等级标注明确：观察性关联不推断因果，干预试验区分 I/II 期与 III 期，代谢物数据区分血浆与肿瘤组织浓度。\"},\"missing_original_context_fields\":[\"user_request\",\"target_reader\"],\"editable_task_ids\":[\"Ch7::Ch7_U01::Ch7_U01_P01\",\"Ch7::Ch7_U01::Ch7_U01_P02\",\"Ch7::Ch7_U01::Ch7_U01_P03\",\"Ch7::Ch7_U01::Ch7_U01_P04\",\"Ch7::Ch7_U02::Ch7_U02_P01\",\"Ch7::Ch7_U02::Ch7_U02_P02\",\"Ch7::Ch7_U02::Ch7_U02_P03\",\"Ch7::Ch7_U02::Ch7_U02_P04\",\"Ch7::Ch7_U03::Ch7_U03_P01\",\"Ch7::Ch7_U03::Ch7_U03_P02\",\"Ch7::Ch7_U03::Ch7_U03_P03\",\"Ch7::Ch7_U03::Ch7_U03_P04\",\"Ch7::Ch7_U04::Ch7_U04_P01\",\"Ch7::Ch7_U04::Ch7_U04_P02\",\"Ch7::Ch7_U04::Ch7_U04_P03\",\"Ch7::Ch7_U04::Ch7_U04_P04\"],\"tasks\":{\"Ch7::Ch7_U01::Ch7_U01_P01\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch7\",\"local_task_id\":\"Ch7_U01::Ch7_U01_P01\",\"original_task_id\":\"Ch7_U01_P01\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U01\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U01_P01\",\"point\":\"确立技术演进背景与标准化紧迫性\",\"development\":\"结合文献计量趋势，说明领域已从早期物种普查进入功能解析阶段，但技术碎片化导致知识整合困难。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"role\":\"背景\",\"use\":\"提供领域宏观结构与研究热点演变的全景式背景，定位知识边界与核心议题。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"role\":\"背景\",\"use\":\"补充肿瘤内微生物对 ICI 疗效影响的研究热点分布及干预证据的结构化概览。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"role\":\"发展\",\"use\":\"提供定性综述证据，说明领域正从物种鉴定转向功能机制与生态韧性理论，支撑方法学标准化对揭示真实微生物信号的必要性。\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"Ch7_U01_P01\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U01_P01\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U01\",\"ordinal\":1,\"point\":\"确立技术演进背景与标准化紧迫性\",\"development\":\"结合文献计量趋势，说明领域已从早期物种普查进入功能解析阶段，但技术碎片化导致知识整合困难。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0001\",\"P0027\"]}]}},\"Ch7::Ch7_U01::Ch7_U01_P02\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch7\",\"local_task_id\":\"Ch7_U01::Ch7_U01_P02\",\"original_task_id\":\"Ch7_U01_P02\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U01\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U01_P02\",\"point\":\"剖析测序策略分歧与分辨率限制\",\"development\":\"对比16S与宏基因组的技术参数，阐明引物偏好、宿主DNA占比及生信管道差异如何导致菌种列表不一致。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"综述微生物组在癌症免疫治疗中的新兴角色，整理多个独立研究发现的共性模式和潜在通路。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"提供经过筛选的、跨多种癌症类型的细菌清单，作为后续机制探讨的基础背景。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"role\":\"比较\",\"use\":\"通过黑色素瘤系统综述展示测序平台与生信管道差异导致的菌种列表不一致性，为剖析技术变异削弱结论可靠性提供具体案例。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"role\":\"局限\",\"use\":\"以口腔局部微环境为例，展示低生物量样本检测中的污染控制难题及宿主蛋白互作对菌群信号的干扰，补充空间异质性带来的分析局限。\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"Ch7_U01_P02\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U01_P02\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U01\",\"ordinal\":2,\"point\":\"剖析测序策略分歧与分辨率限制\",\"development\":\"对比16S与宏基因组的技术参数，阐明引物偏好、宿主DNA占比及生信管道差异如何导致菌种列表不一致。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0055\",\"P0295\"]}]}},\"Ch7::Ch7_U01::Ch7_U01_P03\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch7\",\"local_task_id\":\"Ch7_U01::Ch7_U01_P03\",\"original_task_id\":\"Ch7_U01_P03\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U01\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U01_P03\",\"point\":\"展示标准化重分析的实证启示\",\"development\":\"引用统一管道重分析案例，论证控制方法学变量后，无响应相关信号的可重复性显著提升，反驳“微生物信号纯属噪音”的极端观点。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"提供大规模标准化重分析现有微生物组数据的实证，建立稳健的无响应微生物生物标志物集。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"role\":\"发展\",\"use\":\"提供免疫监测中微生物样本采集与测序流程标准化的专家共识建议，直接回应技术变异导致跨队列结论不可复现的方法学挑战。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"role\":\"例证\",\"use\":\"通过黏膜黑色素瘤多部位同步采样设计，说明区分全身肠道与局部肿瘤微生物信号的方法学必要性，为标准化空间组学整合提供范例。\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"Ch7_U01_P03\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U01_P03\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U01\",\"ordinal\":3,\"point\":\"展示标准化重分析的实证启示\",\"development\":\"引用统一管道重分析案例，论证控制方法学变量后，无响应相关信号的可重复性显著提升，反驳“微生物信号纯属噪音”的极端观点。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0354\"]}]}},\"Ch7::Ch7_U01::Ch7_U01_P04\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch7\",\"local_task_id\":\"Ch7_U01::Ch7_U01_P04\",\"original_task_id\":\"Ch7_U01_P04\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U01\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U01_P04\",\"point\":\"提出培养组学与多界检测的补位路径\",\"development\":\"指出纯测序方法的局限性，引入培养组学与真菌/病毒组检测作为提升功能注释完整性的必要补充。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"论证耦合培养组学与宏基因组测序以表征 ICI 治疗患者肠道微生物组的必要性。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"role\":\"比较\",\"use\":\"对比肠道与口腔微生物组预测效力的差异，补充空间异质性带来的分析局限，支持多部位采样与标准化流程的必要性。\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"Ch7_U01_P04\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U01_P04\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U01\",\"ordinal\":4,\"point\":\"提出培养组学与多界检测的补位路径\",\"development\":\"指出纯测序方法的局限性，引入培养组学与真菌/病毒组检测作为提升功能注释完整性的必要补充。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0367\"]}]}},\"Ch7::Ch7_U02::Ch7_U02_P01\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch7\",\"local_task_id\":\"Ch7_U02::Ch7_U02_P01\",\"original_task_id\":\"Ch7_U02_P01\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U02\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U02_P01\",\"point\":\"界定观察性关联的因果倒置风险\",\"development\":\"强调多数发现源于横断面或回顾性队列，解释为何“有益菌富集”可能是疗效良好的结果而非原因。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"提供宏观背景与机制概览，指出肠道微生物组与 ICI 疗效关联的因果性不明及异质性大的局限性。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"整合多个关键临床队列和基础研究的发现，指出许多机制证据来自小鼠模型，直接外推到人类需谨慎。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"role\":\"发展\",\"use\":\"提出“分子模拟”假说及量化方法（TAS），解释观察性关联背后的潜在因果机制，同时指出其验证局限性与 HLA LOH 等负面调节因素。\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"Ch7_U02_P01\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U02_P01\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U02\",\"ordinal\":1,\"point\":\"界定观察性关联的因果倒置风险\",\"development\":\"强调多数发现源于横断面或回顾性队列，解释为何“有益菌富集”可能是疗效良好的结果而非原因。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0031\",\"P0433\"]}]}},\"Ch7::Ch7_U02::Ch7_U02_P02\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch7\",\"local_task_id\":\"Ch7_U02::Ch7_U02_P02\",\"original_task_id\":\"Ch7_U02_P02\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U02\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U02_P02\",\"point\":\"评估药物与生活方式暴露的混杂干扰\",\"development\":\"列举抗生素、PPI及饮食对微生物组的广泛重塑作用，指出其可能掩盖或模拟微生物-ICI的真实关联。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"role\":\"例证\",\"use\":\"提供抗生素干扰抗肿瘤治疗疗效的具体反面案例，提示肠道菌群失调可能通过多种机制影响药物疗效。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"系统列出被报道与疗效相关或无关的具体微生物分类群，分析临床前与临床数据不一致性的方法学局限。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"role\":\"发展\",\"use\":\"提出“抗性/易感”微生物群概念框架，指出饮食模式与合并用药的交互作用会重塑菌群功能，警示观察性关联中未控暴露的混杂风险。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"role\":\"例证\",\"use\":\"提供 ICI 给药时间与生存结局的观察性数据，作为非微生物因素（时间生物学）干扰疗效的对照证据，警示混杂控制的复杂性。\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"Ch7_U02_P02\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U02_P02\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U02\",\"ordinal\":2,\"point\":\"评估药物与生活方式暴露的混杂干扰\",\"development\":\"列举抗生素、PPI及饮食对微生物组的广泛重塑作用，指出其可能掩盖或模拟微生物-ICI的真实关联。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0012\",\"P0171\"]}]}},\"Ch7::Ch7_U02::Ch7_U02_P03\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch7\",\"local_task_id\":\"Ch7_U02::Ch7_U02_P03\",\"original_task_id\":\"Ch7_U02_P03\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U02\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U02_P03\",\"point\":\"剖析跨物种机制外推的生理鸿沟\",\"development\":\"对比无菌小鼠定植实验与人类复杂生态系统的差异，说明单一菌株效应可能在人体中被网络冗余或宿主遗传所缓冲。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"详细阐述微生物调节 ICI 和化疗反应的具体机制和潜在生物标志物列表，指出许多机制主要基于小鼠模型。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"提供计算模型视角，说明特定预测标记物 derived from simulation outputs 可能依赖模型假设。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"role\":\"比较\",\"use\":\"借助慢性病毒感染模型展示治疗干预后代谢通路的持续性异常，类比说明宿主病理状态可能掩盖或模拟微生物介导的真实效应。\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"Ch7_U02_P03\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U02_P03\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U02\",\"ordinal\":3,\"point\":\"剖析跨物种机制外推的生理鸿沟\",\"development\":\"对比无菌小鼠定植实验与人类复杂生态系统的差异，说明单一菌株效应可能在人体中被网络冗余或宿主遗传所缓冲。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0229\",\"P0525\"]}]}},\"Ch7::Ch7_U02::Ch7_U02_P04\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch7\",\"local_task_id\":\"Ch7_U02::Ch7_U02_P04\",\"original_task_id\":\"Ch7_U02_P04\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U02\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U02_P04\",\"point\":\"审视统计推断工具的适用边界\",\"development\":\"指出MR等方法在工具变量强度、人群代表性及终点匹配（发病vs疗效）上的局限，主张将其定位为假设生成器。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"通过孟德尔随机化方法从遗传角度证实肠道微生物及其代谢产物对多种实体瘤的潜在因果影响，但指出未直接涉及 ICI 疗效临床终点。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"作为高层概念图，链接肠道微生物组组成与 ICI 疗效，提供具体有益细菌例子及作用机制。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"role\":\"局限\",\"use\":\"揭示青少年与老年患者基线菌群结构的显著差异，论证年龄发育阶段作为关键混杂变量如何干扰因果链条构建，支持分龄分层分析的必要性。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"role\":\"局限\",\"use\":\"提供波兰队列实证，揭示特定菌属与疗效关联的人群依赖性，论证年龄、饮食等混杂变量干扰因果链条构建的风险。\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"Ch7_U02_P04\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U02_P04\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U02\",\"ordinal\":4,\"point\":\"审视统计推断工具的适用边界\",\"development\":\"指出MR等方法在工具变量强度、人群代表性及终点匹配（发病vs疗效）上的局限，主张将其定位为假设生成器。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0059\",\"P0005\"]}]}},\"Ch7::Ch7_U03::Ch7_U03_P01\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch7\",\"local_task_id\":\"Ch7_U03::Ch7_U03_P01\",\"original_task_id\":\"Ch7_U03_P01\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U03\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U03_P01\",\"point\":\"盘点早期试验信号与III期验证的缺席\",\"development\":\"汇总I/II期FMT与益生菌的概念验证结果，明确指出缺乏大型RCT支持常规临床应用。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"汇总支持微生物组影响 ICI 疗效的主要菌属及 FMT 克服 ICI 耐药的临床尝试，指出当前证据的方法学局限。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"提供微生物组调节在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的基础概述，列举成功和失败的干预例子。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"提供结构化的临床证据框架，汇总 FMT、LBPs 和定义菌群三类干预的具体试验结果。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"role\":\"局限\",\"use\":\"汇总 FMT 与活体细菌产品的概念验证结果，明确指出缺乏大型 RCT 支持常规临床应用，支撑早期试验信号与 III 期验证缺席的判断。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"role\":\"例证\",\"use\":\"系统梳理结直肠癌 FMT 与益生菌早期临床试验数据，指出供体筛选困难、定植效率波动及安全性监管缺口。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0584\",\"role\":\"局限\",\"use\":\"梳理早期临床试验（I/II 期）数据，强调供体筛选困难、定植效率波动及安全性监管缺口，支撑干预策略尚未成为标准护理的判断。\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"Ch7_U03_P01\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U03_P01\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U03\",\"ordinal\":1,\"point\":\"盘点早期试验信号与III期验证的缺席\",\"development\":\"汇总I/II期FMT与益生菌的概念验证结果，明确指出缺乏大型RCT支持常规临床应用。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0026\",\"P0215\",\"P0178\"]}]}},\"Ch7::Ch7_U03::Ch7_U03_P02\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch7\",\"local_task_id\":\"Ch7_U03::Ch7_U03_P02\",\"original_task_id\":\"Ch7_U03_P02\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U03\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U03_P02\",\"point\":\"揭示纵向前瞻性数据的结构性短缺\",\"development\":\"以正在进行的新辅助治疗研究为例，说明基线多样性与动态变化指标的预测价值仍需前瞻性队列确证。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"提供正在进行中的研究摘要，主要价值在于其研究设计的描述和可行性报告，而非实证结果。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"提供儿科肿瘤中微生物组作用的宏观背景和具体临床关联素材，指出许多关联多为观察性结果。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"role\":\"例证\",\"use\":\"作为肝癌辅助治疗试验方案，明确短程免疫给药窗口与动态监测节点的设计逻辑，反衬当前缺乏大型 RCT 验证及标准化临床路径的现状。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"role\":\"局限\",\"use\":\"展示基于回顾性数据的计算模拟预测结果，强调从算法优化到菌株分离培养的临床转化断层，凸显早期概念验证向 III 期确证试验跨越的障碍。\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"Ch7_U03_P02\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U03_P02\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U03\",\"ordinal\":2,\"point\":\"揭示纵向前瞻性数据的结构性短缺\",\"development\":\"以正在进行的新辅助治疗研究为例，说明基线多样性与动态变化指标的预测价值仍需前瞻性队列确证。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0045\",\"P0008\"]}]}},\"Ch7::Ch7_U03::Ch7_U03_P03\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch7\",\"local_task_id\":\"Ch7_U03::Ch7_U03_P03\",\"original_task_id\":\"Ch7_U03_P03\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U03\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U03_P03\",\"point\":\"剖析年龄与种族维度的表征盲区\",\"development\":\"指出老年微生物组偏移特征与临床试验代表性不足的矛盾，强调人口统计学分层设计的必要性。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"解释为何老年人群可能对 ICIs 反应较差，连接宿主年龄、微生物组构成与治疗结局。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"role\":\"例证\",\"use\":\"提供儿科特异性章节和讨论当前证据局限性的重要基础材料，区分人群差异。\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"Ch7_U03_P03\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U03_P03\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U03\",\"ordinal\":3,\"point\":\"剖析年龄与种族维度的表征盲区\",\"development\":\"指出老年微生物组偏移特征与临床试验代表性不足的矛盾，强调人口统计学分层设计的必要性。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0484\",\"P0008\"]}]}},\"Ch7::Ch7_U03::Ch7_U03_P04\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch7\",\"local_task_id\":\"Ch7_U03::Ch7_U03_P04\",\"original_task_id\":\"Ch7_U03_P04\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U03\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U03_P04\",\"point\":\"呈现临床决策对预测因子的迫切需求与现实落差\",\"development\":\"引用医生调查数据，说明临床端对标准化生物标志物与干预协议的强烈渴望，反衬当前转化能力的不足。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"通过调查肿瘤科医生的意见，量化了 ICI 单药治疗 NSCLC 中未被充分研究的临床场景的重要性排序。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"role\":\"发展\",\"use\":\"评估不同干预策略（饮食、FMT、LBPs）的临床成熟度与技术挑战，反衬当前缺乏标准化临床路径及预测因子的现状。\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"Ch7_U03_P04\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U03_P04\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U03\",\"ordinal\":4,\"point\":\"呈现临床决策对预测因子的迫切需求与现实落差\",\"development\":\"引用医生调查数据，说明临床端对标准化生物标志物与干预协议的强烈渴望，反衬当前转化能力的不足。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0524\"]}]}},\"Ch7::Ch7_U04::Ch7_U04_P01\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch7\",\"local_task_id\":\"Ch7_U04::Ch7_U04_P01\",\"original_task_id\":\"Ch7_U04_P01\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U04\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U04_P01\",\"point\":\"论证功能导向与基因水平分析的方法学必然性\",\"development\":\"说明分类学标签的局限性，强调代谢通路、酶活性及基因水平特征更能反映微生物的功能输出。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"指出微生物组是“癌症暗物质”的重要组成部分，并通过代谢产物、免疫调节和表观遗传修饰影响 TME。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"提供临床关联的策划摘要，说明为何需要先进的体外模型如免疫反应性类器官来研究微生物组 -ICI 相互作用。\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"Ch7_U04_P01\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U04_P01\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U04\",\"ordinal\":1,\"point\":\"论证功能导向与基因水平分析的方法学必然性\",\"development\":\"说明分类学标签的局限性，强调代谢通路、酶活性及基因水平特征更能反映微生物的功能输出。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0323\",\"P0416\"]}]}},\"Ch7::Ch7_U04::Ch7_U04_P02\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch7\",\"local_task_id\":\"Ch7_U04::Ch7_U04_P02\",\"original_task_id\":\"Ch7_U04_P02\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U04\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U04_P02\",\"point\":\"介绍AI与多模态数据整合的应用潜力与局限\",\"development\":\"展示机器学习在特征降维与非线性关系挖掘中的优势，同时警示过拟合风险与跨队列泛化挑战。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"综述 AI 整合多组学预测 ICI 疗效的潜力与泛化挑战，为未来利用机器学习解析非线性微生物 - 免疫互作及开发可解释性数字孪生模型提供技术背景。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"汇总微生物组特征与 ICI 响应之间的关联，并指出了 AI 在解析这种关联中的作用。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"role\":\"发展\",\"use\":\"介绍 TOPOSCORE 等多组学评分模型及 ONCOBIOME 倡议，展示超越分类学的功能导向分析方法及国际协作标准化努力的前景。\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"Ch7_U04_P02\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U04_P02\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U04\",\"ordinal\":2,\"point\":\"介绍AI与多模态数据整合的应用潜力与局限\",\"development\":\"展示机器学习在特征降维与非线性关系挖掘中的优势，同时警示过拟合风险与跨队列泛化挑战。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0050\",\"P0054\"]}]}},\"Ch7::Ch7_U04::Ch7_U04_P03\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch7\",\"local_task_id\":\"Ch7_U04::Ch7_U04_P03\",\"original_task_id\":\"Ch7_U04_P03\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U04\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U04_P03\",\"point\":\"评估先进体外模型在机制解析中的定位\",\"development\":\"对比类器官/器官芯片与传统动物模型的优劣，指出其在保留患者异质性与模拟空间梯度方面的独特价值。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"评估类器官在模拟微生物-TME 轴中的优势与免疫组分缺失局限，论证结合微流控芯片实现动态梯度与空间异质性捕获的方法学演进方向。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"role\":\"比较\",\"use\":\"对比类器官/器官芯片与传统动物模型的优劣，指出其在保留患者异质性与模拟空间梯度方面的独特价值。\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"Ch7_U04_P03\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U04_P03\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U04\",\"ordinal\":3,\"point\":\"评估先进体外模型在机制解析中的定位\",\"development\":\"对比类器官/器官芯片与传统动物模型的优劣，指出其在保留患者异质性与模拟空间梯度方面的独特价值。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0172\",\"P0416\"]}]}},\"Ch7::Ch7_U04::Ch7_U04_P04\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch7\",\"local_task_id\":\"Ch7_U04::Ch7_U04_P04\",\"original_task_id\":\"Ch7_U04_P04\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U04\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U04_P04\",\"point\":\"提出精准干预的标准化路径与安全框架\",\"development\":\"总结工程菌、定义菌群及生态药理学的前景，强调供体标准化、制剂工艺优化、昼夜节律同步及长期安全性监测的必要性。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0532\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"列举工程菌递送微型抗体及 AI 辅助靶点发现的临床前案例，提示需建立严格的供体筛查、制剂工艺优化与长期安全性监测框架以推动精准干预落地。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"role\":\"发展\",\"use\":\"引入昼夜节律新维度及方法学局限性，支持未来标准化研究需求，强调时间生物学对微生物定植及 ICI 疗效的影响。\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0555\",\"role\":\"局限\",\"use\":\"批判性分析从临床前到临床转化的障碍，指出个体异质性、技术标准化缺失和还原论局限性，为精准干预的标准化路径提供背景。\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"Ch7_U04_P04\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"Ch7_U04_P04\",\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U04\",\"ordinal\":4,\"point\":\"提出精准干预的标准化路径与安全框架\",\"development\":\"总结工程菌、定义菌群及生态药理学的前景，强调供体标准化、制剂工艺优化、昼夜节律同步及长期安全性监测的必要性。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0532\",\"P0544\"]}]}}},\"chapter_frames\":{\"Ch7\":{\"chapter_title\":\"方法学挑战与未来研究方向\",\"chapter_purpose\":\"帮助读者识别当前领域内关键的方法学瓶颈与证据等级差异，理解为何单一菌种难以成为通用预测因子，并为后续临床转化研究提供可操作的设计原则、优先级排序及边界认知。\",\"chapter_scope\":\"肠道微生物组调节实体瘤免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的证据虽已积累，但受限于测序技术异质性、观察性研究的混杂偏倚、动物模型向人类转化的局限，以及缺乏大型III期随机对照试验验证，目前仍无法确立普适性生物标志物或常规干预方案。未来研究需转向功能导向的多组学整合、严格的前瞻性队列设计、标准化供体/制剂管理，并明确区分关联证据与因果机制，以推动从描述性关联向精准临床转化的跨越。\",\"chapter_thesis\":\"肠道微生物组调节实体瘤免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的证据虽已积累，但受限于测序技术异质性、观察性研究的混杂偏倚、动物模型向人类转化的局限，以及缺乏大型III期随机对照试验验证，目前仍无法确立普适性生物标志物或常规干预方案。未来研究需转向功能导向的多组学整合、严格的前瞻性队列设计、标准化供体/制剂管理，并明确区分关联证据与因果机制，以推动从描述性关联向精准临床转化的跨越。\",\"chapter_argument\":\"肠道微生物组调节实体瘤免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的证据虽已积累，但受限于测序技术异质性、观察性研究的混杂偏倚、动物模型向人类转化的局限，以及缺乏大型III期随机对照试验验证，目前仍无法确立普适性生物标志物或常规干预方案。未来研究需转向功能导向的多组学整合、严格的前瞻性队列设计、标准化供体/制剂管理，并明确区分关联证据与因果机制，以推动从描述性关联向精准临床转化的跨越。\",\"reader_objective\":\"帮助读者识别当前领域内关键的方法学瓶颈与证据等级差异，理解为何单一菌种难以成为通用预测因子，并为后续临床转化研究提供可操作的设计原则、优先级排序及边界认知。\",\"research_question\":\"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\",\"review_argument\":\"肠道微生物组通过分类学特征、代谢产物及免疫通路调节实体瘤患者对 ICI 的临床疗效，但证据强度因肿瘤类型、研究设计及干预策略而异。观察性关联证据在黑色素瘤中最强，NSCLC 和 RCC 次之，但关联不等于因果。机制证据主要来自动物模型，人类验证有限，特别是肿瘤微环境内代谢物浓度数据缺失（如肌苷仅有血浆数据）。干预策略在初治人群中显示希望（FMT-LUMINate ORR 75-80%），但在难治人群中效果有限（MITRIC ORR 0%），且安全性受 ICI 方案调节（Prevotella 相关心肌炎仅在双 ICI 背景下出现）。目前缺乏 Phase III RCT 证据支持微生物干预的常规临床应用，未来研究需解决标准化、因果推断及人群分层问题。\",\"shared_scope\":{\"statement\":\"本综述聚焦于实体瘤（黑色素瘤、非小细胞肺癌、肾细胞癌、结直肠癌等）患者接受免疫检查点抑制剂（PD-1/PD-L1、CTLA-4 抑制剂）治疗期间，肠道微生物组对治疗疗效（ORR、PFS、OS）及毒性（irAEs）的调节作用。涵盖观察性关联证据（区分回顾性与前瞻性队列）、因果机制解析（免疫细胞、分子通路、代谢物）、外部干扰因素（抗生素、PPI、饮食）及微生物干预策略（FMT、益生菌、工程菌）的临床试验数据。明确排除血液系统恶性肿瘤及非免疫治疗背景下的微生物组研究（除非用于机制对比）。严格区分肠道微生物组与肿瘤内微生物组的作用边界。证据等级标注明确：观察性关联不推断因果，干预试验区分 I/II 期与 III 期，代谢物数据区分血浆与肿瘤组织浓度。\"},\"review_argument_status\":\"calibrated\",\"review_argument_source\":\"whole_plan_improvement\"}},\"unit_contexts\":{\"Ch7\":{\"Ch7_U01\":{\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U01\",\"focus\":\"测序平台、生信流程及样本处理的技术变异是导致跨队列生物标志物难以复现的核心原因，低生物量样本污染与分辨率不足进一步削弱了分类学结论的可靠性。\",\"owner_unit_context\":{\"evidence_conditions\":\"\",\"synthesis\":\"技术噪音不仅放大了队列间的表观差异，也掩盖了真实的生物学信号。标准化重分析表明，当控制测序深度、去噪算法与参考数据库时，部分微生物特征展现出跨队列的稳健性，这提示未来的生物标志物开发必须优先建立统一的元数据采集协议与开源生信工作流，而非依赖单一中心的探索性发现。\",\"transition\":\"技术标准化的推进仅是第一步，即便获得高质量数据，观察性研究中普遍存在的混杂偏倚与因果倒置风险仍会阻碍机制的确证。\",\"supporting_studies\":[{\"contribution\":\"提供免疫监测中微生物样本采集与测序流程标准化的专家共识建议，直接回应技术变异导致跨队列结论不可复现的方法学挑战。\",\"paper_id\":\"705d021ac660029794f037498bc1ffea03cbe239\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\"},{\"contribution\":\"以口腔局部微环境为例，展示低生物量样本检测中的污染控制难题及宿主蛋白互作对菌群信号的干扰，补充空间异质性带来的分析局限。\",\"paper_id\":\"83ee66187aff0ae19e2706481c06aa696e21465b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\"},{\"contribution\":\"通过黏膜黑色素瘤多部位同步采样设计，说明区分全身肠道与局部肿瘤微生物信号的方法学必要性，为标准化空间组学整合提供范例。\",\"paper_id\":\"bf7682bc64d82a0342f438a261f4ce8de81ed9c0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\"},{\"contribution\":\"提供定性综述证据，说明领域正从物种鉴定转向功能机制与生态韧性理论，支撑方法学标准化对揭示真实微生物信号的必要性。\",\"paper_id\":\"ee8eab6a2dc467e53087607197bbc6701429b8ae\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\"},{\"contribution\":\"通过黑色素瘤系统综述展示测序平台与生信管道差异导致的菌种列表不一致性，为剖析技术变异削弱结论可靠性提供具体案例。\",\"paper_id\":\"f9a9ef8d406ee51983cd285f9e60fc41574ae937\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\"},{\"contribution\":\"对比肠道与口腔微生物组预测效力的差异，补充空间异质性带来的分析局限，支持多部位采样与标准化流程的必要性。\",\"paper_id\":\"f9ac47c0add070f4c39ec8ed763518f941ddf164\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\"}]},\"unit_notes\":\"\"},\"Ch7_U02\":{\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U02\",\"focus\":\"现有证据高度依赖观察性关联，抗生素使用、饮食结构、宿主遗传及肿瘤类型等混杂因素严重干扰因果链条的构建，且孟德尔随机化等方法在工具变量强度与人群代表性上存在固有缺陷。\",\"owner_unit_context\":{\"evidence_conditions\":\"\",\"synthesis\":\"混杂偏倚与模型外推的不确定性要求未来研究必须采用严格的纵向设计、详细记录共用药史与饮食基线，并在人类队列中验证动物模型提出的机制假说。统计推断工具（如MR）可作为生成假设的辅助手段，但不能替代前瞻性干预试验提供的因果确证。\",\"transition\":\"即便明确了因果路径，若缺乏大规模随机对照试验的支持与特定人群的表征数据，这些机制仍难以转化为可常规执行的临床指南。\",\"supporting_studies\":[{\"contribution\":\"揭示青少年与老年患者基线菌群结构的显著差异，论证年龄发育阶段作为关键混杂变量如何干扰因果链条构建，支持分龄分层分析的必要性。\",\"paper_id\":\"035c34646887b9612a3901c1b65bb5659e6881bb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\"},{\"contribution\":\"借助慢性病毒感染模型展示治疗干预后代谢通路的持续性异常，类比说明宿主病理状态可能掩盖或模拟微生物介导的真实效应。\",\"paper_id\":\"0ccad85a9f6c41d50296628847b3ffd3596af8ee\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\"},{\"contribution\":\"提出“抗性/易感”微生物群概念框架，指出饮食模式与合并用药的交互作用会重塑菌群功能，警示观察性关联中未控暴露的混杂风险。\",\"paper_id\":\"a23415cfd3d02f562c74b0a4d6569499690c5ecb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\"},{\"contribution\":\"提供波兰队列实证，揭示特定菌属（如P. copri）与疗效关联的人群依赖性，论证年龄、饮食等混杂变量干扰因果链条构建的风险。\",\"paper_id\":\"f31246cd559d1a06b99a32b0ee47bb1ce0265772\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\"},{\"contribution\":\"提供ICI给药时间与生存结局的观察性数据，作为非微生物因素（时间生物学）干扰疗效的对照证据，警示混杂控制的复杂性。\",\"paper_id\":\"f7345b03e8a5419417513da6cf1833522f3be7ed\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\"},{\"contribution\":\"提出“分子模拟”假说及量化方法（TAS），解释观察性关联背后的潜在因果机制，同时指出其验证局限性与HLA LOH等负面调节因素。\",\"paper_id\":\"f845fe79c73bf04f15c7ab75115b887691b09e53\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\"}]},\"unit_notes\":\"\"},\"Ch7_U03\":{\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U03\",\"focus\":\"微生物干预策略的临床证据主要停留在 I/II 期概念验证阶段，缺乏大型 III 期 RCT 支持；特定人群（如老年、儿科、不同种族）数据匮乏，且肿瘤微环境（TME）内关键代谢物的浓度数据缺失，限制了干预方案的精准落地。\",\"owner_unit_context\":{\"evidence_conditions\":\"\",\"synthesis\":\"证据等级的断层与人群异质性表明，微生物疗法不能简单套用“一刀切”模式。TME代谢物浓度的缺失进一步切断了全身循环标志物与局部效应的桥梁。未来必须建立基于基线生态特征、疾病分期与宿主年龄的动态监测体系，并通过多中心协作解决样本量与长期随访的瓶颈。\",\"transition\":\"面对上述缺口，单一的分类学追踪或经验性补充已无法满足精准医疗需求，研究范式亟需向多组学整合与工程化精准干预转型。\",\"supporting_studies\":[{\"contribution\":\"作为肝癌辅助治疗试验方案，明确短程免疫给药窗口与动态监测节点的设计逻辑，反衬当前缺乏大型RCT验证及标准化临床路径的现状。\",\"paper_id\":\"0e52b2409fa157d1812995e5c089e1e03b4bad34\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\"},{\"contribution\":\"展示基于回顾性数据的计算模拟预测结果，强调从算法优化到菌株分离培养的临床转化断层，凸显早期概念验证向III期确证试验跨越的障碍。\",\"paper_id\":\"8c58a2c58d069dea4a7b1ef304fff55a4640d079\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\"},{\"contribution\":\"系统梳理结直肠癌FMT与益生菌早期临床试验数据，指出供体筛选困难、定植效率波动及安全性监管缺口，支撑干预策略尚未成为标准护理的判断。\",\"paper_id\":\"c0d5128fb69f9f60402c1c706b6276fd527e51fd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\"},{\"contribution\":\"汇总FMT与活体细菌产品的概念验证结果，明确指出缺乏大型RCT支持常规临床应用，支撑早期试验信号与III期验证缺席的判断。\",\"paper_id\":\"ee8eab6a2dc467e53087607197bbc6701429b8ae\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\"},{\"contribution\":\"评估不同干预策略（饮食、FMT、LBPs）的临床成熟度与技术挑战，反衬当前缺乏标准化临床路径及预测因子的现状。\",\"paper_id\":\"f2eed100d2b1243d762c69b5b04f8a2a7e2cc82c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\"},{\"contribution\":\"梳理早期临床试验（I/II期）数据，强调供体筛选困难、定植效率波动及安全性监管缺口，支撑干预策略尚未成为标准护理的判断。\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:290154100\",\"source_handle\":\"P0584\"}]},\"unit_notes\":\"\"},\"Ch7_U04\":{\"unit_id\":\"Ch7_U04\",\"focus\":\"未来研究需转向功能导向（代谢通路、基因水平）而非单纯分类学分析，整合 AI、多组学（宏基因组 + 代谢组）及先进模型（类器官、芯片）以解析复杂互作；个性化干预策略需结合宿主基线特征及标准化方案，并建立严格的安全监管框架。\",\"owner_unit_context\":{\"evidence_conditions\":\"\",\"synthesis\":\"多组学整合与人工智能并非万能解药，其效能高度依赖于底层数据的标准化质量与生物学先验知识的注入。类器官与芯片技术为机制验证提供了更接近人体的平台，但仍需克服免疫重建与长期培养的瓶颈。个性化干预的成功将取决于能否建立涵盖供体筛选、制剂冻干工艺、给药时序及宿主基线分层的闭环监管体系。\",\"transition\":\"综上所述，方法学的严谨性、因果推断的透明度与临床转化的阶梯式验证，共同构成了该领域迈向成熟的核心支柱。\",\"supporting_studies\":[{\"contribution\":\"综述AI整合多组学预测ICI疗效的潜力与泛化挑战，为未来利用机器学习解析非线性微生物-免疫互作及开发可解释性数字孪生模型提供技术背景。\",\"paper_id\":\"164f89ae032b4a17e939d4531f3f7f8ddb4c81ee\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\"},{\"contribution\":\"评估类器官在模拟微生物-TME轴中的优势与免疫组分缺失局限，论证结合微流控芯片实现动态梯度与空间异质性捕获的方法学演进方向。\",\"paper_id\":\"4a8bc3da652bbd783e7ea5c1dbde908e5124c442\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\"},{\"contribution\":\"列举工程菌递送微型抗体及AI辅助靶点发现的临床前案例，提示需建立严格的供体筛查、制剂工艺优化与长期安全性监测框架以推动精准干预落地。\",\"paper_id\":\"ed9f49b6f8cea1ce51cbf797f10d7a01e6835e15\",\"source_handle\":\"P0532\"},{\"contribution\":\"引入昼夜节律新维度及方法学局限性，支持未来标准化研究需求，强调时间生物学对微生物定植及ICI疗效的影响。\",\"paper_id\":\"f2eed100d2b1243d762c69b5b04f8a2a7e2cc82c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\"},{\"contribution\":\"批判性分析从临床前到临床转化的障碍，指出个体异质性、技术标准化缺失和还原论局限性，为精准干预的标准化路径提供背景。\",\"paper_id\":\"f661d588e0fee18c37ed1d46fd697c2ad01c4394\",\"source_handle\":\"P0555\"},{\"contribution\":\"介绍TOPOSCORE等多组学评分模型及ONCOBIOME倡议，展示超越分类学的功能导向分析方法及国际协作标准化努力的前景。\",\"paper_id\":\"ff5504ec23a09bb1d577854219dadfe3c7772ece\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\"}]},\"unit_notes\":\"\"}}},\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"atom_id\":\"atom::425a2b2a483b2ca665dd57dc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"abstract\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bb314b16e69d1963247396c5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::833afba9b6b749222c5ed1c3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用文献计量学（Bibliometrics）分析方法。具体步骤包括：1. 数据检索：从Web of Science Core Collection检索2001-2025年间的相关文献；2. 筛选：严格筛选后纳入2,669篇出版物；3. 工具与分析参数：使用CiteSpace软件，设置时间切片为1年，每切片Top N=50，采用Pathfinder剪枝算法；4. 分析维度：涵盖时间发表趋势、合作网络（国家/机构/作者）、关键词共现、聚类分析及突现词检测（Burst Detection）。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::86c93f51292f6ba5a9010b79\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了癌症免疫治疗与肠道微生物群交叉领域的宏观知识图谱，明确了“微生物-免疫-肿瘤”三角框架的结构特征。\",\"limits\":\"作为文献计量学研究，仅反映文献出版层面的统计规律（如引用、合作、关键词频率），未深入探讨具体的生物学机制或临床疗效数据。所给摘要未交代具体的机制细节，仅提及背景中已知的代谢物分泌、免疫细胞调节等一般性机制。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3d03746407449a9359784d05\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"2001-2025年 WoSCC 数据库\",\"finding\":\"研究领域呈现“萌芽-发展-爆发”三阶段增长模式，2024年达到峰值（525篇文章）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5746eced4aab3f5fdc705ace\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"国家合作网络\",\"finding\":\"中国（988篇）和美国（762篇）是高产国家；英国具有最高中心性（0.30），是全球合作枢纽。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::439778384de1bdfa2c53ffa9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"机构合作网络\",\"finding\":\"德克萨斯大学系统（149篇）、INSERM（124篇）和MD Anderson癌症中心（123篇）是高产机构；加州大学系统具有最高中心性（0.19）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::784fd12a57becc8b7c60b978\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"作者影响力\",\"finding\":\"发文量前三的作者为Zitvogel, Laurence (50篇), Routy, Bertrand (47篇), Wargo, Jennifer A (39篇)；高中心性作者包括Kroemer, Guido等。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::18aa2b0d688dff26fa4ab1eb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"关键词分析\",\"finding\":\"高频关键词为gut microbiota, immunotherapy, colorectal cancer；高中心性关键词为immunotherapy, t cells, gut microbiota；新兴突现关键词为microsatellite instability, health, diversity。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c03581ddab9a9bef368e0a62\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"聚类分析\",\"finding\":\"揭示五大主要研究方向：免疫检查点抑制剂、乳腺癌、结直肠癌、疗效、肿瘤微环境。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9ea95ca7a2703d43706ee0d4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7bdf128c5cc511124c9dd6d3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"随着癌症免疫治疗中肠道微生物群相关研究的迅速增加，传统定性综述方法难以系统性地分析该领域的知识结构、热点演变趋势及跨学科动态。本研究旨在解决如何从宏观层面梳理这一快速增长领域的知识图谱，识别关键研究者、机构及新兴研究方向的问题。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ab714a828f5ecb6932ddac7c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"该研究聚焦于癌症免疫治疗领域，具体考察肠道微生物群（gut microbiota）与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）疗效之间的关系。研究对象为2001年1月1日至2025年7月7日期间在Web of Science核心合集（WoSCC）中发表的文献，涵盖国家、机构、作者及关键词等 bibliometric 指标。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b96b88671b0277df944c9f5a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"这是一篇基于文献计量学的综述论文，旨在绘制癌症免疫治疗中肠道微生物群研究的“知识景观”。鉴于该领域文献爆炸式增长且传统综述难以系统分析其知识结构，作者利用CiteSpace软件对筛选出的2,669篇文献进行定量分析。研究通过时间切片、合作网络、关键词共现、聚类及突现检测等方法，揭示了该领域的增长模式、主要贡献者、国际合作格局以及新兴热点，最终构建了一个“微生物-免疫-肿瘤”三角知识框架，并为未来个性化免疫治疗策略的临床转化提供了宏观视角。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a0da938e437186cd694c1a1c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文为综述提供了关于“肠道微生物群-免疫检查点抑制剂”领域宏观结构、研究热点演变及主要贡献者的全景式背景素材。它不直接回答具体的分子机制，但能帮助用户定位该领域的知识边界、核心议题（如结直肠癌、MSI状态）及关键学术共同体，适用于综述的引言背景、领域现状描述及未来方向展望部分。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f91958cbdab94422e5faf534\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"仅提供文献分布统计，不直接提供微生物调节ICI疗效的具体临床效果大小或异质性数据。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了该领域研究规模的宏观证据，确认了肠道微生物群与ICI疗效关联已成为一个独立且快速扩张的研究子领域。指出了结直肠癌（colorectal cancer）和免疫检查点抑制剂（immune checkpoint inhibitor）是该领域最核心的关键词集群，暗示了在这些特定癌种中微生物调节ICI疗效的研究最为集中。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f078ddb1ffd8be970ab761ca\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"关键词突现代表关注度上升，不代表机制已被完全阐明。摘要未提供具体的分子通路细节，需结合其他实证研究论文来填充具体的机制链条。\",\"contribution\":\"通过关键词突现分析（burst detection），识别出“microsatellite instability (MSI)”、“diversity”和“t cells”作为新兴热点。这表明当前机制研究的前沿可能集中在MSI状态下的微生物特征、微生物多样性对T细胞浸润的影响等方面。同时，聚类结果指向“tumor microenvironment”（肿瘤微环境）为主要研究方向之一。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::38c34e6fb892b9f774fcac73\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"摘要指出传统综述难以分析知识结构，本研究构建了“微生物-免疫-肿瘤”三角框架。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::61c8cb832c511cc207f211f4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"列出了Zitvogel, Routy, Kroemer等关键作者及MD Anderson、INSERM等机构。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::87492d1c99b1b7dc8e17db25\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"结论提到需要整合跨尺度机制探索和标准化临床转化路径。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9999f33c5d2cb360fe617601\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该论文为文献计量学综述，其“发现”是基于文献计数的统计结果（如关键词频率、引用中心性），而非生物学实验的直接观察。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4e780b89aa8335294feadf2e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"摘要中提到的“Ruminococcus”, “Bifidobacterium”, “L-selenomethionine”仅为背景介绍中已确认的作用，非本论文的新发现，引用时需区分这是领域共识还是本文贡献。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bc2fb4c5dd29b080e055091c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"关键词“colorectal cancer”的高频出现提示该癌种研究较多，但不能推断所有实体瘤的微生物机制相同，需注意不同癌种的异质性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c5579360f2d8d045eeef1617\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"摘要未提供具体的机制细节，若需了解具体分子通路，必须查阅被引用的原始实证研究论文。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e0c96c710ac880e15fe6ed77\",\"source_handle\":\"P0001\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"identity\",\"reason\":\"source identity was not independently verified\",\"status\":\"input_attributed\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\"status\":\"partial\"}],\"material_scope\":\"abstract_plus_snippets\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s213\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5f9724705076028708ce84e3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::03a3d96e2e275c4aa63e60a3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::de758f4203639975b7669e42\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用双轨并行的文献计量与综述综合路线： 1. 宏观知识图谱构建：检索Web of Science Core Collection中关于“intratumoral microbiota”的文献（截至2025年12月22日），经筛选保留1,278篇，使用VOSviewer、CiteSpace和SCImago Graphica进行年度发文量、国家/机构/作者合作网络、关键词共现、聚类及突现词分析，以揭示领域结构和演进路径。 2. 微观干预证据汇总：检索PubMed中与肿瘤内微生物干预抗肿瘤疗效相关的临床研究及临床前试验，依据PICO原则筛选出69项符合条件的研究（包括动物实验、纳米研究、工程菌、RCT等），按肿瘤部位、干预类型、微生物种类及治疗效果（正向/负向）进行分类统计和分析。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fece5bde50262cd3e15e1fb2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了肿瘤内微生物研究领域的系统性全景图，明确了从基础关联到机制探索再到临床转化的演进脉络；梳理了针对肿瘤内微生物的干预策略分类及其在联合治疗中的潜在角色；指出了低生物量样本检测中的污染控制这一关键方法论瓶颈。\",\"limits\":\"作为文献计量学综述，其结论依赖于数据库收录情况和检索策略，可能遗漏非索引或非英文文献； bibliometric指标无法直接反映单篇研究的临床质量或生物学因果机制；对69项干预研究的分析仅为描述性统计，未进行严格的偏倚风险评估或Meta分析；所引用的具体机制细节多来自转述其他研究，本文本身未提供新的原始实验数据。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a7f610275b94d2b8a9478d8b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"基于Web of Science数据库的1,278篇文献\",\"finding\":\"自2012年起发文量总体上升，2020年后显著加速；中国和是美国两大中心；关键词聚类显示“肿瘤免疫治疗”和“免疫微环境”是两大重要分支；具核梭杆菌、肠道微生物群、结直肠癌是高频主题。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c492adc39c3afa4cb3e70e15\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"基于PubMed筛选的69项干预研究\",\"finding\":\"绝大多数研究（约48/69）报告肿瘤内细菌对治疗产生负面影响（促进耐药或免疫抑制），其中25项涉及具核梭杆菌；部分研究（如乳酸杆菌、阿克曼氏菌）显示对免疫检查点抑制剂有增效作用；目前仅有极少数进入临床试验阶段，大部分仍处于动物模型或体外实验阶段。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::702bc85a1fd9ffa011d3b5e8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1bf891b80e20e0c25010df22\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"肿瘤内微生物研究领域的发展现状如何？其核心研究热点、合作网络及演进轨迹是什么？目前针对肿瘤内微生物的干预策略（特别是与免疫治疗的结合）处于何种阶段，存在哪些主要挑战和未来方向？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::460278473abde33efdffefc3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"肿瘤微环境（TME）内的微生物群（intratumoral microbiota, ITM），涵盖其分布、与宿主免疫的相互作用、检测技术进展及在抗肿瘤治疗（特别是免疫治疗）中的干预潜力。数据来源为Web of Science和PubMed收录的文献，时间跨度至2025年12月。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8f3db771375cd6d6d127492c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本研究是一篇基于文献计量学和可视化分析的综述论文，旨在系统描绘肿瘤内微生物研究领域的知识结构、热点演变及未来趋势。作者利用VOSviewer、CiteSpace等工具对1,278篇WoS核心合集文献进行宏观图谱分析，识别出“肿瘤免疫治疗”和“免疫微环境”为核心聚类；同时整合PubMed数据，筛选出69项针对肿瘤内微生物干预的临床前及临床试验，重点分析了以具核梭杆菌（Fusobacterium nucleatum）为代表的目标菌种在不同癌症类型和治疗模式下的作用效果。研究发现该领域自2020年起进入快速发展期，中国和美国为主要贡献国，当前研究正从单纯的菌群特征描述向机制解析和临床转化过渡，但多数干预手段仍停留在临床前阶段，且面临低生物量带来的污染控制挑战。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::229e9bbd5115c33ed640fc05\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文为综述规划提供了关于“肠道微生物群-肿瘤轴”及“肿瘤内微生物对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效影响”的宏观背景、研究热点分布及现有干预证据的结构化概览。它特别指出了肠道微生物群在肿瘤定植方面的新兴热点，以及具核梭杆菌等特定菌种在调节ICI疗效中的双重作用（促进或抑制）。虽然缺乏具体的分子机制深度数据，但其对干预策略的分类（如纳米递送、工程菌、益生菌）和对临床转化阶段的评估，有助于定位当前证据的成熟度。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1e05373668d60d7a6a1080d4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"仅提供了相关性描述和干预结果的汇总，未深入解释具体的分子或细胞机制；对于“如何调节”的回答仅限于表型结果（如T细胞浸润增加），缺乏通路层面的细节。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物群与肿瘤内微生物群重叠性的宏观观察，指出乳酸杆菌、双歧杆菌等常见肠道菌也在肿瘤中被检测到；总结了69项干预研究中，不同微生物（包括肠道来源菌）对ICI疗效的影响方向（正向增强或负向抑制），例如Lactobacillus reuteri和Akkermansia muciniphila被报道可增强CD8+ T细胞浸润和ICI疗效。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bab75b8f60178d665554ac6e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这些机制描述是基于对其他研究的转述和综述，并非本文的新发现；具体信号通路细节（如miRNA3655/SURF6/IRF7/IFNβ轴）虽被提及，但未在本综述中展开验证；需结合其他提供具体机制实验数据的论文来充实这部分内容。\",\"contribution\":\"讨论了微生物代谢物（如短链脂肪酸丁酸、乳酸）作为连接微生物与宿主免疫的关键中介因素；提到丁酸可增强TCR信号传导，而厌氧菌产生的乳酸可导致微环境酸化并抑制iNKT细胞功能；强调了多组学整合在揭示微生物-代谢-免疫互作中的重要性。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::89530421d7aa3c2d7928ff02\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"肿瘤内微生物研究自2020年后的快速上升趋势，以及从关联研究向机制和临床转化转变的总体轨迹。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::68e912c643063ef20f33cd1e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"低生物量样本中污染控制的极端重要性，以及不同研究中心间检测标准不统一的问题。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b1e658d834a9151da99aad64\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"针对肿瘤内微生物的多种干预手段，包括特异性清除（纳米药物、疫苗）、重塑微生态（益生菌、工程菌）及联合治疗。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ac74c74d6e2438f8ebc2a108\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该论文是文献计量学和综述性质的文章，其提供的“发现”多为对已有研究的统计归纳和趋势判断，而非新的原始实验证据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a28df6909bfda1c329c39738\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"关于肠道微生物群在肿瘤中定植的结论，主要基于对现有文献中共同检出菌群的观察，尚未建立完整的因果链条或定植机制的确证，需谨慎解读其普遍性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c6008a7b86950a2db51f2876\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"干预研究的效果总结（如“大多数为负面”）是基于纳入的69项研究的简单计数，未考虑研究设计的异质性、肿瘤亚型差异及统计学效力，不能直接推断所有肿瘤内微生物均有害。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::67b5405704b6ad7537c29821\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的具体机制（如丁酸、乳酸的作用）是作者对他人研究的综合转述，引用时需追溯原始实验研究以获取确切的分子细节。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::516384e0bad277cc6e673d50\",\"source_handle\":\"P0027\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-4dcc7c19ae5301df5638\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-966f01de18a592374440\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-8a0e6e25273d717fa14c\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-74e1075e2b497ab9b22a\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-cba144da26e8f18f1eb8\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-c230d024caf9f7ff8d85\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-4003f472cc949089d526\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-6354a360c17fcb1654b2\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-d2b97217c6260ef55897\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"kind\":\"assets\",\"reason\":\"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\"status\":\"missing\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s284\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ad1e8154b0a6960ead59310c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e51d116e16ccbea9748af8d6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1a73c41b6335085faab23b1f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用二次定性综述设计。检索策略包括对PubMed、Europe PMC、Crossref和Google Scholar的结构化搜索，以及对相关文献的向后引文追踪。纳入标准为2017年至2026年4月发表的人类原发性研究，要求提供肠道微生物组组成或微生物组调节暴露与实体瘤ICI临床结局之间的连接。排除综述、动物研究和纯机制实验室论文（但用于背景框架）。最终选取15项具有代表性的主要临床研究，通过解释性主题程序（interpretive thematic procedure）对研究进行编码，按调节类型分类并 juxtapose（并列比较）重复出现的解释模式。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bb1f3d9c218571d23c4ecf84\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提出了从“分类学焦点”向“功能焦点”和“生态系统模型”的范式转变观点，强调微生物多样性、代谢物相互作用和黏膜屏障活性作为系统性免疫控制层的作用。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代具体的统计检验方法或严格的纳入排除评分标准细节；证据基础偏向黑色素瘤，其他实体瘤的干预数据较少；现有研究样本量小、测序平台不统一、缺乏对饮食和地理因素的充分控制，导致无法支持简单的通用处方。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::83414a3e3fae35233ee887ad\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"基线微生物特征与响应表型\",\"finding\":\"响应者表型反复与较高的微生物多样性及特定菌属富集相关，包括Akkermansia、Ruminococcaceae、Faecalibacterium和Bifidobacterium。这种关联在不同肿瘤队列中表现出生态学模式的一致性，但具体物种因人群和测序平台而异。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9e4dd5f47fda6a2395ed9679\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"生态干扰与偶然调节（抗生素与益生菌）\",\"finding\":\"在启动ICI期间无控制的抗生素暴露与较差的预后相关（尤其在上皮肿瘤和非小细胞肺癌中），提示生态脆弱性。益生菌补充的效果数据难以解释，可能受混杂因素影响，且高剂量益生菌有时与多样性降低相关，表明简单的细菌添加不如维持生态完整性重要。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ab04ce96345a2cf76ab4ebf0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"治疗性微生物组工程化\",\"finding\":\"粪便微生物群移植（FMT）、高纤维饮食和活体细菌产品展示了概念验证（proof of concept），证明可以通过治疗性操纵使微生物群落对ICI疗法更具反应性。例如，FMT在抗PD-1难治性黑色素瘤患者中诱导了新的临床反应，CBM588联合疗法在肾癌中显示积极信号。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::141b36432711d0058eb9029b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::badff7011b3a302ca2c5e042\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"传统生物标志物（如PD-L1、TMB）无法充分解释ICI疗效的异质性；需要理解肠道微生物组是否不仅是相关性指标，而是可被重塑以影响免疫状态和治疗的宿主决定因素，以及目前的证据基础在方法学上存在哪些优势与局限。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c044873b9ecec12e1c285594\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"人类实体肿瘤患者，聚焦肠道微生物组（Gut Microbiome）与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效及毒性的关联。涵盖黑色素瘤、非小细胞肺癌、肾细胞癌、肝细胞癌等实体瘤类型。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b13ae81092a39b50e2e4a02d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇二次定性综述（Secondary Qualitative Review），旨在综合临床证据，探讨肠道微生物组如何作为宿主决定因素影响实体瘤患者的免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）反应、生存期及毒性。研究通过结构化搜索PubMed、Europe PMC等数据库并结合引文追踪，筛选出15项主要临床研究进行主题合成。文章未进行定量荟萃分析，而是从响应表型、生态干扰（如抗生素/益生菌暴露）和治疗性工程化（如FMT、饮食干预）三个主题出发，评估微生物组调节的机制合理性与临床可行性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0793c841b7f3ce068049ed3f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为理解肠道微生物组如何作为宿主生态因子调节ICI疗效提供了理论框架和临床证据的综合视图。其核心价值在于将分散的临床观察整合为三个主题：基线生态签名、生态干扰风险和治疗性工程潜力。它不直接提供单一因果机制的实验数据，而是通过主题合成揭示了当前证据的方法学局限性和生物学合理性，有助于界定综述中关于“微生物组作为疗效预测因子”和“微生物组干预策略”的讨论边界。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8161bac800ee67bffb51c02a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"仅基于15项研究的定性合成，非定量荟萃分析；具体菌种的普适性受限，不能直接外推至所有实体瘤亚型；未提供具体的效应量数值。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了关于肠道微生物组特征与ICI疗效关联的主题综合。指出响应者通常具有高多样性和特定有益菌（Akkermansia, Faecalibacterium等）富集，而抗生素暴露与较差预后相关。同时强调了不同肿瘤类型间具体菌种的不一致性，提示需关注生态整体而非单一标记物。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b889a447834235936ab7bdb8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制部分主要基于作者引用的理论框架和对现有研究的解读，而非本篇提供的原始实验数据；具体分子通路细节未在文中展开，需结合其他机制研究；干预试验的因果效力尚未在大样本随机对照试验中得到确证。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了微生物组调节疗效的理论机制框架，包括癌症免疫循环、生态韧性理论和精准宿主调节。解释了为何多样性比单一菌种更重要（生态韧性），以及微生物如何通过抗原呈递、T细胞 priming 和短链脂肪酸生成影响免疫状态。同时指出了当前干预试验（FMT、活体产品）处于早期阶段，机制尚不完全明确。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a270ba0cc300126faed82feb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文章提出的从“分类学”到“功能/生态系统”的范式转变，以及癌症免疫循环、生态韧性理论在解释ICI异质性中的应用。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::73fee9aabd3f6493470c882a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文章指出的当前证据的方法学缺陷：小样本、测序平台不均、饮食/抗生素/地理因素控制不足、选择性偏倚（如抗生素使用的指征混杂）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3f4ef01c5233246635897e13\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"对FMT、高纤维饮食、活体细菌产品（CBM588）和益生菌等不同干预方式的疗效信号和局限性的总结。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::06aa3e99f643d69c9215b8cc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述是定性主题合成，非定量荟萃分析，因此不提供合并效应量或统计显著性检验结果。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f3d959faf05885a11d0dcb2d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"具体有益菌属（如Akkermansia）的关联在不同肿瘤队列和测序平台间存在不一致性，不能视为普适性生物标志物。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a45022f7c9091753bc1dab0b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"抗生素与不良预后的关联可能受到疾病严重程度等混杂因素的影响，需谨慎解读因果关系。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::21ced29101158164b19fe567\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"FMT和活体产品的积极结果来自早期、小规模、非随机或单臂试验，尚不足以确立为标准治疗。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::673c47c128f2dda5097ee8b1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"所给材料未提供详细的统计学分析方法或严格的文献质量评分工具细节。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c166496624c9d9db7f16ef6b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0534\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s262\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6af0ba669d074ea8ba1e2040\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ba9e31855dab38ca50ac025c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d3346c6e9544214a13e3fbb7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用文献综述法。作者检索并综合了关于宿主-微生物互作的基础研究、利用无菌/悉生小鼠进行的机制探索、以及人类临床队列中微生物组特征与治疗反应关联的研究。文章按逻辑模块组织材料：1) 方法论基础；2) 因果证据（从动物到人类）；3) 潜在机制分类（信使类型与免疫效应）；4) 临床应用潜力。未进行新的原始数据收集或系统性Meta分析统计，而是对现有分散证据进行定性归纳和理论框架构建。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::88ecd8fa60772b6b885bc028\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物组影响癌症免疫治疗疗效的综合性机制框架，将分散的实验证据归类为‘信使’（活菌、代谢物、分子模式、细胞因子）和‘效应’（抗原性、佐剂性、旁观者激活）两大维度。\",\"limits\":\"作为综述，其结论依赖于所引用的原始研究的质量和设计；对于具体菌株在不同人群中的普适性、非细菌组分（真菌、病毒）的作用以及长期安全性等问题的解答仍不充分，属于待研究领域。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4374e070f05d81910f56d2a0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"基于无菌小鼠模型及人类临床观察\",\"finding\":\"特定肠道细菌（如双歧杆菌、阿克曼氏菌、拟杆菌属某些种）的存在与对ICB（抗PD-1/CTLA-4）的良好治疗反应正相关，而其他菌群则与耐药或毒性相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fedf14dfcbb0e473c9635b14\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"机制层面\",\"finding\":\"微生物可通过多种途径调节免疫：1) 交叉反应性T细胞识别细菌与肿瘤共同抗原；2) MAMPs/PAMPs作为佐剂激活树突状细胞（DCs）；3) 微生物代谢物（如SCFAs）调节免疫细胞功能；4) 诱导局部细胞因子（如IL-12, IL-22）产生系统性影响。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6d16ee714b2e06d982b7651b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"临床转化角度\",\"finding\":\"抗生素使用可能损害ICB疗效；粪便微生物移植（FMT）和特定益生菌/代谢物补充具有改善预后的潜力，但尚处于早期临床试验阶段，且存在个体差异和安全性不确定性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ad537fe95ee18635c692eb16\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0a525502ff5e378e81a97a66\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"旨在回答：肠道微生物群在癌症免疫治疗中扮演什么角色？其影响疗效的具体机制是什么？目前有哪些方法可以利用这一知识优化治疗效果？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::48b76de668c575df11e5da7e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"肠道微生物群（gut microbiome）与癌症免疫治疗（特别是免疫检查点抑制剂 ICB，如抗PD-1/PD-L1和抗CTLA-4）疗效之间的关联。涵盖从基础微生物学、无菌小鼠模型机制研究到临床相关性证据的综合回顾。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b01bc4859983a1d7d81ea157\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇综述，系统梳理了肠道微生物群如何影响癌症免疫治疗的疗效。文章首先介绍了宿主-微生物相互作用的基础研究方法（如16S rRNA测序、宏基因组测序及无菌/悉生小鼠模型的使用及其局限性），随后总结了证明肠道菌群组成与免疫治疗疗效存在因果联系的关键实验证据（包括动物模型中的定植实验和人类队列的相关性研究）。接着，文章详细探讨了可能的生物学机制，包括活细菌或微生物相关分子模式（MAMPs/PAMPs）作为信使通过增强抗原性、佐剂效应或旁观者激活来调节抗肿瘤免疫，以及微生物代谢物（如短链脂肪酸）和宿主细胞因子作为信使的作用。最后，文章讨论了将微生物组作为预后生物标志物、谨慎使用抗生素以及开发基于微生物组的干预策略（如FMT、益生菌、噬菌体疗法）的临床前景，并指出了当前研究的局限性和未来方向。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ff1f020048be065446fd0396\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为理解肠道微生物群如何调节实体瘤免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）疗效提供了全面的背景知识和机制分类。它不直接提供单一确凿的因果链条，而是整理了多个独立研究发现的共性模式和潜在通路，特别有助于解释‘为什么不同患者对同一ICIs药物反应不同’以及‘微生物可能通过哪些具体生物化学或免疫学路径介入’。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b0c5a8d7c38eaaab6e57cf00\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"仅展示相关性或初步因果推断，未确立通用的‘最佳菌群’配方；不同研究间的具体菌种列表不完全重合，需谨慎引用具体物种。\",\"contribution\":\"列举了与ICBs疗效正负相关的特定细菌类群（如双歧杆菌、阿克曼氏菌与响应正相关；某些拟杆菌与耐药或结肠炎相关），并指出这种关联在不同研究中存在不一致性，提示情境依赖性。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cfb9703de7d635e116138ace\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这是理论假设和早期证据的汇总，许多机制（如具体的交叉反应肽段、特定的代谢物浓度阈值）尚未在人体中得到完全验证或量化。\",\"contribution\":\"提出了一个系统的机制分类框架，区分了四种主要信使类型（活细菌/MAMPs、代谢物、细胞因子、免疫细胞）及其对应的免疫效应（增强抗原性、佐剂效应、旁观者激活、抑制性调节）。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5066353359ccce6eaf061846\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文中详细对比了16S rRNA测序与宏基因组测序的优缺点，以及无菌小鼠模型的生理缺陷和微生物残留干扰问题。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f9f44dd21b9842e42af4e79a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"概述了FMT、益生元/饮食调整、益生菌、噬菌体和代谢物补充等多种干预手段的原理及当前进展。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e48120ecf4cebc5e1bafcaa0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"指出当前研究多聚焦于细菌，而真菌（mycobiome）和病毒（virome）也可能调节免疫，但目前证据较少。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::01c5d880718ea85b7b6946a3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述涵盖多种癌症类型（黑色素瘤、肺癌、肾癌、胰腺癌等）和多种ICI药物，但在具体机制上多为小鼠模型推导，需区分动物实验结论与人类临床证据的强度差异。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::19a3a17ed39f9ff6414416d1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的‘共识’是基于多篇独立研究的汇总，而非单一大型随机对照试验的结果，因此具体菌种的预测价值仍存在争议和不一致性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::05c51b859eba2ea39414cad8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"机制部分包含大量‘假说’和‘潜在’通路，并非所有提及的机制都在人类实体瘤中得到了直接证实，引用时需保持谨慎，避免过度解读因果关系。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d6fcc7ceb27b41dcafc8367b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0055\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s216\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8e2259ff05ac2be19653b172\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b667b56f2d16309d6772beaa\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c0b1b32b8dc03ed0bac355c4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用系统综述方法。1. 检索策略：基于PICO框架，在三个主要数据库中搜索关于实体瘤患者ICI治疗与肠道微生物群的研究。2. 筛选：两名审稿人独立筛选摘要和全文，依据纳入/排除标准确定最终18项研究。3. 质量评估：使用修改版的ROBINS-I工具评估偏倚风险；因数据异质性高且缺乏置信区间，未使用GRADE系统评估证据质量。4. 数据合成：定性叙事综合。将细菌按分类学层级整理，并根据其在响应者（R）或无响应者（NR）中的出现情况，归类为“有利预后”或“不良预后”。重点比较不同癌症类型下的细菌分布，并讨论测序技术（16S vs MSS）和方法学差异带来的局限性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::eed32adb7a79149a08121391\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了截至2021年关于肠道微生物群与ICI疗效关联的综合图谱，明确了多个具有重复性的潜在预测性细菌物种（如F. prausnitzii, B. obeum）。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代具体的统计检验细节（如p值校正方法），仅进行了定性归纳。由于研究间异质性大（测序平台、样本采集时间、癌症类型、ICI药物种类不同），无法得出因果结论或统一的效应量。证据质量被评定为低或极低。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::26d4772ef636410fde68fb19\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"指出了当前领域的方法学不一致性，特别是16S rRNA测序与宏基因组鸟枪法测序结果的不可直接比较性，以及粪便样本与黏膜微生物群的差异。\",\"limits\":\"未能解决选择性报告偏倚的问题，因为许多原始研究的协议未在clinicaltrials.gov注册或未公开。对于混杂因素（如饮食、抗生素使用前的基线状态控制）的处理能力有限，因为原始研究对这些变量的报告不完整。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::69aa3cd296a7d2dc8d65e42b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"在所有纳入的实体瘤患者中，对比ICI响应者（R）与无响应者（NR）\",\"finding\":\"观察到特定的微生物群模式。最常报道与较好预后相关的物种包括：Faecalibacterium prausnitzii, Streptococcus parasanguinis, Bacteroides caccae, 和 Prevotella copri。最常报道与较差预后相关的物种包括：Blautia obeum 和 Bacteroides ovatus。此外，Akkermansia muciniphila 在两组中均有发现，不具有特异性区分度。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f75a1cfb377c725859dd8e5a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"不同癌症亚组（MM, NSCLC, mRCC, HCC/GI）\",\"finding\":\"虽然总体趋势一致，但具体细菌丰度和显著性在不同癌症类型间存在差异。例如，F. prausnitzii 在多种癌症中被提及，而某些细菌仅在特定癌症类型的研究中显著。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e4a641ef4e64ed5c6657e51d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d645e59bbd1d7226bdf4c703\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"动机在于尽管ICI疗法在某些癌症亚组中显示出持久疗效，但患者反应差异巨大且缺乏有效的预测生物标志物。已知肠道微生物群可能调节ICI疗效，但具体哪些微生物特征与反应相关尚不明确。本研究试图通过系统综述厘清粪便微生物群组成与ICI治疗反应（响应vs无响应）之间的关联模式。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::19de0255db9ece45e8630f66\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"针对接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI，包括抗PD-1、抗PD-L1或抗CTLA-4）治疗的实体瘤患者，研究其粪便肠道微生物群组成与ICI治疗反应之间的关联。涵盖的癌症类型包括转移性黑色素瘤（MM）、非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）、转移性肾细胞癌（mRCC）、肝细胞癌（HCC）和胃肠道癌症。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f6491012a4293912ddddd53f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"这是一篇2023年发表的系统综述，旨在调查肠道微生物群作为预测生物标志物的潜力。作者遵循PRISMA指南，检索了EMBASE、Medline和Cochrane Library数据库，筛选出18项涉及775名实体瘤患者的队列研究。由于各研究在测序方法（16S rRNA、宏基因组鸟枪法测序等）、癌症类型及反应定义上的异质性，无法进行定量荟萃分析，因此采用定性叙事综合的方法。研究识别出与良好预后（响应者）和不良预后（无响应者）相关的特定细菌物种，并讨论了不同技术方法和混杂因素对结果解释的影响。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::dc73955ff0b33d2c2d3b1c0c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文为综述提供了关键的实证汇总素材，主要用于回答“哪些肠道微生物与ICI疗效相关”这一描述性问题。它不直接提供机制解释，而是列出了观察到的关联列表。对于规划员而言，其价值在于提供了一个经过筛选的、跨多种癌症类型的细菌清单，可作为后续机制探讨的基础背景，同时其讨论部分关于方法学局限性的内容有助于在综述中解释为何不同研究结果可能存在冲突。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::049c91454bbba7e4bdf1eb58\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"仅展示观察性关联，不涉及因果机制。结果受限于原始研究的定义（如RECIST标准 vs irRC标准）和测序深度。不能直接外推至所有ICI药物或所有癌症类型，需结合具体癌症背景使用。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了具体的细菌物种列表及其与ICI疗效（响应/无响应）的关联方向。例如，确认了F. prausnitzii, S. parasanguinis, B. caccae, P. copri常出现在响应者中，而B. obeum, B. ovatus常出现在无响应者中。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::320c7d3b927b05662dea04a9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"本综述未进行功能富集分析或代谢通路分析，因此提供的机制信息是间接的、基于文献引用的，而非本研究的新发现。不能替代专门的机制研究来解释“如何”调节。\",\"contribution\":\"在讨论部分简要提及了一些细菌的功能背景（如F. prausnitzii维持肠道稳态，B. obeum可能具有抗生素抗性），并引用了其他研究关于FMT（粪菌移植）克服耐药性的案例。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::14f48a9c0511bfb3c2367595\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"讨论了16S rRNA测序与宏基因组鸟枪法测序（MSS）的技术差异，指出前者覆盖率高但偏差大，后者可分析功能但成本高且易受宿主DNA干扰。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d5d6f1a93b34ca48b5be8c47\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"提到粪便样本与黏膜微生物群的差异，以及粪便样本可能无法完全代表与宿主免疫系统相互作用的黏膜相关菌群。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6641e04e62791a2d4b376814\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"提及FMT在黑色素瘤患者中恢复ICI响应的案例研究。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::edbbd751ab16d1eae729ec05\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述包含的是观察性关联，而非因果关系。细菌的存在可能与疗效相关，但不一定导致疗效。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ce0f3c36bf1bb726074ca4f9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"结果受到原始研究中“响应者”定义不一致的影响（部分研究将稳定疾病SD视为响应，部分视为无响应），这可能导致某些细菌的分类模糊。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c2e2a294c7c188e4f32b612e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"不同癌症类型的微生物背景不同，不能简单地将一种癌症中发现的细菌标志物推广到其他癌症，除非有跨癌症的一致证据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6d04e4e129cf4c658534c39d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"由于未进行定量荟萃分析，所谓的“最常被报道”是基于频率的定性判断，而非统计学上的显著优势比。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1dad7205cfa2109d35fc769c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0295\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s184\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::318963856f1951debff390b4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cc6e9d9dbcf8904943e682a9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fdec5075cda50780958d8f2e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"遵循PRISMA 2020指南进行系统综述。单一评审员执行文献搜索、筛选、数据提取和偏倚风险评估。使用ROBINS-I工具评估观察性研究的偏倚风险。由于临床、方法和统计异质性过大，无法进行定量荟萃分析，因此采用基于效应方向和一致性的叙事综合（Narrative Synthesis）。重点分析了特定菌属/种、代谢通路、饮食因素以及纵向动态变化。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4b7fe47de065df24431a07bc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了截至2025年关于肠道微生物组与黑色素瘤ICI反应关联的全面定性综合，明确了SCFA产生菌的积极角色和真菌失调的消极角色，并指出了微生物组作为预测生物标志物和潜在治疗靶点的潜力。\",\"limits\":\"由于严重的异质性，无法提供定量效应估计。证据主要来自观察性研究，存在显著的混杂和选择偏倚。结论受限于纳入研究的规模小、单中心设计以及分析方法的不一致性。不能直接外推至其他癌症类型或不同免疫疗法组合。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::938e71d76663e61501972ebd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"多数队列中\",\"finding\":\"产短链脂肪酸（SCFA）的菌属（如Faecalibacterium prausnitzii, Akkermansia muciniphila, Bifidobacterium）丰度增加通常与治疗反应改善相关；而病原体或真菌（如Candida albicans, Malassezia restricta）富集或与失调相关的特征则与疗效降低和不良生存结局相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2179546388fe33b2e37076a9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"跨队列比较时\",\"finding\":\"微生物组-反应关联具有高度异质性和队列依赖性。没有单一的微生物签名能一致地预测所有队列的反应。例如，F. prausnitzii在某些队列中与无反应相关，而在其他大型再分析中被识别为一致的阳性生物标志物。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c7584d00f2e05f3e1c15e1d9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"机制层面\",\"finding\":\"微生物衍生的代谢物（如SCFA、钴胺素）可能通过调节树突状细胞功能、抗原呈递和T细胞激活来影响抗肿瘤免疫。纵向数据显示，治疗期间A. muciniphila的丢失可能与早期耐药性相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::373f32f8bc3e6618a2bb78ca\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"证据质量\",\"finding\":\"纳入的25项研究中，17项（68%）被评定为中度偏倚风险，8项（32%）为严重偏倚风险。主要偏倚来源包括残留混杂因素和小样本单中心设计。没有研究被评为低风险。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7d7587eb8993cdf4013907d1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2b0db90d979da2168d366c90\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管免疫检查点抑制剂改善了黑色素瘤患者的临床结局，但治疗反应差异巨大且缺乏可靠的预测生物标志物。本研究旨在解决：肠道微生物组的哪些特征（组成、多样性、功能）与ICI的治疗反应相关？其潜在的生物学机制是什么？当前的证据基础质量如何？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::15579518b50eb196b81bb83c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"人类黑色素瘤患者，接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI，包括抗PD-1、抗PD-L1或抗CTLA-4）治疗。聚焦于肠道微生物组（组成、多样性、代谢功能）与治疗反应（疗效及免疫相关不良事件irAEs）之间的关联。纳入2015-2025年间发表的观察性研究和数据集二次分析，排除干预性试验和仅暴露研究。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::87cdb1d49ace86cdf4fe5065\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"这是一篇系统综述，旨在评估肠道微生物组特征与黑色素瘤患者免疫检查点抑制剂治疗反应之间的关联及其潜在机制。作者通过PubMed数据库检索并筛选出25项符合条件的观察性研究，采用定性综合而非定量荟萃分析的方法，因为各研究在测序平台、分类方法、结果定义和分析流程上存在显著异质性。研究评估了微生物组成、多样性及代谢功能对治疗结局的影响，并使用了ROBINS-I工具对纳入研究的偏倚风险进行了正式评估。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::15a78806db3bf6146e66cf60\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为“肠道微生物组如何调节实体瘤中免疫检查点抑制剂的疗效”这一核心问题提供了关键的背景框架和具体证据汇总。它详细列举了与疗效正负相关的特定微生物类群（如F. prausnitzii, A. muciniphila vs. Candida），阐述了潜在的免疫调节机制（SCFA、DC成熟、T细胞激活），并强调了当前证据的异质性和局限性。这对于构建综述中关于“微生物组作为生物标志物的现状与挑战”以及“机制解释”的部分至关重要。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d8a2f9c469d95bbd2fcf7e8e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这些关联主要基于观察性研究，存在混杂因素。不同队列间结果不一致，不能简单地将某一菌属视为通用生物标志物。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了具体的微生物特征与ICI疗效关联的证据汇总：产SCFA菌（F. prausnitzii, A. muciniphila）通常与良好反应相关，而真菌失调（Candida, Malassezia）与较差反应相关。同时指出这种关联是异质的，没有单一的一致性签名。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6353277b76ca3f94e31fbe6d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"许多机制证据来自动物模型或体外研究，在黑色素瘤患者中的直接因果证据有限。综述本身未提供新的实验数据，而是综合现有解释。\",\"contribution\":\"阐述了微生物组影响免疫治疗的潜在机制：SCFA促进树突状细胞成熟、抗原呈递和CD8+ T细胞激活；微生物屏障完整性受损可能导致免疫抑制。还提到了纵向动态变化（如A. muciniphila丢失预示耐药）作为早期指标。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::85f2c57212b2af458d68af2d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"综述指出当前研究存在严重的异质性，包括测序平台、生物信息学管道、差异丰度分析方法（如LEfSe, DESeq2, ANCOM）的不一致，以及组成型数据的统计陷阱。这解释了为什么难以获得统一的生物标志物。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b51d1aa1a071a0ad56186c4f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"提到饮食（纤维、Omega-3）、抗生素使用、地理变异和宿主遗传是常见的混杂因素。大多数研究是小样本单中心设计，偏倚风险高。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2fa55144dd6936958f9ca74b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"指出某些研究发现α多样性与反应无关，或特定菌属在不同队列中表现相反（如F. prausnitzii在某些情况下与无反应相关）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9c35f083340ae354c42df6ca\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述仅针对黑色素瘤，虽然机制可能与其他实体瘤有重叠，但不能直接假设其在所有实体瘤中具有相同的效力或特异性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6a8ee95b372bbddb17edcded\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"纳入的研究均为观察性设计，因此发现的关联不等于因果关系。尽管引用了一项小鼠干预研究支持因果性，但这属于外部证据，非本综述的主要发现。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::741f5d210706336bf85b893a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"由于异质性，综述未提供合并效应量。任何关于特定菌属效应的解读都应谨慎，避免将其视为确定的预测标准。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5739c36a11fda93014ea8f6b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"综述承认未进行定量荟萃分析，因此其结论是基于叙事综合，可能存在选择偏倚或主观解释。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d32f64d557afe254ad0447cb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0565\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s009\",\"s045\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::04fa5d1460dc556fb89ebb28\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::81f1a8795e694f0e9d6ed206\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d5bf08d9e5eba1132b013f83\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"1. **研究对象与样本收集**：纳入109名SCC患者，收集基线（诊断时）和随访期（6个月或12个月）的刺激性全唾液样本。根据治疗方案分为化疗放疗组（n=50基线，n=33配对）、单纯手术组（n=15配对）等亚组。 2. **微生物组分析**：提取唾液DNA，扩增16S rRNA基因V4区，使用Illumina MiSeq测序。利用mothur软件进行序列处理，基于97%相似度聚类OTUs。使用NMDS、AMOVA评估群落结构差异；使用ALDEx2和LEfSe进行差异丰度分析；使用PICRUSt预测KEGG通路功能。 3. **蛋白表达分析**：对部分患者（n=48用于WB，n=28用于ELISA）的唾液样本进行DMBT1蛋白定量，采用Western Blot和ELISA技术，并使用线性混合模型分析时间效应。 4. **动物实验验证**：在裸鼠皮下注射UM-SCC-1细胞构建肿瘤模型，监测肿瘤生长，并在不同时间点收集唾液，通过Western Blot检测DMBT1表达变化，以验证SCC对宿主蛋白表达的抑制作用。 5. **关联分析**：计算唾液DMBT1蛋白表达水平与微生物组OTU丰度之间的Pearson相关系数，探索两者间的联系。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::33c982b34f406263a35061f0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了SCC治疗前后唾液微生物组纵向变化的详细图谱，区分了化疗放疗和单纯手术的不同影响模式。\",\"limits\":\"样本量相对有限，特别是单纯手术组和长期随访数据不足，限制了统计效力和对长期预后的推断。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2fd7f9218d115314b02c93f7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"首次在同一队列中将唾液微生物组变化与宿主抗菌蛋白DMBT1的表达联系起来，提出了“微生物-宿主蛋白”互作的可能机制线索。\",\"limits\":\"相关性分析基于小样本子集（n=20），且为观察性研究，无法确立因果关系；16S测序分辨率限制了对具体菌株功能的精确解析。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::02c05b85cb1a60ea994bc9c2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"识别了潜在的预后生物标志物（如基线Prevotella、治疗后Gemella/DMBT1），为无创监测治疗反应提供了方向。\",\"limits\":\"发现的特异性细菌标记物需在大独立队列中验证；作者承认多种分析方法（ALDEx2 vs LEfSe）结果不一致，提示方法学敏感性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c91312c9f1cf0c25ba5b9248\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"所有SCC患者治疗后（6个月 vs 基线）\",\"finding\":\"唾液微生物组的整体丰富度和多样性显著降低；Firmicutes门丰度增加，Bacteroidetes、Fusobacteria和Proteobacteria门丰度减少；Porphyromonaceae和Prevotellaceae科减少，Lactobacillaceae科增加。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ec6801442219d92b6836ac45\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"化疗放疗组（n=33配对）\",\"finding\":\"治疗后微生物群落结构发生显著变化；Richness降低但Alpha多样性无显著变化；Prevotellaceae、Pasteurellaceae等减少，Lactobacillaceae增加。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2597364cbf3f04094bbe9463\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"单纯手术组（n=15配对）\",\"finding\":\"治疗后Richness显著降低，但群落结构（Beta多样性）和Alpha多样性无显著变化；LEfSe显示术前富集未分类Lactobacillales spp.，术后富集Pseudomonas。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::dcf8090677ba2051d0d2a2ae\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"化疗放疗响应者 vs 非响应者（基线）\",\"finding\":\"群落结构有显著差异，但Alpha多样性无差异；LEfSe显示非响应者基线时Prevotella (OTU0029) 丰度较高，而响应者中未分类Pasteurellaceae、Veillonella等较多。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1a844f0beb8a0fc411b0ecbf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"化疗放疗响应者 vs 非响应者（治疗后6个月）\",\"finding\":\"群落结构差异更显著（p=0.006）；响应者中Veillonella、Streptococcus、Rothia、Gemella等丰度较高；PICRUSt预测响应者氨基酸合成代谢通路富集，非响应者糖代谢和脂肪酸合成通路富集。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::41be884663059428b61b7412\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"SCC患者唾液DMBT1表达\",\"finding\":\"治疗前DMBT1表达较低；治疗后6个月和12个月DMBT1表达显著升高（约1.9-2.1倍）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5da8f6e36bf9d147e28492d2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"小鼠肿瘤模型（UM-SCC-1注射）\",\"finding\":\"与对照组相比，携带肿瘤的裸鼠唾液DMBT1分泌显著减少，证实SCC抑制宿主DMBT1表达。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0360f9d26c1481afa2d08391\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"DMBT1表达与微生物组相关性\",\"finding\":\"治疗后DMBT1水平的增加与Gemella、Pasteurellaceae、Lactobacillus和Oribacterium等菌群丰度的增加呈正相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b8bf5a4021a56af50c5297da\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6b71c4645c71140a08726ac0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"1. SCC治疗（特别是化疗放疗与手术）如何改变患者的唾液微生物组结构和功能？ 2. 治疗前后的唾液微生物组特征是否能预测SCC患者对化疗放疗的反应？ 3. 唾液中的抗菌蛋白DMBT1在治疗过程中的表达变化如何，且其与微生物组的变化是否存在关联？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6d847255917453bd4ef1d903\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"口腔鳞状细胞癌（SCC）患者的唾液微生物组及抗菌蛋白DMBT1表达；涉及化疗放疗联合治疗与单纯手术治疗的纵向对比，以及治疗反应（响应者vs非响应者）的关联分析。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::11668d1545927d2927d2d8e4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本研究是一项针对口腔鳞状细胞癌（SCC）患者的纵向研究，旨在探讨癌症治疗对唾液微生物组的影响，并考察这些变化与治疗反应及唾液抗菌蛋白DMBT1表达之间的关联。研究纳入了接受不同治疗方案（化疗放疗、单纯手术等）的患者，通过16S rRNA基因测序分析基线（0个月）和治疗后（6个月）的唾液样本。结果显示，治疗后唾液微生物组的丰富度和多样性普遍降低，且特定菌群结构发生显著变化。在化疗放疗患者中，响应者与未响应者在治疗前后的微生物组成存在差异，其中Prevotella属与非响应相关，而Gemella属等与响应相关。此外，研究发现SCC会抑制唾液DMBT1的表达，治疗后DMBT1水平回升，且DMBT1水平的增加与Gemella等特定菌群的丰度增加呈正相关。该研究首次在同一队列中纵向追踪了SCC治疗引起的唾液微生物组变化及其与宿主免疫蛋白表达的关联。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::80a47613fde36c399548c3a0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文虽聚焦于口腔鳞状细胞癌（SCC）而非直接研究肠道微生物组与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs），但其核心逻辑——即肿瘤微环境/局部微生物组通过调节宿主免疫因子（如DMBT1）进而影响治疗反应——为综述提供了重要的旁证和机制类比素材。它展示了实体瘤治疗（化疗放疗）中微生物组作为预后因子的潜力，以及宿主-微生物互作在调节治疗结局中的作用。对于综述而言，此文可作为“非肠道微生物组在实体瘤治疗反应中的作用”或“宿主免疫蛋白介导的微生物-治疗反应关联”的案例，补充关于局部微环境（口腔）而非全身肠道微生物组的证据，并提示DMBT1等分子可能作为连接微生物与宿主免疫反应的潜在桥梁。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f8f66a1710930b7ca86a27cf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"研究对象为口腔癌，治疗手段为化疗放疗而非ICIs；样本量较小；仅展示关联性，未证明因果。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了实体瘤（SCC）中局部微生物组（唾液）与治疗反应（化疗放疗响应）关联的证据。虽然不涉及ICIs，但证明了微生物组特征（如Gemella, Prevotella）可区分响应者与未响应者，支持微生物组作为治疗反应生物标志物的概念。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f1f25d86db4599ba1868cbea\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制仅为相关性观察，未通过干预实验验证DMBT1是否直接导致菌群变化或改善疗效；DMBT1主要涉及先天免疫凝集作用，与ICIs涉及的适应性免疫（T细胞）机制不同。\",\"contribution\":\"揭示了宿主抗菌蛋白DMBT1在SCC中被抑制，治疗后恢复，且其水平与特定菌群（Gemella等）正相关。这提供了一个具体的分子机制假设：宿主免疫蛋白可能通过调节微生物组成来影响治疗微环境。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9032260ca5d7ec0ecf396fab\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"SCC患者治疗后唾液微生物组多样性降低、特定菌群（Lactobacillaceae增加，Porphyromonaceae减少）变化的描述。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fc6fcd557e9ca6c63cca3f18\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"DMBT1在肿瘤状态下被抑制，治疗后恢复并与有益菌群（Gemella）增加相关的发现。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0225372f9c7f55d65e3e3220\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"研究中提到ALDEx2和LEfSe分析结果的不一致性，以及16S测序物种分辨率的限制。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0358fad2236acb82385888a5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"本文研究的是口腔鳞状细胞癌（SCC）的化疗放疗反应，而非黑色素瘤或其他实体瘤的免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）反应。因此，其发现的微生物标志物（如Gemella, Prevotella）不能直接外推至ICIs疗效预测。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8d400174eb4e66ce74983b9f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"DMBT1是一种唾液抗菌蛋白，主要参与先天免疫和病原体凝集，与ICIs作用的适应性免疫通路（PD-1/PD-L1, CTLA-4）不同。将其机制直接套用于ICIs需谨慎，应视为不同的免疫调节路径。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::894dab08e63ef8cc37e52a65\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"研究样本量有限（特别是配对样本和长期随访数据），且为单中心研究，结果的普适性有待验证。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f282099a77f4f5d8f5b20288\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"微生物组与治疗反应的关联多为观察性，未排除混杂因素（如抗生素使用、口腔卫生状况等）的潜在影响。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9aea8e8a548ecbdf7c26d798\",\"source_handle\":\"P0302\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-a91f0ed643887e9f1b1d\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"missing\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-5aad79f97d71912b82ad\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"missing\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-c92166e138f72865e733\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"missing\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-ef95a97dcd7bd8c151c4\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"missing\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-4fa4a8b9381a7a33035d\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"missing\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-501f35983c2f020a5c71\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"missing\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-b65d3b6b4567139063c9\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"missing\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-81ec1ef0c2a046851171\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"missing\"},{\"kind\":\"assets\",\"reason\":\"supplementaryFiles_fetch_body_too_large\",\"status\":\"missing\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s032\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::84a28c504a034d3cef0d5c6b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8fe692234c2fbed55ba6ed0f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c2466fcd955a9bec6b8ae2db\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"The authors performed a meta-analysis of raw 16S rRNA amplicon and whole-genome shotgun (WGS) metagenomic sequencing data from five public datasets (Chaput, Frankel, Gopalakrishnan, Matson, Routy). They applied a uniform bioinformatics pipeline: Resphera Insight for 16S taxonomic assignment and MetaPhlAn2 for WGS. Statistical analysis included random effects meta-analysis models (Hedges' g) to identify species enriched in R or NR groups, correcting for false discovery rate (FDR). An 'integrated microbiome prediction index' was constructed using weighted coefficients of significant species. Validation was performed on three independent cohorts (Peters, Hakozaki, Zheng) representing melanoma, NSCLC, and hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC). Sensitivity/specificity analyses (AUC) were used to evaluate index performance.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::179f3ff7e459d0dc0a7d563b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Provides a standardized bioinformatics pipeline for reanalyzing heterogeneous microbiome data, demonstrating that consistent methods can resolve inconsistencies in prior reports.\",\"limits\":\"Relies on retrospective reanalysis of publicly available data; response criteria varied across original studies (e.g., definition of Stable Disease); limited information on concurrent medications other than antibiotics; validation cohorts were small and diverse in tumor type.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fa2ed9facd6ef67ae810e9c0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Identifies a robust set of bacterial signatures associated with ICI non-response, suggesting that targeting these microbes may be a viable therapeutic strategy.\",\"limits\":\"Correlation does not imply causation; mechanistic insights are limited to functional pathway predictions (PICRUSt) and require experimental validation.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cac8fc30ee9c4641c814a9a4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Develops an integrated prediction index that outperforms single-species or literature-derived indices in predicting non-response.\",\"limits\":\"Index performance varied by tumor type (better in Melanoma/HCC than NSCLC); requires further validation in larger prospective cohorts.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bcd2e6342e95ae2f0d004e35\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Reanalysis of 5 cohorts (n=303) using random effects model and FDR correction\",\"finding\":\"Confirmed enrichment of Faecalibacterium prausnitzii, Bifidobacterium longum, Collinsella aerofaciens, and Enterococcus faecium in responders (R). Identified novel R-enriched OTUs including Roseburia hominis, Oxalobacter formigenes, and Prevotella buccalis.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::96739fee47f46631b98b259f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Reanalysis of 5 cohorts (n=303) using random effects model\",\"finding\":\"Identified multiple species enriched in non-responders (NR), including Veillonella parvula, Bacteroides spp. (fragilis, coprocola, thetaiotaomicron, uniformis), Clostridium spp., Parasutterella excrementihominis, Scardovia wiggsiae, Oribacterium sinus, and Megasphaera micronuciformis. NR signals were generally stronger and more consistent than R signals.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e39ab82b58c28bb326e5e1d7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Comparison of integrated index vs. literature-based indices\",\"finding\":\"The NR-associated integrated index showed the strongest association with ICI outcome (mean AUC 70.3%), outperforming literature-based indices which did not show significant NR signals. The composite index also modestly improved over literature indices.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::79194d46c5c532505ce8f755\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Validation in 3 independent cohorts (Melanoma, NSCLC, HCC; n=105)\",\"finding\":\"The sum integrated index performed well in Melanoma (AUC >80) and HCC (AUC >80). Performance in NSCLC was lower but improved when patients with recent antibiotic exposure were excluded. Antibiotic exposure negatively impacted alpha diversity and index performance.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b7672a715582a1cdf22eda76\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Longitudinal analysis (Chaput and Routy cohorts)\",\"finding\":\"No significant changes in beta diversity or specific taxa over time during ICI treatment, suggesting stability of the gut microbiome during therapy.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::748a3802a00a439baaa42415\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::624f26be2012347fc6c26e0a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"Previous studies on the gut microbiome and ICI response have yielded inconsistent results due to variable analytic methods, small sample sizes, and differing bioinformatics pipelines. This study aims to determine if a standardized computational approach can reveal robust, generalizable microbial biomarkers for ICI outcomes across different cancer types and geographic locations, specifically focusing on identifying signals for both responders and non-responders.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0178b697c366cb2c1b5339eb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"The study focuses on the gut microbiome as a biomarker for predicting clinical outcomes (response vs. non-response) in patients with solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, HCC) treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It reanalyzes raw 16S rRNA and metagenomic sequencing data from five previously published cohorts (n=303 unique patients) and validates findings in three independent cohorts (n=105).\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d845e1afbea13aaf3976bcf2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"This empirical study addresses the inconsistency in microbial biomarkers for ICI efficacy across previous small-scale studies by applying a uniform computational pipeline to reanalyze raw sequencing data from multiple cohorts. The authors identified novel bacterial signatures associated with responders (R) and non-responders (NR), developed an integrated microbiome prediction index, and found that signals associated with non-response were stronger and more consistent than those for response. The study highlights the potential of NR-associated indices to identify patients who might benefit from microbiome-based interventions.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::095b02036b06ac9703f600e1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"This paper provides a large-scale, standardized reanalysis of existing microbiome data related to ICI efficacy. Its primary value lies in establishing a robust set of microbial biomarkers for non-response (NR) to ICIs, which contrasts with earlier focus on responders. It offers specific bacterial species and an integrated index that can be used to contextualize the consistency of microbiome signals across different solid tumors and to discuss the impact of technical variability (pipelines) on biomarker discovery.\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::11e2125872af1f66df5f62d3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Findings are based on retrospective reanalysis; causal mechanisms are not established. Performance varies by tumor type (e.g., weaker in NSCLC validation).\",\"contribution\":\"Identifies specific bacterial species and OTUs consistently associated with ICI non-response (NR) across multiple cohorts, including Veillonella parvula, Bacteroides spp., and Clostridium spp. Also identifies responder-associated species like Faecalibacterium prausnitzii and novel ones like Roseburia hominis.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bf7c276dd59d8a0219936d6c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Index validation was done on small independent cohorts; generalizability to all solid tumors is not fully confirmed.\",\"contribution\":\"Demonstrates that an integrated microbiome prediction index based on NR-associated species has higher predictive power (AUC ~70%) than literature-based indices or responder-only indices.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::96ef0834806dc6baddff3e99\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Antibiotic timing and definitions varied across cohorts; only a subset of cohorts had detailed antibiotic metadata.\",\"contribution\":\"Shows that antibiotic exposure negatively impacts microbiome diversity and reduces the predictive accuracy of the integrated index, particularly in NSCLC.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c51679519310d068f7861a58\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Functional predictions are inferred from taxonomy (PICRUSt) and not directly measured via metatranscriptomics or metabolomics; correlation does not prove mechanism.\",\"contribution\":\"Functional analysis (PICRUSt) suggests pathways enriched in NR (nucleotide sugar metabolism, nitrogen metabolism) and R (flagella assembly, pantothenate biosynthesis, mTOR pathway modifiers).\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::073968f55285ef0742e6ad52\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"The paper critiques previous studies for using variable pipelines and small samples, leading to inconsistent results. It demonstrates how standardization reveals stronger NR signals.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a5c489f0a7e54389c1755261\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Discussion of varying response criteria (RECIST vs irRC), undefined Stable Disease (SD) categories, and regional differences in baseline microbiota (Bacteroides vs Prevotella).\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::84b679c186c7b08ce88d7bed\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Longitudinal analysis showed no significant beta diversity shifts during treatment.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::31ac71e0821ad9aff5bee684\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The study is a reanalysis of existing data; it does not generate new primary clinical trial data.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::dfdbf5602d00d1826650b214\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Predictive indices are derived from retrospective cohorts and validated on small independent sets; they are not yet clinically approved tools.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6d7b47f3ffe77612c95990e7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Functional predictions are based on PICRUSt, which has known limitations compared to direct metagenomic/metatranscriptomic profiling.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b5aaf7bd486b74da01ed0f60\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The strong signal for non-response may reflect a distinct biological phenomenon or simply be more robustly detectable due to methodological factors; caution is needed in interpreting this as a universal rule for all ICI contexts.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::35b9fb64277036b388571810\",\"source_handle\":\"P0354\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"identity\",\"reason\":\"source identity was not independently verified\",\"status\":\"input_attributed\"},{\"kind\":\"pdf\",\"reason\":\"full-page text extracted; page positions retained\",\"status\":\"fitz\"},{\"kind\":\"fitz\",\"reason\":\"layout, table relations, formulas, figure pixels, and scanned text may be lost\",\"status\":\"known_gap\"},{\"kind\":\"xml_text_cleanup\",\"reason\":\"removed 24 XML 1.0 forbidden characters from derived PDF text; original PDF and page positions retained\",\"status\":\"normalized\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s190\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8e94c8ea9c941d64a48d876a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ee8a66419522a8b794e8398e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2a7b8862c1f98643fd80ef06\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"作为一篇专家共识/综述，本研究通过召集多学科专家（来自工业界、学术界和政府），针对特定主题（免疫调节与调制的系统评估）进行文献回顾和讨论。文章采用分类叙述的方法，按样本类型（血清/血浆、白细胞、组织、骨髓、微生物组、输入细胞）和技术层面（蛋白质组学、转录组学、基因组学、细胞表型）梳理现有知识和最佳实践建议。最后，提出了一种名为“het set”（异质数据集）的概念框架，用于整合来自不同组织和测定的数据，并列举了适用于此类数据的统计分析方法（如回归建模、网络分析、惩罚回归、决策树、关联规则挖掘）。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::327f9d7024d3a5af4c46cfd7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了癌症免疫治疗中多种生物样本（特别是非传统样本如骨髓、微生物组）的标准化采集和处理建议；总结了高通量检测技术的优缺点；提出了整合多维免疫监测数据的分析框架。\",\"limits\":\"这是一篇基于专家意见和文献回顾的建议性综述，而非原始实证研究；许多建议（特别是关于微生物组和骨髓的具体操作）基于初步数据或类比推理，缺乏大规模临床试验验证；对于具体生物标志物的临床效用，文章指出大多数尚未完全确立。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::003006b073e98476774bfbee\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"外周血样本处理\",\"finding\":\"抗凝剂类型、凝血时间、温度、储存条件和冻融次数显著影响血清肽图谱和细胞因子测量的可重复性；血浆被认为是研究细胞外囊泡（EV）最生理相关的介质。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6ae13d9acca8ce2cc9c8cb87\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"肿瘤组织活检\",\"finding\":\"存档的福尔马林固定石蜡包埋（FFPE）样本存在显著的预分析变异性，且可能无法代表疾病进展或复发时的免疫微环境；推荐在可行且符合伦理的情况下使用专门的研究活检，并严格记录缺血时间和处理步骤。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8ee1419266e7e289796f7d71\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"骨髓样本\",\"finding\":\"骨髓中的T细胞主要是记忆T细胞且CD8+ T细胞富集，与外周血不同；EDTA抗凝优于肝素用于需要PCR的研究；避免脱钙过程对核酸/蛋白的损伤，推荐使用“颗粒团块”（particle clots）或快速冷冻部分核心样本。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7a22cbec6f73ccf3e4986471\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"肠道微生物组\",\"finding\":\"肠道微生物组的组成影响多种癌症治疗（包括检查点抑制剂）的疗效；目前证据主要来自动物实验，临床数据有限；16S rRNA测序是常用方法，但物种水平鉴定能力受限；宏基因组学和宏转录组学成本更高且分析更复杂。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::813e24becfcb2118e1486e14\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"数据整合与分析\",\"finding\":\"单一分析往往无法捕捉系统性免疫反应；建议构建“het set”以跨平台、跨组织整合数据；可使用监督算法（如决策树、随机森林）进行分类，或使用无监督方法（如聚类、关联规则挖掘）发现模式。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f5adfe51e5b1cafc2916b6cf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::152e64ef8855d73e73d9abc9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"随着癌症免疫疗法的进展，识别和评估预测性及预后性生物标志物成为关键，但目前缺乏统一的系统性方法来监测免疫反应并解释从各种测定中获得的数据。需要解决如何标准化样本采集、选择适当的检测技术以及整合复杂的多维度数据以指导临床决策的问题。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0f0bbfb2ec3d683eb75b46d3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"癌症免疫治疗（包括检查点抑制剂、过继细胞疗法等）中的免疫监测，涵盖外周血、肿瘤微环境（TME）、骨髓、微生物组及输入细胞等多个样本来源的采集、处理、分析及数据整合策略。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f033e89d6dd4a750ee095ec2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是Society for Immunotherapy of Cancer (SITC)免疫生物标志物工作组第3工作组（WG3）发布的综述，旨在为癌症免疫治疗的免疫监测提供系统性评估和建议。文章讨论了不同生物样本（血液、组织、骨髓、微生物组、输入细胞）在免疫治疗背景下的独特采集和处理要求，介绍了用于评估潜在生物标志物的高通量检测方法（如流式细胞术、质谱、测序、蛋白阵列等），并提出了整合多平台异构数据以分析系统性宿主反应的分析框架。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::506b8ef426b1a282e1ce913c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为理解肠道微生物组如何影响免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效提供了重要的背景机制和现状评估。虽然它不直接提供针对实体瘤的详细临床效应数据，但它确立了微生物组作为免疫调节关键因素的生物学基础，指出了当前证据主要来自动物模型的限制，并提示了未来通过靶向微生物组增强疗效的可能性。此外，文中关于系统性免疫监测和数据整合的建议有助于理解如何设计和解释涉及微生物组与ICI交互作用的临床研究。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ec283d051b18bb5f3914f5e5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"明确说明目前的临床证据有限，大部分信息来自实验动物模型；未提供具体的实体瘤患者队列中微生物组变化与ICI疗效的相关性数据。\",\"contribution\":\"确认了肠道微生物组的存在及其组成是多种癌症治疗（包括免疫检查点抑制剂）疗效的必要条件，并受其影响。指出微生物组通过教育浸润免疫细胞产生炎症介质来促进抗肿瘤适应性免疫反应。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::16877ef95490bf21b9b15a9b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制描述较为通用，未详细阐述针对实体瘤中特定ICI（如抗PD-1/PD-L1）的具体分子或细胞通路细节；未区分不同肿瘤类型的特异性机制。\",\"contribution\":\"描述了微生物组调节免疫反应的一般机制：微生物群落在上皮屏障表面定植，调节人体生理功能，特别是炎症和免疫。特定的细菌属或种已被鉴定为促进或拮抗不同类型癌症治疗或抗肿瘤宿主免疫反应。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b4e7f876dc628cc4f086184c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文中详细讨论了微生物组样本（粪便、皮肤、口腔黏膜等）的采集、存储、测序（16S vs 宏基因组）和分析流程，强调了标准化对于结果可重复性的重要性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::46c12acec25f6e1dcb845584\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"介绍了“het set”概念及多种统计分析方法（回归、网络分析、机器学习）用于整合来自不同组织和测定的数据。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0b6dd6570db281557df3e0a5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"指出抗生素、放疗和化疗会诱导微生物组组成的持久变化，通常伴随细菌种类减少。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4bb08d432bb800e728cfe260\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"作者明确指出关于微生物组在人类癌症患者中的预后意义和生物标志物识别的信息主要来自动物实验，临床数据尚不充分，因此在将其应用于实体瘤ICI疗效解释时需谨慎外推。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::df9d5f37496e94405874868d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述侧重于监测方法和数据分析框架，而非具体的因果机制验证，因此其提供的机制描述属于一般性生物学原理，而非针对特定实体瘤-ICI组合的详细分子机制。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8aadd980b9319449bbd782c2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的微生物组对治疗的影响是广泛的（包括化疗、放疗、过继细胞疗法等），需结合其他文献聚焦于免疫检查点抑制剂的特异性作用。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8cb8976381d79ba681012156\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"deep_read_material\",\"paper_title\"],\"value\":\"Systematic evaluation of immune regulation and modulation\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1b71aa5a219b2d5029ae6dcf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"deep_read_material\",\"plain_text\"],\"value\":\"\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8d87fc269d7f9972c9e8f7e3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"deep_read_material\",\"question_material\"],\"value\":{\"examples\":[{\"attribution\":\"本研究\",\"conditions\":\"适用于癌症免疫治疗临床试验中的微生物组监测；涉及不同解剖部位（主要是粪便，也包括皮肤、口腔、阴道）；对比了16S扩增子测序与宏基因组/宏转录组测序在分辨率、成本和生物信息学复杂性上的差异。\",\"finding\":\"文章提出针对癌症免疫治疗研究中微生物组分析的标准化建议：\\n1. **标本采集与元数据**：强调标本采集和元数据显著影响下游分析。需确定感兴趣的解剖部位（如粪便、皮肤、口腔黏膜、阴道黏膜），因为空间分离较小的部位可能含有不同的细菌群落，因此采样一致性至关重要。大多数肿瘤研究聚焦于粪便，但其他部位也可提供独特信息。选择病例和对照、采样频率及方法时需考虑可行性（如自我收集）和患者参与度。\\n2. **测序策略选择**：\\n   - **16S rRNA基因测序**：最常用的方法，通过扩增和测序细菌16S rRNA基因的可变区域来确定微生物群的分类组成。由于新平台通常不测序完整基因，仅选择部分可变区域，这有助于有效鉴定属，但可能降低物种水平的识别能力。引物选择基于临床生物样本来源（如粪便样本常用V4引物，皮肤样本常用V1-3引物）以优化物种水平鉴定。Illumina MiSeq是最常用的平台。\\n   - **宏基因组测序（Shotgun Metagenomic Sequencing）**：分析样本中所有微生物的所有基因，不仅能鉴定细菌、真菌和病毒，还能识别群落中存在的基因和功能。最近还使用了宏转录组分析来评估哪些基因被转录及其程度。\\n3. **分析工具与比较**：\\n   - 16S数据分析常用QIIME和mothur等管道。\\n   - 宏基因组和宏转录组分析需要比扩增子测序更高的测序深度（导致更高成本），且生物信息学数据分析更具挑战性。\",\"reference_ids\":[],\"use_in_review\":\"提供微生物样本采集、存储及测序分析（16S vs 宏基因组）的标准化建议流程，直接回答任务要求。\"}],\"explanation\":\"文章指出，微生物组在调节人体生理功能（特别是炎症和免疫）方面发挥重要作用，其组成变化可影响癌症的发生、进展及对治疗的反应。目前微生物组分析尚未成为癌症患者免疫评估的常规部分，但 emerging evidence 显示其具有重要潜力。\\n\\n在标准化流程方面，核心原则是**标本采集的一致性和元数据的完整性**。由于不同身体部位的微生物群落具有特异性，且同一部位不同区域的微生物分布也可能存在差异，因此必须保持采样方法的一致性。对于粪便样本，考虑到可行性和患者依从性，自我收集是一种可行的策略。\\n\\n在测序技术的选择上，文章阐述了两种主要路径的差异：\\n1. **16S rRNA基因测序**：这是一种基于扩增子的方法，通过靶向细菌16S rRNA基因的可变区域进行测序。其优势在于成本低、技术成熟，能有效鉴定到“属”的水平。然而，由于现代测序平台通常无法覆盖完整的16S基因，仅测序部分可变区，这限制了其在“种”水平上的分辨能力。引物的选择（如V4用于粪便，V1-3用于皮肤）对优化特定样本类型的物种鉴定至关重要。\\n2. **宏基因组测序**：这是一种无偏倚的方法，对样本中所有DNA进行测序。它不仅能提供微生物的分类学信息（包括细菌、真菌、病毒），还能提供功能基因信息（即微生物群落的代谢潜能）。此外，宏转录组测序可以揭示实际表达的基因。尽管宏基因组提供了更丰富的信息，但它需要更高的测序深度，从而带来更高的成本和更复杂的生物信息学分析挑战。\\n\\n总体而言，标准化的关键在于根据研究目的（是需要快速、低成本的群落结构概览，还是需要高分辨率的物种鉴定或功能分析）选择合适的测序策略，并严格规范采样和元数据采集过程以确保结果的可重复性和临床相关性。\",\"question_id\":\"Q01\",\"remaining_points\":[\"具体的粪便保存液类型或运输温度细节未在文中详细展开，仅提到需考虑可行性和患者参与。\",\"未提及具体的DNA提取试剂盒或步骤的标准化建议。\"]},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5c7e21cd4798e1696a8e5476\",\"source_handle\":\"P0264\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-3aa25875e4222837763e\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s140\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ade3d4b04067f089ab421426\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"abstract\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c740a46407fafe55e7955cfa\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9f13e13821d3538904fef1dd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用前瞻性纵向队列设计。方法包括：对新鲜肿瘤组织进行全基因组测序（WGS）、RNA测序和T细胞受体（TCR）测序；对FFPE标本进行NanoString数字空间蛋白组学（DSP）；对粪便标本及受累的黏膜和肿瘤部位（拭子）进行全基因组鸟枪法宏基因组分析和16S rRNA基因测序；对正常组织和肿瘤组织进行配对测序。同时收集参与者生活方式、患者报告结果（PROs）和饮食评估。利用新鲜组织开发患者来源的异种移植（PDX）模型和细胞系。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::66359b9655767334b4ab4ac2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了一个大规模、多维度（基因组、转录组、蛋白组、微生物组、临床表型）的前瞻性MM队列的资源框架和基线数据。\",\"limits\":\"当前仅为中期进展报告，缺乏最终的因果关联分析、机制验证及统计学结论。样本量相对较小（n=98），且为单中心研究，可能限制外推性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3d02b5dc8e9f1f19733a1ad4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"截至2023年11月的初步队列数据（n=98）\",\"finding\":\"描述了人口统计学特征（中位年龄64岁，白人占85%）、原发部位分布（鼻口腔24%，泌尿生殖道30%，肛门直肠27%等）及临床体细胞突变情况（KIT 16%, NRAS 11%, BRAF 12%）。记录了样本收集进度（血液95例，粪便50例，黏膜拭子38例等）及生存随访数据（中位随访16个月，死亡率18%）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::913277b102318dbaa8556fa4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"所给摘要未交代最终分析结果\",\"finding\":\"摘要明确指出这是正在进行的研究，预期将提供关于肿瘤/微环境/宿主相互作用的见解，但具体的微生物组与ICI疗效的相关性发现、机制验证或统计显著性结果在提供的材料中缺失。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::95fea73e9cf28bfcfc45fadc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::29f3da943517f7c21e196c2a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"黏膜黑色素瘤的生物学机制尚不清楚，且对ICI治疗反应率低。研究旨在解决如何全面描绘MM患者的分子、微生物组和生活方式特征，以阐明驱动MM风险和ICI治疗反应/耐药的种系、肿瘤和外在因素之间的相互作用。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ef09cffcabe6808f0bfeeb84\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"黏膜黑色素瘤（Mucosal Melanoma, MM）患者队列，涉及分子变异、种系易感性、免疫状态、肠道/黏膜/肿瘤微生物组及可改变风险因素。研究情境为MD Anderson癌症中心的前瞻性纵向收集项目，截至2023年11月数据截止点。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::be2ef68bd2393e80b8da2faa\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文介绍了一项针对罕见且生物学特性独特的黏膜黑色素瘤（MM）的前瞻性、统一且全面的队列研究。鉴于MM具有低免疫原性和低肿瘤突变负荷，其对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）的反应率较低，本研究旨在通过多组学 profiling 确定分子变异、种系易感性、宿主免疫、微生物组（肠道、黏膜和肿瘤）以及可改变风险因素与晚期MM中ICI反应和耐药性之间的相互作用。目前处于数据收集和初步分析阶段，已入组98名患者，并建立了包括PDX模型和细胞系在内的生物样本库。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cd2f24db5132a85ce234315f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文为综述提供了关于黏膜黑色素瘤这一特定实体瘤亚型的详细基线特征和多组学数据采集框架。虽然尚未提供最终的微生物组-ICI疗效关联结果，但其详细的样本类型（粪便、黏膜拭子、肿瘤组织）和方法论（宏基因组、16S、DSP）为理解如何在固体肿瘤中整合微生物组数据提供了重要的技术参考和研究设计范例。它特别强调了黏膜部位特异性微生物组与肠道微生物组的并行采集策略。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::95e71795c27056d323112611\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"仅提供了数据采集的规模和类型，未提供微生物组组成与ICI疗效的具体相关性数据或统计结果。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了黏膜黑色素瘤患者队列中肠道微生物组（粪便）与局部微生物组（黏膜/肿瘤拭子）同步采集的方法论实例和基线样本量数据。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a5ea765bcd2a84ffaee32ef4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"具体机制通路尚未在摘要中揭示，仅作为计划中的分析路线。\",\"contribution\":\"介绍了结合数字空间蛋白组学（DSP）与微生物组测序的多组学分析路线，旨在探索宿主-微生物-肿瘤相互作用。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::761fcf1841a091cd68003482\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"98例患者的详细人口学、解剖部位分布及体细胞突变谱（KIT/NRAS/BRAF比例）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::96355d4436429d79a4c1ea05\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"提到收集了患者报告结果（PROs）和饮食评估，并计划调查可改变的微生物组决定因素。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2b27a3e449b05a269e203765\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该论文目前仅提供基线数据和队列描述，严禁将其预期的“洞察”解读为已证实的结论。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1a49dc35e97dbe4b7cac1c11\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"所有关于微生物组影响ICI疗效的陈述均为研究目标或假设，而非本摘要中的实证发现。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::46b04d946d8fdf0003113935\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"样本量有限（n=98），且为单中心前瞻性研究，其基线特征不能代表所有黏膜黑色素瘤患者。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6a24b121147a482f2d434c19\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"需明确区分“计划进行的分析”与“已完成的结果”，避免混淆研究设计与实际发现。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::87baace0cb0d72c5e862768b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0436\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"identity\",\"reason\":\"source identity was not independently verified\",\"status\":\"input_attributed\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"no complete research body was indexed\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\"status\":\"partial\"}],\"material_scope\":\"abstract_only\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s002\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d96e99ceab41ca2847f00ece\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e02e81b3bbda5c4946b05f7c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"no_material\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7d8b043a7e1885793d80ee0b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"研究设计采用横断面比较分析。首先，从22名接受ICI治疗的NSCLC和黑色素瘤患者及7名健康志愿者中收集粪便样本。其次，使用高通量培养组学技术（包括直接接种和富集培养，结合MALDI-TOF MS鉴定）分离细菌。同时，对部分NSCLC患者样本进行鸟枪法宏基因组测序。最后，通过统计检验（如Mann-Whitney检验、PERMANOVA、Chi-squared检验等）比较各组间的微生物组成、多样性和特定物种的富集情况，并分析培养组学与宏基因组结果的重叠与差异。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::59372e89d6fadb48d6a8f2c7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了癌症患者与健康人之间肠道微生物组成的具体差异图谱，特别是通过培养组学验证了特定菌属（如Bifidobacterium, Bacteroides）在健康状态下的富集，以及Enterocloster等在癌症中的富集。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代具体的机制验证实验，仅基于观察性数据提出假设。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b4f177e1ffefaafe67ae2a0e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"证实了培养组学与宏基因组测序在表征肠道微生物组时的互补性，指出了宏基因组可能遗漏的特定物种。\",\"limits\":\"样本量较小（N=22患者，N=7健康对照），统计效力有限，可能导致校正后的p值不显著。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ce1489e7b71a95bc8ebb19ed\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"初步识别了与ICI治疗响应和非响应相关的特定细菌物种，为后续生物标志物开发提供候选列表。\",\"limits\":\"缺乏功能验证，且健康对照组年龄显著小于癌症组，年龄因素可能混淆结果，限制了结论的外推性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a8cc8cda624eadf3085dd174\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"癌症患者 vs. 健康志愿者 (HV)\",\"finding\":\"HV组的平均物种丰富度显著高于癌症组（34 vs. 18, p=0.002），且β多样性显示两组形成独立聚类。HV组富集双歧杆菌属（Bifidobacterium spp.）和拟杆菌属（Bacteroides spp.），而癌症患者中肠梭菌属（Enterocloster spp.）和小韦荣氏球菌（Veillonella parvula）过度代表。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fa312f25ce9477605951cb39\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"ICI响应者 (R) vs. 非响应者 (NR)\",\"finding\":\"在非响应者中，Enterocloster属物种、Hungatella hathewayi和Cutibacterium acnes显著富集；而在响应者中，拟杆菌属（Bacteroides spp.）占主导地位。值得注意的是，在使用Benjamini-Hochberg方法校正p值后，部分差异不再显著。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::22d712b8e9e9bd60ef353f51\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"培养组学 vs. 宏基因组测序 (NSCLC亚组)\",\"finding\":\"宏基因组测序识别出的物种总数多于培养组学，但两者存在显著重叠。在培养组学鉴定的154个物种中，有61个（39%）也被宏基因组检测到，而94个物种仅由培养组学发现，突显了培养组学在检测低丰度或难培养物种方面的互补价值。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cb097ca6db878d31ac3e207f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a906be3054c8959c5a03e4d7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"现有的宏基因组测序技术在生物信息处理复杂性、阳性检测阈值要求以及无法检测活体生物等方面存在局限，阻碍了对肠道微生物组的完全表征。本研究试图解决如何通过整合培养组学和宏基因组测序来更稳健地定位微生物组作为ICI疗效生物标志物的问题，并探索癌症相关菌群失调及与治疗响应的关联。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bee4a1228e564c7b3d38e76a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"研究对象为接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和皮肤黑色素瘤患者，以及健康志愿者。研究情境涉及加拿大和英国的两个学术中心，样本包括22名癌症患者和7名健康对照。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0a9c1a13d27f322f57e4af6b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本研究旨在通过结合高通量培养组学（culturomics）和宏基因组测序，全面表征接受ICI治疗的癌症患者的肠道微生物组，以克服单一技术的局限性。研究对22名癌症患者和7名健康志愿者的粪便样本进行了培养分离和宏基因组分析。结果显示，健康志愿者的物种丰富度显著高于癌症患者，且两组在β多样性上存在显著差异。在临床结果方面，非响应者中富集了Enterocloster属、Hungatella hathewayi和Cutibacterium acnes，而响应者中则主要富集Bacteroides属。此外，宏基因组测序在NSCLC患者中识别出94种仅由培养组学检测到的独特物种，证实了两种方法的互补性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ff6d3e47c045447f4bd75832\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"论文展示了培养组学与宏基因组测序在物种检出上的重叠与差异，指出宏基因组可能遗漏94种仅由培养组学发现的物种。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2c54a33740e7dedb9f378026\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"论文引言部分回顾了预临床模型（无菌小鼠、抗生素处理）和大型荟萃分析中关于肠道微生物组与ICI疗效关联的证据。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a0dc85abe92182c72570f407\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"样本量小，且健康对照组年龄较轻，可能存在年龄混杂因素。结果主要基于观察性关联，未证明因果关系。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了接受ICI治疗的NSCLC和黑色素瘤患者与健康志愿者之间肠道微生物组成的具体差异数据。显示癌症患者物种丰富度降低，且特定菌属（如Enterocloster, Veillonella）在癌症中富集，而有益菌（如Bifidobacterium, Bacteroides）在健康人中富集。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ba6d102058ac96ac3a60ccd3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"统计显著性在校正后减弱。不同癌症类型（NSCLC vs Melanoma）的结果合并分析，可能掩盖亚型特异性。需结合其他研究综合评估这些标志物的普适性。\",\"contribution\":\"识别了与ICI治疗响应相关的特定细菌物种。响应者富集Bacteroides spp.，而非响应者富集Enterocloster spp., Hungatella hathewayi, Cutibacterium acnes。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c3980550b952c2ce2ae970e2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这是作者基于文献的推测性讨论，本研究本身未进行功能验证实验。机制链条尚不完整，属于待检验假说。\",\"contribution\":\"讨论了潜在的免疫调节机制，如免疫抑制性细菌（Enterocloster等）可能通过产生免疫抑制代谢物、促进调节性T细胞分化及影响MAdCAM-1表达来削弱抗肿瘤免疫反应。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::afcf0b683f352a74efcac3bb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文为综述提供了关于肠道微生物组与实体瘤免疫治疗响应关联的具体实证数据，特别是通过培养组学补充了宏基因组数据的不足。它提供了癌症患者与健康人、以及ICI响应者与无响应者之间微生物组成的详细对比，包括特定的富集物种和多样性差异。这些内容可用于支持综述中关于微生物组作为生物标志物的潜力及其组成特征的论述。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4b62454185d4e9a929a5285a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"样本量较小（N=22），统计效力有限，校正后的p值可能不显著，需谨慎解读其统计强度。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bb55235ea250ec552f4a84ba\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"健康对照组年龄显著低于癌症组，年龄是影响微生物多样性的已知因素，这可能混淆癌症与健康的差异归因。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a5a10bc9ee81f4b93fa5f751\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"研究为观察性设计，发现的细菌与ICI响应的关联仅为相关性，不能推断因果关系。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b44f84bfe77dd6283fc6eb07\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"机制部分为作者基于文献的推测，本研究未提供直接的功能验证证据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d830adacda90c0c9e376b722\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"结果来自NSCLC和黑色素瘤的混合队列，虽分别分析了NSCLC亚组，但整体结论可能不适用于所有实体瘤。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9d845cd59287ba918bdbdd11\",\"source_handle\":\"P0367\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s146\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6d240e881f1b784cd3dd7a66\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::05e59afaac2c6f222c295a1c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::16131621d0424b348f162b60\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用结构化但非系统的文献检索策略，基于 PubMed/MEDLINE, Embase, Scopus (2015-2026) 及会议摘要。优先纳入肺癌相关的临床队列和随机数据，补充机制性临床前研究。通过叙述性综合方法，整合不同研究关于微生物组成、多样性、代谢功能及临床混杂因素的发现，对比肠道与口腔微生物组的预测价值，并评估现有证据的方法学局限性和转化前景。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e8730e7cd201aaca9a764fdd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了肺癌 ICI 治疗中肠道与口腔微生物组预测价值的对比综述，明确了肠道微生物组更强的预测一致性，并指出了口腔微生物组的情境依赖性（仅在与化疗联用时可能有效）。\",\"limits\":\"作为叙事性综述，未应用 PRISMA 协议或正式偏倚风险评估；证据主要来自回顾性、单中心、小样本研究，缺乏前瞻性外部验证；SCLC 数据严重缺失；大多数研究未充分调整临床混杂因素。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0ff179b525de417fc3453d26\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"NSCLC 患者，高肠道微生物 alpha 多样性\",\"finding\":\"与改善的 PFS 和 OS 一致相关；作者指出这是跨地理人群稳健的指标。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::915d97969810c208a1b1dfee\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"特定有益菌属富集 (Akkermansia muciniphila, Faecalibacterium prausnitzii, Bifidobacterium)\",\"finding\":\"与增强的 ICI 疗效相关；但 Akkermansia 的作用呈剂量依赖性，过度富集可能关联免疫抑制环境。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6ea15ea0aa6712ed0c9eb521\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"使用抗生素或 PPI\",\"finding\":\"诱导菌群失调，显著降低 PFS 和 OS；抗生素在 ICI 启动前后 30-60 天使用影响最强。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::783f657ba50dbc2d934e71b6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"口腔/唾液微生物组\",\"finding\":\"预测价值有限且不一致；仅在局部晚期 NSCLC 接受放化疗联合免疫治疗的患者中观察到较高颊部微生物多样性与改善 PFS 的关联，而在转移性 ICI 单药治疗中无显著差异。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6ab4403099f415c643bd0258\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"功能性代谢标记 vs. 分类学标记\",\"finding\":\"功能性代谢能力（如 SCFA 产生通路）比单纯的分类学组成更可靠地预测 PFS；机器学习模型结合功能通路优于简单分类谱。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ddb8a03eee58ddc3801977a2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bc58b5231303597a3760c61c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"解决肺癌免疫治疗临床结局高度异质性的问题，特别是原发性/获得性耐药和免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）。旨在明确微生物组（尤其是肠道和口腔）能否作为非侵入性预测生物标志物，以优化 ICI 疗效并管理毒性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::02909b647840efc2dba418aa\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"肺癌（主要为非小细胞肺癌 NSCLC，小细胞肺癌 SCLC 数据缺失）患者接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗时的肠道和口腔/呼吸道微生物组。研究范围涵盖微生物组成、多样性、功能代谢物、临床混杂因素（抗生素、PPI）以及作为预测生物标志物的潜力。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cb10a6832f9807d6009cd8c5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"这是一篇叙事性综述，旨在综合评估微生物组作为肺癌免疫治疗疗效和毒性预测生物标志物的证据。文章系统梳理了肠道和口腔微生物组在 ICI 治疗中的角色，重点分析了特定菌属（如 Akkermansia muciniphila）、微生物多样性及代谢产物（如短链脂肪酸、肌苷）与无进展生存期（PFS）和总生存期（OS）的关联。同时，综述讨论了抗生素和质子泵抑制剂（PPI）对微生物组的破坏作用及其对预后的负面影响，并探讨了从单一物种标记向复合评分模型转变的趋势，以及粪菌移植（FMT）等干预策略的早期临床数据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::535b63d34d78fad676bccd7e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为综述规划提供了关键的比较维度：区分肠道与口腔微生物组的预测效力差异，以及分类学标记与功能性代谢标记的价值差异。它提供了具体的菌属、代谢物和临床混杂因素（抗生素/PPI）作为素材，用于回答 F1（效应）和 F2（机制），并强调了当前证据在标准化和前瞻性验证方面的缺口，有助于界定综述中“已证实”与“待验证”内容的边界。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bb97eec65a48d4b515580494\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"证据多为观察性关联，因果推断受限；口腔微生物组的阳性结果仅限于特定治疗组合（放化疗+免疫），不可外推至所有 ICI 场景；SCLC 数据缺失。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物组特征（高 alpha 多样性、特定有益菌）与 ICI 疗效（PFS/OS 改善）的正向关联证据，以及抗生素/PPI 暴露与疗效下降的负向关联证据。同时指出口腔微生物组在 ICI 单药治疗中预测价值有限，但在联合治疗中可能有信号。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::57ee940b9154bb8ebec71f77\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"许多机制细节源自黑色素瘤或胰腺癌的临床前模型，在 NSCLC 中的直接临床验证不足；部分代谢物（如 SCFAs）的作用具有双重性或情境依赖性（如 butyrate 在黑色素瘤中可能有害，在肺癌中未直接评估）。\",\"contribution\":\"详细阐述了介导机制：微生物代谢物（SCFAs, inosine, Uro A）通过调节树突状细胞成熟、CD8+ T 细胞priming、TME 重塑及 gut-lung axis 通讯来增强抗肿瘤免疫。同时也提到了潜在的负面机制（如某些 SCFAs 增加 Tregs，LPS 促进 IL-6）。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::faa138d638b4ef961b6eb3c4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"综述指出当前研究存在严重的异质性（测序平台、采样时间、生信流程），且多数研究未调整抗生素/PPI 等关键混杂因素。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1fd06e0624ce56a056b016c7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"提及 FMT-LUMINate 试验等早期阶段 FMT 干预数据，显示在 PD-L1 高表达 NSCLC 患者中取得高客观缓解率。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::acb1f02292f978c4fafc718b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述主要聚焦于 NSCLC，SCLC 的证据几乎空白，结论不能直接推广到小细胞肺癌。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6310df1ab85c47992b704566\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"口腔微生物组的预测价值具有高度的治疗情境依赖性（仅在联合治疗中可能有效），不能泛化为所有免疫治疗的通用标志物。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e334203f3b602dbb33f589fa\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"所引用的机制多来自其他肿瘤类型的临床前模型，在肺癌中的直接适用性需谨慎对待，作者已明确指出这一点。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3e99ed01c95e2c5a4011ad60\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"抗生素和 PPI 的影响是间接证据，综述未区分其对肠道和口腔微生物组的具体独立贡献。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::110a10deaf00848d9f26dfb3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0566\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s212\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5198686663715b4d988b29f0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f031ab1a69ff8b4e0e17ba3c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0e0fa36df6dd0fc2c9cfed13\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"本文采用叙述性综述与观点阐述相结合的方法。作者基于现有文献（引用12篇近期研究），从理论框架出发，梳理微生物组作为生物标志物和靶点的逻辑链条；通过分类讨论（疾病风险、治疗应用、肿瘤学）归纳微生物组在不同临床场景下的作用机制与应用现状；最后系统性地列出技术、伦理和基础设施层面的挑战，并提出未来发展方向。未涉及新的实验数据收集或统计分析。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::332802380144a43c6d4a885a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了微生物组在精准医学中应用的系统性全景图，特别是明确了其在肿瘤免疫治疗响应预测中的潜在角色及具体挑战。\",\"limits\":\"作为观点/评论文章，未提供原始实证数据；对具体机制的描述多为概括性陈述，缺乏针对特定固体瘤类型的详细分子通路分析；未提供具体的临床验证结果或统计显著性证据。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f9fe92e0bea3d4a62b063515\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"肠道菌群失调（Dysbiosis）\",\"finding\":\"可预测结直肠癌、炎症性肠病（IBD）、2型糖尿病、神经退行性疾病（帕金森、阿尔茨海默症）及肥胖等疾病的发病风险，早于临床症状出现。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::47fbbea83020b0d9819eba26\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"药物代谢与免疫治疗\",\"finding\":\"微生物组影响药物代谢（如左旋多巴在帕金森病中的代谢）及免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在癌症治疗中的疗效和毒性反应。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::da43992d96c01ea2a92d6d67\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"临床转化障碍\",\"finding\":\"个体间和时间上的高度变异性、采样与分析方法不一致、因果关系难以确立、纵向数据缺乏、监管框架不完善以及人群代表性偏差是主要限制因素。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3822fe691559dca026c2a8f3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"perspective\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bb9cf892c940f97762694aaf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管微生物组在精准医学中展现出巨大潜力，但当前面临的主要障碍是什么？如何将微生物组数据有效整合到临床决策中以实现真正的个性化预防、诊断和治疗？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d06066d95fe2d4cf0ab6fadd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"人类微生物组（Human Microbiome）在精准医学（Precision Medicine）中的应用前景，涵盖疾病风险分层、治疗应用及肿瘤学领域。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c5b931bcf0e389024f9c17af\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇编辑引言/观点文章，旨在探讨人类微生物组如何作为精准医学的新前沿重塑疾病病理学理解及个性化医疗策略。文章指出微生物组不仅是健康的被动反映者，更是代谢、免疫和药物反应等关键功能的动态参与者。作者综述了微生物组在早期诊断生物标志物开发、药代动力学影响（Pharmacomicrobiomics）、以及通过粪菌移植（FMT）或定制益生菌进行干预方面的潜力，同时分析了将其整合到临床实践中面临的标准化、因果推断、数据隐私及监管挑战，并展望了多组学联合与人工智能驱动的未来方向。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d3688b08d8644f3bf2b61ebe\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文为综述主题提供了宏观背景与机制概览，特别指出了肠道微生物组与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效之间的关联及其作为生物标志物的潜力。虽然它不直接回答“如何调节”的具体分子机制细节，但它确立了这一关系在精准医学中的重要性，并指出了当前研究的局限性（如因果性不明、异质性大），有助于规划员定位需要深入挖掘的实证研究缺口。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5b59140d7e2229eee427ca6e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"仅陈述关联性，未提供具体菌株或代谢物如何调节T细胞功能或肿瘤微环境的具体机制细节；未限定于特定类型的固体瘤，需结合其他实证研究细化。\",\"contribution\":\"确认了肠道微生物组组成与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效及毒性的关联，指出微生物特征可用于预测预后和指导治疗策略。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d000b902024313e63163e159\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"本文本身未阐明具体机制路径，仅作为问题提出的来源；其提到的机制多为一般性描述，缺乏针对固体瘤微环境的特异性解释。\",\"contribution\":\"提出了微生物组通过代谢产物（促进或抑制肿瘤生长）和影响免疫反应来参与疾病进程的假设性机制框架；指出了因果推断困难是当前知识瓶颈。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fbbe94d3915a0a2a24ca21c8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"微生物组作为个性化签名（Personalized Signature），受遗传、年龄、饮食、地理等因素影响；微生物组-宿主互作网络。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::42e720e8ac52c1a97ded02de\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"标准化难题、因果推断困境、纵向数据缺失、监管与伦理问题。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4104ad6c0144d63a09e922a3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"本文是观点/评论文章，非实证研究，其声称的关联（如微生物组与ICI疗效）需由后续实证论文验证，不可将此处的陈述视为已证实的结论。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c670656ba85216475975b742\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的‘固体瘤’相关内容较为宽泛，未区分具体癌种（如黑色素瘤、肺癌等），在提取机制时需警惕过度泛化。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ad10144c31957b028bc15924\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"作者强调因果推断困难，因此在利用本文素材时，应明确标注其为‘提出潜在联系’而非‘证明机制’。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f684c0e6dd0e8ac3f6de764b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0031\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"identity\",\"reason\":\"source identity was not independently verified\",\"status\":\"input_attributed\"},{\"kind\":\"pdf\",\"reason\":\"full-page text extracted; page positions retained\",\"status\":\"fitz\"},{\"kind\":\"fitz\",\"reason\":\"layout, table relations, formulas, figure pixels, and scanned text may be lost\",\"status\":\"known_gap\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s104\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::588f1a1bd6f3ca1ef607f35e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6fed13ee3e0c7ddd385f0f64\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cd73c0f181b0330ab3328ee1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用系统性文献回顾与综合叙述的方法。作者按逻辑顺序组织材料：从肠道黏膜屏障（先天免疫）入手，逐步分析对髓系细胞（巨噬细胞、树突状细胞）和淋巴系细胞（ILCs、T细胞）的影响；接着聚焦于特定微生物代谢物（SCFAs、肌苷、TMAO、色氨酸、胆汁酸）介导的抗肿瘤免疫反应；最后综述结合ICIs的微生物群治疗策略（FMT、益生菌、益生元、饮食）及其在预防irAEs中的应用。文中引用了大量临床观察性研究、队列研究和动物模型实验证据进行综合论述。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::639d3b1baaee912770ba34f1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物群调节癌症免疫治疗的多层次机制框架，涵盖了从黏膜屏障到全身免疫细胞（髓系和淋巴系）的广泛互作网络。\",\"limits\":\"作为综述，其结论依赖于引用的原始研究，部分机制主要基于动物模型或小型观察性研究，缺乏大规模随机对照试验的直接因果证据。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6ca66daecb12bd49acdd5815\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"系统梳理了五种主要微生物代谢物（SCFAs, Inosine, TMAO, Tryptophan derivatives, Bile acids）在免疫调节中的具体作用路径。\",\"limits\":\"不同研究中代谢物的测量方法、样本类型（粪便vs血浆）及癌症类型各异，导致直接比较存在困难；部分关联仅为相关性，尚未完全确立因果关系。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::947c49ed771b71df32520851\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"评估了FMT、益生菌、益生元和饮食干预等临床转化策略的现状，指出了标准化和定植效率等关键挑战。\",\"limits\":\"目前大多数临床试验处于早期阶段（Phase I/II），样本量小，且FMT供体选择、给药方案和长期安全性尚未标准化，难以形成统一的临床指南。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::86aadbb229018afa8c76e39c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"指出了当前研究的空白，如微生物特征是否具有泛癌种普适性、SCFAs的双向作用矛盾、治疗期间微生物动态变化的预测价值等。\",\"limits\":\"这些未解问题本身即为局限性的体现，表明该领域仍处于探索阶段，许多假设仍需未来多组学研究和大型前瞻性队列验证。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::184db8501301ec4d0502dee4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"转移性黑色素瘤患者接受伊匹木单抗治疗\",\"finding\":\"基线肠道微生物群富含Faecalibacterium和其他厚壁菌门的患者比富含拟杆菌的患者具有更长的无进展生存期（PFS）和总生存期（OS）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::879a32130d48905cf03cb52c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"胰腺导管腺癌（PDAC）小鼠模型及临床观察\",\"finding\":\"乳酸杆菌产生的TMAO促进巨噬细胞向M1型极化，增强效应T细胞反应并提高ICI疗效；而高表达AhR的巨噬细胞与PDAC患者较差的免疫治疗反应相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6915227a4c4ed95c31ceef17\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"晚期胃肠道癌症患者接受抗PD-1/PD-L1治疗\",\"finding\":\"粪便中较高浓度的乙酸、丙酸、丁酸和戊酸（SCFAs）以及与PD-1抑制剂疗效显著延长PFS相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f1356dfb86975218fe960216\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"三阴性乳腺癌临床观察队列（n=360）\",\"finding\":\"由梭菌目细菌产生的TMAO通过触发癌细胞焦亡增强CD8+ T细胞驱动的抗肿瘤免疫反应，从而提高免疫治疗疗效。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::30b095e52ad9dd495a39b64d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"接受PD-1阻断治疗的结直肠癌患者\",\"finding\":\"具核梭杆菌（Fusobacterium nucleatum）抑制抗肿瘤T细胞介导的适应性免疫；而Akkermansia muciniphila的补充可重新建立PD-1阻断的疗效。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::afc8e779e61ff2cdf0207616\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"接受PD-1抑制剂治疗的胃癌患者队列\",\"finding\":\"既往抗生素暴露（pATB）与显著降低的PFS和OS相关，客观缓解率（ORR）和疾病控制率（DCR）在非pATB组显著更高。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7b657e933f0cabb151e5b80a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::59169f7db2f838b92912b609\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"旨在澄清肠道微生物群与抗肿瘤免疫反应之间的机制关系，解释为何不同患者对免疫治疗的反应存在差异，并探讨如何利用微生物群作为预测性生物标志物和辅助治疗手段以优化癌症免疫治疗 outcomes。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d41c291461a2e726d93e8cdd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"肠道微生物群与癌症免疫治疗（特别是免疫检查点抑制剂，ICIs）疗效及免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）之间的关系。涵盖多种实体瘤（如黑色素瘤、非小细胞肺癌、结直肠癌、肝细胞癌等），涉及宿主-微生物双向互作、微生物代谢物介导的免疫调节机制以及基于微生物群的临床干预策略。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d4370aa1a51c8a09881791ed\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇综述，系统阐述了肠道微生物群如何通过复杂的生物双向相互作用调节癌症免疫和免疫治疗结果。文章首先介绍了肠道作为最大免疫器官的背景，随后详细分析了微生物群通过模式识别受体信号传导和表观遗传调控影响先天免疫（如巨噬细胞、树突状细胞）、适应性免疫（T细胞、NK细胞）及固有淋巴细胞的机制。重点讨论了短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）、肌苷、氧化三甲胺（TMAO）、色氨酸衍生物和胆汁酸等关键微生物代谢物在驱动免疫细胞分化和活性中的作用。此外，综述评估了粪菌移植（FMT）、益生菌、益生元和饮食干预等治疗策略在增强ICI疗效和管理irAEs方面的潜力与挑战，并指出了当前研究在标准化、定植效率及因果机制验证方面的局限性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fb032f53935cfbe883db5b6c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为理解肠道微生物群如何影响实体瘤免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效提供了全面的机制背景和治疗策略概览。它特别适用于回答关于微生物群调节ICI疗效的具体生物学机制（如代谢物介导的信号通路、免疫细胞亚群的重塑）以及如何利用微生物群干预（如FMT、特定菌株补充）来克服耐药性或管理副作用的问题。虽然它不报告单一的新实验数据，但它整合了多个关键临床队列和基础研究的发现，可作为构建综述中“机制”和“干预策略”章节的核心素材。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d52c609c9103892c8aaaec0c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这些关联多为观察性研究结果，存在癌症类型特异性（如黑色素瘤 vs 肺癌 vs 肠癌），且受混杂因素（如饮食、合并用药）影响，不能直接推断因果。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物群组成与实体瘤ICI疗效关联的临床证据汇总。例如，指出富集Faecalibacterium、Akkermansia muciniphila与改善PFS/OS相关，而Bacteroides富集或与较差预后相关。同时列出了抗生素暴露（pATB）与生存期缩短的关联。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0f5d7d096251017b490735bf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"部分机制主要在动物模型中证实（如小鼠FMT实验），人类临床数据的直接验证有限；某些代谢物的作用具有情境依赖性（如SCFAs在某些情况下可能抑制T细胞 trafficking）。\",\"contribution\":\"详细阐述了微生物群调节ICI疗效的具体分子和细胞机制。包括：1) SCFAs通过HDAC抑制和GPCR信号影响Treg分化和巨噬细胞功能；2) TMAO通过焦亡增强CD8+ T细胞活性；3) 色氨酸代谢物（如IAC）通过AhR/IDO1通路调节Treg/CD8+ T平衡；4) 胆汁酸通过NKT细胞积累影响肝脏肿瘤免疫；5) 微生物抗原通过DCs激活T细胞。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7844395ad2d0985d2f12fb18\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"多数干预措施处于早期临床试验阶段，缺乏大规模III期RCT证据；FMT的定植效率和长期安全性仍是主要障碍；益生菌产品的标准化和质量控制问题突出。\",\"contribution\":\"总结了基于微生物群的干预策略（FMT, 益生菌, 益生元, 饮食）在增强ICI疗效方面的临床前和早期临床研究结果。例如，FMT使部分ICI耐药黑色素瘤患者获得PR/CR；特定益生菌（如L. casei + L. reuteri）在PDAC模型中增强ICI疗效。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1e79e4b409e44183c62bb807\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"irAEs的微生物机制仍在研究中，保护性菌群的作用主要在动物模型中得到验证，人类临床应用的规范尚不明确。\",\"contribution\":\"解释了微生物群如何影响免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）。指出irAEs的发生与特定菌群失调（如Bacteroides intestinalis增加，有益菌减少）相关，并提到FMT可用于治疗难治性ICI诱导的结肠炎。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::daf05ebcac9a4ccc4ba5b7d8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"引言部分关于GI tract免疫功能的描述，以及微生物群通过循环代谢物影响全身免疫的概念。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ed2e668db070b35892b903f4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Discussion部分的“Unresolved issues and contradictory findings”。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::45517040011b84cb6fbcf265\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Translational challenges部分。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c3e678fb3ea2081e63b354fd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述涵盖多种实体瘤，但不同癌症类型中微生物群的作用可能截然不同（如Akkermansia在NSCLC/RCC中有益，但在其他癌症中不一致），使用时需注意癌症类型的特异性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d2360beb5d7ef22710f37801\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的许多机制证据来自小鼠模型，直接外推到人类需谨慎，尤其是涉及复杂的人体免疫系统和微生物群落结构时。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::50359ff5e38cdcbacfb28b5a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"临床观察性研究中的关联不等于因果，特别是对于代谢物水平与疗效的关系，可能存在反向因果或混杂因素（如饮食、药物）。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4615d5edd36a172156421c14\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"FMT和益生菌的效果在不同研究中差异巨大，部分源于产品标准化不足和患者基线状态差异，不能一概而论地认为所有微生物干预都有效。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c28946c806a4057bba9aea36\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"抗生素暴露对ICI疗效的负面影响在多队列中得到一致报道，但具体影响的微生物机制仍需进一步阐明。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b72a761761b778df736e9e8f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0433\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s273\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ff98946ce345f3fbc8f0ccdf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9cb0bfe96806bac2fcc1e5c0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::38095d2723cf3006b98ba9f7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"作为一篇理论性综述，本研究未进行新的实验数据采集，而是采用文献综合与逻辑推演的方法。首先回顾肿瘤新抗原的定义、免疫原性及在ICI治疗中的必要性；其次，分析当前预测ICI响应的临床标志物（如TMB、PD-L1表达）的局限性；接着，整合关于微生物组（特别是肠道菌群）影响ICI疗效的临床前和临床研究证据；最后，基于“分子模拟”概念，提出微生物肽段与肿瘤新抗原序列相似性的假设，并详细设计了两套研究方案（小鼠模型构建与人类临床队列生物信息学分析）以验证该假说。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4aaa25b309ffca2f07cb6edb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"系统性地提出了“微生物肿瘤新抗原模拟”作为解释微生物组调节ICI疗效的新机制框架；提供了具体的实验设计路线图（包括动物模型构建和人类临床样本的生物信息学分析指标“肿瘤抗原相似性”TAS）。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代具体的原创性实验数据来直接证实该模拟机制在人类患者中的因果效应；目前主要依赖间接证据（如抗生素/益生菌干预的结果）和理论推导；净效应（促进还是抑制免疫）尚不明确，且存在个体差异和情境依赖性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::62ec9168dbd857721493d326\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"基于现有临床前模型（如无菌小鼠、抗生素处理小鼠）和部分临床观察\",\"finding\":\"微生物组的组成和功能状态显著影响ICI的治疗效果。例如，补充特定细菌（如双歧杆菌、拟杆菌属）可增强ICI疗效，而抗生素使用则削弱疗效。粪菌移植（FMT）从 responder 患者转移到受体可恢复疗效。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2d0b9cab1bcfd2d5a6d831f7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"基于免疫学和生物信息学理论推导\",\"finding\":\"人体微生物组拥有巨大的遗传多样性，统计上极有可能存在与人类肿瘤新抗原具有相同或高度相似氨基酸序列的微生物肽段。这些微生物来源的表位可能激活交叉反应的T细胞克隆，从而间接增强抗肿瘤免疫。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::47bb8afbfa1b6138466bb146\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"基于胰腺癌长期生存者的数据引用\",\"finding\":\"在胰腺癌长期生存者中发现了针对肿瘤新抗原的T细胞克隆，这些克隆表现出对微生物表位的预测交叉反应性，支持了分子模拟在体内实际发生的观点。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c4a4cab39ade76a97f52aa7e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4947a9c714bd762ac8bdfb56\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）在许多实体瘤中取得了显著疗效，但仍有大量患者无法受益或出现耐药。除了已知的肿瘤突变负荷（TMB）和T细胞浸润等标志物外，肠道微生物组被证明能调节ICI疗效，但其具体分子机制尚不明确。本文试图回答：微生物产生的肽段是否通过模拟肿瘤新抗原来调节抗肿瘤免疫？这种模拟对ICI治疗的响应性和结果有何具体影响？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::26a10265049ec4edc7625d04\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"癌症免疫治疗（特别是免疫检查点抑制剂，ICIs）中的肿瘤新抗原及其与微生物组的关系；聚焦于肠道和肿瘤局部微生物产生的肽段对肿瘤新抗原的分子模拟现象。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::315ed5797bc100d811c58dc3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇综述文章，旨在阐述肿瘤新抗原在癌症免疫治疗中的核心作用，并重点探讨由肠道及额外肠道微生物物种通过自然基因表达程序产生的、与肿瘤新抗原相似的表位（即分子模拟）如何影响宿主抗肿瘤免疫反应。文章指出，这种微生物介导的新抗原模拟可能是解释为何部分患者对免疫检查点阻断疗法产生长期有利反应而其他患者无反应的关键机制之一。文章梳理了现有证据，提出了该假说的生物学基础，并设计了未来验证这一机制的实验策略。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::416604217849a168d4c078e0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为理解肠道微生物组如何调节免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在实体瘤中的疗效提供了重要的机制性假说——“分子模拟”。它不直接提供因果证据，但提供了连接微生物组组成与治疗响应的理论桥梁，并建议了量化这种关联的具体方法（TAS）。对于综述而言，其价值在于解释“为什么某些微生物有益”，并为后续研究如何验证这一机制提供方法论参考。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::52fe348fdea7a925c6ecc268\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这是理论假说，尚未在大规模临床试验中得到确证。净效应（是促进还是诱导耐受）尚不清楚。不能直接用于预测单个患者的具体响应，除非结合具体的TAS计算。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了微生物组调节ICI疗效的潜在机制假说：微生物肽段通过模拟肿瘤新抗原，激活交叉反应的T细胞，从而增强抗肿瘤免疫。文中指出，高微生物多样性增加模拟概率，与更好的ICI响应相关；抗生素减少多样性，降低模拟，导致疗效下降。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ebf5b60d36bc65fe74b98c5f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"序列相似性不等于免疫原性。文中承认并非所有模拟肽段都能达到足够的浓度或被呈递。HLA I类分子的丢失（LOH）可能干扰这一过程，需作为混杂因素考虑。\",\"contribution\":\"详细阐述了分子模拟的生物学基础：微生物基因组庞大，存在与人类新抗原序列相同或相似的肽段。提出了两种可能的模拟形式：完全相同的序列和仅核心区域相似的序列。还提到了微生物代谢物（如短链脂肪酸、肌苷）的辅助调节作用。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::094396a7ab8220ce967708a4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这是一种建议的研究策略，而非已完成的实证结果。需要高质量的测序数据和复杂的生物信息学流程支持。\",\"contribution\":\"提出了评估微生物-肿瘤模拟程度的具体生物信息学方法：通过全外显子组测序（WES）和RNA-seq鉴定肿瘤新抗原，通过宏基因组测序鉴定微生物抗原序列，计算“肿瘤抗原相似性”（TAS），并将TAS与临床结局关联。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2cd8117d46ec4a60724bb265\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文章强调了肿瘤新抗原是ICI起效的必要条件，并指出当前标志物（TMB, PD-L1）的局限性。同时介绍了微生物组在ICI疗效中的已知作用（抗生素负面、FMT正面）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::58cc3c80cdb229fa4d6c103a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文章提到微生物代谢物（短链脂肪酸、肌苷）也可能调节免疫，与分子模拟假说并列。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bc01aa160f430d2b4cf044d0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文章建议通过补充益生菌、增加微生物多样性或工程化改造共生菌来增强模拟效应，从而提高ICI响应率。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::82835fe9e0946c17b0f34bc7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该论文是综述而非原始研究，其提出的“分子模拟”机制目前仍属于假说阶段，缺乏直接的人类因果证据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7bf0c966467032c358c89729\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中引用的证据多为间接的（如抗生素/FMT干预结果），不能直接等同于证明了分子模拟的存在。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c4020d03213a1f5ad272386f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"“肿瘤抗原相似性”（TAS）是作者提出的概念，尚未成为临床常规检测指标。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::462e05446d3fceff7fc1f05f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"微生物组的影响具有高度的情境依赖性（如肿瘤类型、宿主免疫状态），不同研究间可能存在异质性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e71d76c4b6bc7a8bf3767be0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"HLA I类分子丢失（LOH）可能削弱或消除由模拟肽段引发的T细胞反应，这是一个重要的负面调节因素。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::941743b13cac1bbd7e0ea15f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0561\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s230\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8347d53db17c421f0cbebd65\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::336117ada34774b108edf279\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::24203a85bfdc072771ead098\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用单中心回顾性队列设计。纳入标准：确诊晚期黑色素瘤或NSCLC，接受指定TKI（达非替尼、维莫非尼、吉非替尼、阿法替尼、厄洛替尼）一线治疗。暴露定义：在TKI开始前2周至开始后6周内使用任何抗生素（ABX+组）vs. 该期间未使用抗生素（ABX-组）。主要终点：PFS和OS，依据RECIST v1.1标准评估。统计分析：首先进行单变量Cox比例风险模型分析筛选显著因素，随后构建多变量Cox模型以调整年龄、ECOG体能状态（PS）、LDH水平、脑转移等协变量，评估ABX使用的独立预后价值。探索性分析包括ABX累积使用次数及ABX与PS的交互作用。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e06f4e0000a449162427f3a7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了早期证据，表明在常规临床实践中，抗生素使用是接受TKI治疗的晚期黑色素瘤和NSCLC患者不良预后的独立预测因子。\",\"limits\":\"研究为回顾性观察性设计，无法确立因果关系；样本量较小（仅55例ABX使用者），限制了按抗生素类别细分分析的效力；未能控制感染本身对预后的潜在影响；所涵盖的TKI药物组合（如单药达非替尼/维莫非尼）已非当前晚期黑色素瘤的标准治疗（现常联合MEK抑制剂），结果的外推性受限。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ec6cf0223e6e7a02047edcc2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"全队列（n=168），多变量调整后\",\"finding\":\"抗生素使用与缩短的PFS [HR 1.71, 95% CI 1.15-2.54, P=0.008] 和 OS [HR 2.24, 95% CI 1.47-3.39, P<0.0001] 独立相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::92b8554a4f885a0a07562584\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"体能状态较差亚组（ECOG PS ≥2）\",\"finding\":\"抗生素使用对OS的负面影响尤为显著，HR高达3.82 (95% CI 1.18-12.36, P=0.025)。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ededc437b42ac178b3e63302\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"不同抗生素使用模式\",\"finding\":\"单次使用与累积多次使用抗生素相比，未显示出显著不同的有害效应差异；累积使用并未证明有“安全阈值”。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a806a9055ca026973db26dda\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d9a739d182bc58a1b3426790\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"抗生素的使用是否会影响接受酪氨酸激酶抑制剂（TKI）治疗的晚期黑色素瘤和NSCLC患者的生存结局？其影响方向及强度如何？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ec4c4cafe0181188fe78f47f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"回顾性队列研究，对象为2015年1月至2017年4月在英国The Christie NHS Foundation Trust接受一线酪氨酸激酶抑制剂（TKI）治疗的晚期黑色素瘤和非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c39e506871ab6013a37ad0b2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本研究旨在探讨抗生素（ABX）使用对接受靶向治疗（TKI）的晚期实体瘤患者疗效的影响。鉴于既往研究显示抗生素通过破坏肠道菌群可能降低免疫检查点抑制剂和化疗的疗效，但其在TKI治疗中的作用尚不明确，作者利用回顾性临床数据，比较了在使用TKI前后特定时间窗内使用抗生素与未使用抗生素患者的无进展生存期（PFS）和总生存期（OS）。研究纳入了168名可评估患者，通过多变量分析调整混杂因素后，发现抗生素使用与较短的PFS和OS独立相关，且这种负面影响在体能状态较差的患者中更为显著。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f16a9ebdf0d9feefd21414f5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文提供了抗生素干扰抗肿瘤治疗疗效的一个具体反面案例：在靶向治疗（TKI）而非免疫治疗背景下，抗生素同样与生存获益减少相关。这有助于综述论证“抗生素对多种抗癌疗法具有普遍负面影响的假设”，并提示肠道菌群失调可能不仅限于调节免疫反应，也可能通过其他机制（如炎症、代谢或药代动力学）影响靶向药物疗效。同时，它指出了现有研究中关于因果机制（感染 vs. 菌群）的不确定性。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::aeee672c4cf1dba74b44a631\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"该研究针对的是TKI，不能直接外推至所有类型的免疫治疗或新型靶向药物；且为观察性关联，非机制性解释。\",\"contribution\":\"证实了在非免疫治疗（TKI）情境下，抗生素使用依然与较差的临床结局（PFS/OS）相关，支持了抗生素广泛抑制抗癌疗效的观点。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d51f96398e0f18e8e77b25aa\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"作者明确指出未进行粪便微生物分析，因此这些机制仅为基于文献的推测和药理学合理性假设，并非本研究的实证发现。感染本身的免疫抑制效应未被排除。\",\"contribution\":\"提出了抗生素影响TKI疗效的可能机制假说，包括肠道菌群多样性丧失、全身炎症反应改变以及潜在的药代动力学相互作用（如CYP3A4酶诱导/抑制）。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a893735614a9bfd81a1677c6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"TKI治疗中ABX使用导致PFS和OS缩短的多变量分析结果，特别是HR值和时间窗定义。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e8e9cbbb736eed2d2a18b979\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"研究中关于ABX与ECOG PS交互作用的发现，以及作者承认未探索感染原因的限制。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f93b25ce515311a0a0c8e807\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"讨论部分提到的大环内酯类抗生素对CYP3A4的抑制作用可能影响TKI代谢。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::db66f853b09ab5461710be4b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该研究结论仅限于回顾性观察到的关联，不可解读为抗生素必然导致TKI失效的因果证据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1b81170d45711b784e1fc3aa\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"研究对象为2015-2017年的患者，使用的黑色素瘤治疗方案（单药BRAF抑制剂）已过时，结果可能不适用于当前的双药联合疗法（BRAF+MEK抑制剂）。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::dce1fe918e0af1515735f452\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"研究中ABX使用者的样本量较小（n=55），且未按抗生素种类进行分层分析，因此无法判断特定类别抗生素的影响差异。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::758d496721e15630dea05a21\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"未能区分抗生素使用是因为预防性措施还是治疗活动性感染，后者本身可能就是预后不良的标志。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a5281619a9dadfc2cf297edd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0012\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-edcd953058d1d5fa5081\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-eb9c2f9558e012b438e7\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"kind\":\"assets\",\"reason\":\"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\"status\":\"missing\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s124\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0070263b30459eccccb2c8c3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1fe7abb276fe0af1c83c1c10\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6d4dcfbcfa788578fcc324d1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用叙述性综述方法。作者检索并筛选了关于肠道微生物组与ICIs疗效关系的已发表文献，分为“临床前研究”和“临床研究”两部分进行归纳。在临床前部分，按免疫治疗类型（抗CTLA-4、抗PD-L1、抗PD-1）整理动物实验中的微生物干预措施（如抗生素处理、粪便移植、单菌定植）及其对肿瘤生长和免疫表型的影响。在临床研究部分，按基线微生物多样性、抗生素使用影响、免疫介导的结肠炎以及代谢特征等主题汇总人类患者数据。最后，通过对比两类研究的异同，讨论免疫调节机制、转化挑战及未来标准化需求。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2048f488b617a9941ce34256\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了截至2019年关于肠道微生物组与ICIs疗效关系的全面文献总结，建立了包含临床前和临床发现的系统分类框架。\",\"limits\":\"作为一篇叙述性综述，其结论依赖于所纳入研究的原始质量，且由于各研究间设计、人群和技术平台的差异，无法提供统一的定量效应估计。文中明确指出当前数据存在不一致性，尚未确立标准化的微生物生物标志物。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3c3b6661d01e420b1c6293d1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"临床前模型（小鼠）\",\"finding\":\"共生肠道菌群对于ICIs的抗肿瘤活性至关重要。抗生素清除或无菌环境会削弱疗效；特定细菌（如Bacteroides spp.、Akkermansia muciniphila、Bifidobacterium spp.）的补充可恢复或增强对PD-1/PD-L1/CTLA-4阻断的反应，涉及增加CD8+ T细胞浸润、促进树突状细胞成熟及诱导Th1型免疫反应。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::dbc0101da3ccadc1272bcb82\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"临床研究（黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC等）\",\"finding\":\"响应者通常表现出更高的肠道微生物α多样性，且富集特定菌属（如Faecalibacterium、Clostridiales目、Ruminococcaceae科、Akkermansia muciniphila）。相反，非响应者中Bacteroidales目、Escherichia coli等丰度较高。抗生素使用在某些研究中与较差的PFS/OS相关，但在其他研究中无显著影响，显示结果不一致。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8c928549ce5370fc33a0db5b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"机制探讨\",\"finding\":\"微生物可能通过抗原模拟、提供共刺激信号或直接代谢产物影响免疫系统。具体机制包括增强DCs的抗原呈递能力、促进记忆T细胞从淋巴结向肿瘤微环境（TME）迁移、减少调节性T细胞（Tregs）和髓系衍生抑制细胞（MDSCs）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::92d8a6983e5f875ef67f29cb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::df3118577f22ec33a98f4663\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管肠道微生物组被认为可能影响免疫检查点抑制剂的疗效，但目前的临床前和临床研究结果存在不一致性，且其作为预测性生物标志物的临床效用尚不明确。本研究旨在解决如何整合现有证据以理解微生物组的作用，并识别阻碍其转化为可靠生物标志物的关键障碍。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a2a62233a277d1362a8ccff8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"该综述聚焦于肠道微生物组（gut microbiome）与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs，包括PD-1、PD-L1和CTLA-4抑制剂）抗肿瘤疗效之间的关系。研究范围涵盖了临床前（小鼠模型）和临床研究两个层面，旨在梳理现有的证据基础、潜在的免疫调节机制以及当前研究中存在的不一致性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::63945f6ef57088b1a632725a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇系统性综述，旨在评估肠道微生物组作为预测免疫检查点抑制剂疗效生物标志物的潜力。作者综合了已发表的临床前研究和临床研究结果，详细列举了与ICIs疗效正相关或负相关的特定细菌物种及分类群。文章不仅总结了微生物组影响抗肿瘤免疫反应的潜在机制（如树突状细胞成熟、T细胞浸润等），还深入探讨了临床前与临床研究之间发现的不一致性问题，分析了导致这些差异的可能原因（如宿主-微生物生态系统的复杂性、采样与分析方法的标准化不足等），并提出了未来建立可靠生物标志物所需的研究方向和方法学改进建议。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2c7a048c4a0b6dc1bd6bdbe2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为构建“肠道微生物组如何调节实体瘤中ICIs疗效”的综述提供了核心的背景框架和机制假设库。它系统地列出了被报道与疗效相关或无关的具体微生物分类群（Facet F1的关键素材），并详细阐述了作者提出的免疫调节机制路径（Facet F2的核心解释）。此外，它对临床前与临床数据不一致性的分析，为讨论研究异质性和方法学局限提供了重要的论述素材。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e3d16a2075982ff7167de376\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这些关联主要基于观察性研究和小型队列，因果关系未完全确立。不同研究间的定义标准（如OTU聚类算法）不同，直接比较丰度数值需谨慎。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了具体的微生物-疗效关联列表：正面关联包括Akkermansia muciniphila, Bifidobacterium spp., Faecalibacterium genus, Ruminococcaceae family, Clostridiales order等；负面关联包括Bacteroidales order (含Bacteroides spp.), Escherichia coli, Roseburia intestinalis等。同时指出了不同研究中结果的矛盾之处（如Bacteroidetes在某些研究中与响应相关，在其他中与不响应相关）。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d3542d1a49feb8f802f06372\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"许多机制细节来自小鼠模型（如B. fragilis诱导Th1反应），在人体中的直接验证有限。综述指出具体细菌种类与特定免疫通路的精确对应关系仍不完全清楚，需警惕将动物模型机制直接外推至人类。\",\"contribution\":\"阐述了微生物影响ICIs疗效的潜在生物学机制：1) 增强树突状细胞（DCs）成熟和抗原呈递；2) 促进CD4+和CD8+ T细胞（特别是记忆T细胞和效应T细胞）向肿瘤微环境的募集和活化；3) 调节Treg和MDSC的比例；4) 通过代谢产物（如短链脂肪酸等，虽提及但未详述具体分子）影响免疫状态。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::17da5e4bc3b5aa34f96ea596\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"综述讨论了采样方法（粪便vs盲肠内容物）、测序技术（16S rRNA vs 宏基因组鸟枪法）、数据分析流程以及混杂因素（饮食、抗生素、地理位置）对结果一致性的影响。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ab7cd056b8a8f9e73a8a6530\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"提到了正在进行的临床试验（Table 3），涉及粪便微生物移植（FMT）、益生菌/益生元联合治疗等策略。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c56379e4e6e58b401d0143eb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"讨论了肠道微生物组与免疫介导的结肠炎（immune-mediated colitis）的关系，如Firmicutes门富集与ipilimumab诱导的结肠炎风险增加相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9f5db9130e896bccddcbe99a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述发表于2019年，后续可能有大量新研究出现，需注意时效性限制。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::30a8980c13b3672ea88d08e4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"综述中引用的临床前和临床研究之间存在明显的异质性，不能简单地将所有阳性结果合并为一个统一的“有益微生物”列表，必须保留其情境依赖性（如肿瘤类型、ICI药物类型）。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bb2e061a8745a6ec51f716ef\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"对于“抗生素使用”的影响，综述本身也指出了相互矛盾的证据，因此在引用时应明确区分不同研究的结论，避免一概而论。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d7d25ce2adf86513b9ea7b91\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"机制描述多基于作者对现有文献的综合推断，部分机制（如特定细菌与特定T细胞亚群的直接因果联系）在人类中尚待更严格的实验验证。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b50e56c3bbd31c7a7385298e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0171\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-57c86dec56d8ae37b5be\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-cf2fc9e893310420ac34\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"kind\":\"assets\",\"reason\":\"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\"status\":\"missing\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s054\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7d353bc4bd873e32582c670f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::09b4e0a1ba12760e2fb8442f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::87fbbb61dc2c0edaa5061341\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"作为一篇综述，本文采用主题综合的方法，而非系统性的文献检索流程。作者选取了五个具有代表性的研究领域（癌症免疫治疗、食品乳化剂、IBD患者队列、可溶性纤维补充、人群血糖反应），分别阐述其中微生物群如何影响干预效果。通过对比不同研究中关于特定细菌与临床结局关联的异质性，以及展示微生物群介导的饮食效应（如乳化剂诱导的炎症、纤维诱导的肝癌或缓解结肠炎），构建“抗性/易感”概念框架，进而评估个性化干预的现状与前景。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6e9e45e9a3ffa6a4e686f161\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提出了“抗性”与“易感”微生物群的概念框架，强调个体间微生物群差异是解释饮食和药物干预结果异质性的关键因素。\",\"limits\":\"文章未提供新的实验数据，而是对现有文献的综合评述；对于如何标准化定义“抗性”和“易感”状态，以及具体的临床实施路径，尚缺乏统一标准。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::14cff54e09e9534717ce9940\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"指出了当前微生物群研究在方法学上的局限，如测序平台和分析工作流的不统一，以及物种水平分析的不足，呼吁向宏基因组和宏转录组层面发展。\",\"limits\":\"未能详细比较不同测序技术的具体优劣，也未提供具体的技术操作指南。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::db7920471cda288170f1db00\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"强调了非微生物因素（如性别、遗传、昼夜节律）对微生物群及干预效果的潜在影响，为未来研究提供了多维度的视角。\",\"limits\":\"对这些因素如何具体交互作用的机制探讨较为简略，主要作为未来研究方向提出。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::de133c33149b49c1c784eb79\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"癌症免疫治疗（抗PD-1疗法）\",\"finding\":\"肠道微生物群组成可预测免疫检查点抑制剂的疗效；响应者中Faecalibacterium属丰度较高，非响应者中Bacteroidales目丰度较高；Akkermansia muciniphila的丰度与临床反应相关，且补充该菌可恢复小鼠模型中的治疗 efficacy。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cf7780ad4ecf33898bebec6b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"饮食乳化剂（CMC和P80）摄入\",\"finding\":\"乳化剂改变微生物群组成，促进微生物侵入粘液层，引发低度肠道炎症和代谢紊乱；这种有害效应依赖于复杂的微生物群，且在缺乏微生物群的无菌小鼠中不出现。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f9f1ee51c96cee6ae31e3533\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"麦芽糊精摄入与克罗恩病（CD）\",\"finding\":\"麦芽糊精增强CD相关粘附侵袭性大肠杆菌（AIEC）的生物膜形成；由于仅30%-40%的CD患者携带AIEC，针对全人群的无麦芽糊精饮食试验可能因混杂了AIEC阴性个体而显示无效，但在AIEC阳性亚组中可能有效。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a28cf92576eebd223952fef6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"可溶性纤维（菊粉）补充\",\"finding\":\"在野生型小鼠中有益，但在IL10KO基因易感小鼠中加剧结肠炎；在雄性小鼠中导致肝细胞癌（HCC），且该效应由微生物群介导，可通过抑制微生物发酵预防。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2660117baf2722ea13854afd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"餐后血糖反应（人群研究）\",\"finding\":\"相同饮食引起的餐后血糖反应存在高度个体差异；整合微生物群组成的机器学习算法能准确预测个体的血糖反应，支持基于微生物群的个性化饮食推荐。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fc9ea9de3c5e6fed92bf1f31\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d98313016ef4abf0fb2ba063\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"在慢性炎症性疾病管理中，基于肠道微生物群组成的个性化饮食干预是否已经成熟到可以应用于临床？其科学依据、现有证据及面临的障碍是什么？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::775e297de80479c8f6a3e278\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"慢性炎症性疾病（包括炎症性肠病、结直肠癌、代谢综合征等）与肠道微生物群之间的相互作用，重点探讨基于微生物群组成的个性化饮食干预的可行性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e9df2c6b2f020f9468f10f72\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇综述，旨在回答“我们是否准备好使用基于肠道微生物群组成的个性化饮食干预来治疗慢性炎症性疾病？”这一问题。文章首先概述了非遗传因素（如饮食成分）对肠道微生物群及宿主炎症的影响，随后通过癌症免疫治疗、乳化剂研究、患者队列研究、可溶性纤维研究以及人群基础研究的案例，论证了个体间微生物群差异对干预结果的决定性作用。作者指出，尽管目前已有证据表明微生物群可以预测药物疗效和饮食反应，但由于细菌物种关联的不一致性、检测方法的局限性以及机制的复杂性，完全个性化的临床实施仍面临挑战。文章建议将粪便采样纳入常规临床试验，并探索更精细的微生物分析手段以识别“抗性”和“易感”个体。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c7bddf823cab2a6f36aeec5f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为“肠道微生物群如何调节实体瘤免疫检查点抑制剂疗效及其机制”这一主题提供了重要的背景支持和类比证据。虽然其主要焦点是饮食干预，但其中关于癌症免疫治疗的部分直接涉及ICIs疗效与微生物群的关联，可作为F1和F2问题的背景材料。此外，文中提出的“抗性/易感”概念、微生物群介导的药物代谢机制、以及不同细菌物种在预测治疗反应中的作用，有助于理解ICIs疗效异质性的潜在原因。同时，文中指出的方法学挑战（如测序不一致、物种关联差异）也为讨论机制研究的可靠性提供了反面教材或注意事项。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7239e636c35d0ccf8dfdf308\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这些发现来自黑色素瘤研究，且不同研究间存在细菌物种关联的不一致性，需谨慎外推至其他实体瘤类型。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了癌症免疫治疗中微生物群预测疗效的直接证据：Gopalakrishnan等发现响应者富集Faecalibacterium，非响应者富集Bacteroidales；Routy等发现Akkermansia muciniphila与响应相关，且补充该菌可恢复疗效。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2603601f994fa56e8980351a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"文章未深入阐述具体的分子机制，仅指出微生物群的中心作用，具体通路需参考其他专门研究机制的论文。\",\"contribution\":\"提示了微生物群可能通过影响宿主免疫状态或药物代谢来调节疗效的机制线索：例如Akkermiasia muciniphila的补充恢复了PD-1阻断的疗效，暗示微生物群可能通过调节局部或全身免疫环境发挥作用。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7433488fa448a7e804425140\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这是从饮食干预研究中推导出的方法论建议，并非直接针对ICIs试验的设计规范。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了关于临床试验设计的重要启示：由于个体间微生物群差异巨大，基于群体的平均结果可能掩盖亚组的显著疗效，因此需要考虑基于微生物群的 stratification。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7bf6b8989f1a421ea3102de3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这属于对领域现状的评论，而非具体的机制发现。\",\"contribution\":\"指出了当前机制研究的局限性：不同研究报道的与疗效相关的细菌物种存在差异，这可能反映了技术平台、分析流程或患者人群异质性的影响，而非单一的因果机制。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fbaa0ef7abb83c3ce43bb95b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文章开篇总结了肠道微生物群在慢性炎症性疾病中的角色，以及饮食作为核心影响因素的背景。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0b547d2fdf7e2a50155284e3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"提出了“抗性”与“易感”微生物群的概念，并图示说明不同个体对同一干预（如乳化剂、膳食纤维）的不同反应。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c93c2f2f360978f7c92c35be\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文章指出目前大多数研究依赖16S rRNA测序，可能不足以准确预测反应，需要宏基因组或宏转录组分析，甚至菌株水平的鉴定。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5bd50b5bc6be59c5dd2ec247\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"提到了FMT在复发性艰难梭菌感染中的成功应用，以及在IBD中的探索性应用。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f699ad0c5b4c2d633ece8cd7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"本文主要聚焦于饮食干预，其对ICIs疗效的讨论主要集中在癌症免疫治疗领域，且多为观察性关联，需谨慎推断因果关系。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3690087e9bf834aa5c74a070\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文章中提到的细菌物种（如Faecalibacterium, Akkermiasia）在不同研究中的关联可能存在冲突，不能简单视为普适性标志物。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f4f82da340149475a0e7b6fc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文章未提供具体的ICIs临床试验数据，其关于个性化干预的建议是基于逻辑推导和跨领域类比，而非直接的ICIs证据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6d9c0219637b872c2715ad88\",\"source_handle\":\"P0375\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s115\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9ec8d6abd7d45ecb2afdff8e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"abstract\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c0469283aef12ec7b089ec63\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::22c2a86826ff5178286311d1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"Retrospective cohort study. Patients receiving ICIs for advanced/metastatic disease between Jan 2018 and Dec 2023 were grouped based on infusion timing relative to the median time of all treatments ('early group': <50% cycles after median time; 'late group': ≥50%). Primary endpoint was OS. Multivariable-adjusted Hazard Ratios (HRs) were estimated using standard Cox models and time-dependent Cox models to account for potential changes in group assignment over time. Sensitivity analyses were performed.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3411659c8a5c411b2e7aba87\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Provides evidence from a large sample size suggesting a benefit in OS with early ICI administration, utilizing time-dependent Cox models to reduce immortal time bias.\",\"limits\":\"Retrospective design limits causal inference; results may be specific to the single-centre setting; no difference found when chemotherapy is included; sensitivity analysis results varied by model type.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::86be55c0fd1c481f08135111\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Overall cohort (n=2631)\",\"finding\":\"Median OS was significantly shorter in the late group (13.1 months) compared to the early group (21.4 months). Time-dependent Cox model showed HR 1.30 (95% CI 1.16-1.44) for death in the late group.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1c462fad1719cdc8697afb2a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Regimens with ICIs alone (n=1886) or ICIs plus tyrosine kinase inhibitors (n=163)\",\"finding\":\"The association between later administration and shorter OS remained significant.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::83d0fdb0fb696690c582b8f6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Regimens comprising chemotherapy (n=582)\",\"finding\":\"No significant difference in OS was observed between early and late groups.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7c00aacbe807f3ae64142343\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Sensitivity analysis based on exposure at 3 months\",\"finding\":\"Standard model showed no difference (HR 1.09, 95% CI 0.98-1.20); time-dependent model showed higher risk of death for late group (HR 1.14, 95% CI 1.02-1.26).\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b0fc8533710744ce6605ea36\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3deb489d5cb67e2529f53c32\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"To determine if the time of day of ICI infusion affects treatment response and overall survival in patients with advanced solid tumours, addressing limitations of previous small-scale studies with methodological biases.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b9f8df840eb553c32c248e70\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"Advanced solid tumours (lung cancer, melanoma, renal carcinoma, head and neck, urothelial cancer) treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) at a large tertiary cancer centre; retrospective cohort analysis.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8f8d3bef8a6d1205a4fe9cb4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"This study investigates whether the timing of ICI administration influences overall survival (OS), based on evidence of circadian dependence in the immune system. Using a large single-centre cohort of 2631 patients, the authors compared outcomes between 'early' and 'late' treatment groups, defined by whether ≥50% of cycles were administered after the median infusion time. The analysis employed Cox models with and without time-dependent variables to mitigate immortal time bias, adjusting for age, sex, ECOG status, cancer type, and treatment regimen.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1237dc0b4d752de2f02409ef\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"This paper offers observational data linking ICI administration timing to survival outcomes in solid tumours, specifically highlighting a potential circadian effect. It provides quantitative evidence (HRs, OS differences) that can serve as a comparative baseline or contextual factor when evaluating the gut microbiome's role in ICI efficacy, particularly regarding non-microbial factors influencing treatment response timing or variability.\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1270b9c8a5eee9f889b793cf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Does not address microbiome mechanisms directly. Results are associative, not causal. The lack of effect in chemo-combined regimens suggests interaction with other drug classes, which complicates direct comparison to microbiome studies that might focus on different regimen types.\",\"contribution\":\"Provides observational data on how non-microbial factors (administration timing) correlate with ICI efficacy in solid tumours. Specifically, it shows that earlier administration is associated with better OS in ICI-only and ICI+TKI regimens, but not in chemo-combined regimens.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8f7c3d6374184de4f9ebc6fc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"The mechanism is proposed based on general immune system circadian dependence, not specifically linked to gut microbiota in this study. It does not provide evidence for microbiome-mediated mechanisms.\",\"contribution\":\"Offers a mechanistic hypothesis (circadian dependence of the immune system) as an alternative or complementary explanation for ICI efficacy variation.\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::264c6709cc910d12ebd5a8dc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Findings on the impact of infusion timing on OS across different cancer types and regimen combinations.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1c2fc03bd228d69f90700d6f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Use of time-dependent Cox models to address immortal time bias.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::efb551cb64f4a996542cfcde\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The study is retrospective and single-centre, limiting generalizability.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cc9ac9200723c62e3332eec1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Associations do not imply causation; unmeasured confounders may exist.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a65a67c7fc1223583e7be583\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The 'early' vs 'late' grouping is based on median infusion time, which may not reflect optimal biological timing.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d76e4eb2c50a15b19045343c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Results differ by regimen type (chemo vs non-chemo), so findings cannot be universally applied to all ICI treatments.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::09bde12acd20d48d0d686ba1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Sensitivity analysis yielded mixed results depending on the statistical model used.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::82ade6aaf80d65c3443ed8a5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0558\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"identity\",\"reason\":\"source identity was not independently verified\",\"status\":\"input_attributed\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"no complete research body was indexed\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\"status\":\"partial\"}],\"material_scope\":\"abstract_only\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s042\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5dfa2f6307bf1552e1a399f9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cbf91a989264a5e9ed236597\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4aee8f5e401934d0c175afb0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用叙述性综述方法，整合来自临床前模型（小鼠模型、类器官）和人类患者队列的研究数据。文章按主题组织：1) 微生物在癌症发生中的作用；2) 微生物调节抗癌药物（化疗、ICI）疗效的机制；3) 微生物生物标志物用于预测疗效；4) 通过干预手段（抗生素、益生菌、FMT、噬菌体、纳米技术）调控微生物群的方法；5) 当前研究的局限性与未来展望。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::95bca79832feaf98a134a7b2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物群调节癌症治疗（特别是ICI和化疗）机制的综合框架，包括代谢降解、免疫调节和生态变化（TIMER框架）。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代具体的文献检索策略和筛选标准；作为综述，其结论依赖于引用的原始研究，且许多机制主要基于小鼠模型，存在向人类外推的不确定性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::193438df5e5ac33fd79baef2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"总结了多种微生物调控策略（益生菌、FMT、噬菌体、纳米技术）的临床前和早期临床证据。\",\"limits\":\"指出目前缺乏大规模多中心临床试验验证微生物疗法的长期安全性和有效性；部分临床结果存在冲突（如益生菌试验），归因于个体差异和研究设计局限。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e82b793a7ce02d60b98b6908\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"化疗药物（吉西他滨、环磷酰胺、5-FU等）\",\"finding\":\"特定细菌可代谢药物使其失活（如Gammaproteobacteria代谢吉西他滨导致胰腺癌耐药）；某些共生菌（如Enterococcus hirae, Barnesiella intestinihominis）通过刺激Th17细胞或γδT细胞浸润增强环磷酰胺疗效；具核梭杆菌通过TLR4/MYD88通路激活自噬促进5-FU耐药。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::48d9aafeca596013be0f3518\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"免疫检查点抑制剂（CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1）\",\"finding\":\"Bacteroides fragilis和Bacteroides thetaiotaomicron通过诱导淋巴结Th1反应和树突状细胞成熟增强抗CTLA-4疗效；Akkermansia muciniphila富集与非小细胞肺癌和肾细胞癌中对PD-1阻断剂的响应相关；黑色素瘤患者中Faecalibacterium和Ruminococcaceae富集与生存期延长相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::dec77698dba2619f48ff3701\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"肿瘤发生与进展\",\"finding\":\"幽门螺杆菌通过β-catenin信号通路促进胃癌；具核梭杆菌通过FadA粘附素结合E-cadherin激活Wnt/NF-kB通路促进结直肠癌；Peptostreptococcus anaerobius通过PI3K-Akt通路促进增殖和炎症。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9511e05d6896aa7fa29e9b9c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"治疗毒性管理\",\"finding\":\"FMT可缓解ICI引起的结肠炎和放疗引起的肠道毒性；Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG通过释放脂磷壁酸（LTA）保护上皮干细胞免受辐射损伤。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::599db5fe66f0c6df0c804397\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bd18c6ef74b443a822a4424f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管已有大量关于肠道微生物群影响癌症治疗的证据，但需要综合理解微生物与癌症治疗的具体交互机制，以便识别新的预防策略、对患者进行分层以提高治疗效果并减少并发症。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::27c44bf3d7caa7f1d1f260de\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"肠道微生物群在癌症治疗中的作用，涵盖化疗药物、免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）及放疗的疗效调节、肿瘤发生机制、微生物生物标志物、治疗相关毒性的管理以及通过益生菌、粪菌移植（FMT）、噬菌体和纳米技术进行微生物调控的策略。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3342e506c85d5bbfddf3ee03\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇综述，系统梳理了肠道微生物群与癌症治疗之间的相互作用。文章首先阐述了微生物群失调如何促进肿瘤发生（如幽门螺杆菌、具核梭杆菌等），随后重点讨论了不同细菌物种如何通过代谢药物、调节免疫反应或诱导耐药性来影响化疗和免疫治疗的疗效。此外，综述还评估了利用微生物特征作为诊断/预后标志物的潜力，探讨了通过抗生素、益生菌、FMT和新型纳米技术/噬菌体疗法调控微生物群以增强疗效或减轻毒性的策略，并指出了当前研究在因果机制验证、动物模型外推性及临床转化方面的局限性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e34b9cc7bb31799111285bd1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为理解肠道微生物群如何具体影响固体肿瘤对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）和化疗的反应提供了详细的机制背景和潜在的生物标志物列表。它特别有助于回答“哪些细菌物种增强或削弱ICI疗效”以及“背后的免疫和代谢机制是什么”这两个子问题。同时，它提供了关于微生物调控策略（如FMT、益生菌）在改善治疗耐受性和疗效方面的现状评估，可用于讨论临床转化的挑战和前景。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d68f1d7be2df847cbd65c8ef\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"相关性不等于因果性；不同研究使用的测序方法（16S vs metagenomics）、样本类型（粪便vs组织）和癌症类型可能导致结果偏差；部分发现仅在小鼠模型中验证，人类数据有限。\",\"contribution\":\"列举了与ICI疗效正相关和负相关的特定细菌物种。例如，Bacteroides fragilis、Bacteroides thetaiotaomicron、Akkermansia muciniphila、Faecalibacterium prausnitzii、Ruminococcaceae被报道与ICI响应相关；而某些未明确命名的菌群或缺乏有益菌的状态与无响应相关。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7de397c7634b39d8bdffe607\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"许多机制细节（如Akkermansia的具体通路）主要基于小鼠模型或体外实验，人类体内的确切机制仍需更多验证；不同细菌的作用可能相互交织，难以孤立分析单一机制。\",\"contribution\":\"详细描述了微生物调节ICI疗效的机制：1) Bacteroides species诱导淋巴结Th1反应和肿瘤内树突状细胞成熟；2) Akkermansia muciniphila通过IL-12途径促进CCR9+CXCR3+CD4+ T淋巴细胞募集到肿瘤微环境；3) 微生物通过TLR4激活髓系细胞产生TNF等炎症因子，增强免疫监视；4) 微生物代谢产物（如短链脂肪酸SCFAs）可能增强CD8+ T细胞的记忆潜能。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::54bb4fdad7705305ec54b250\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"本题目聚焦ICI，化疗机制可作为背景参考，但不直接回答ICI的特异性机制。\",\"contribution\":\"指出微生物群也影响化疗疗效，如Gammaproteobacteria代谢吉西他滨导致耐药，而某些细菌增强环磷酰胺疗效。这为理解广义的“抗癌治疗”提供了背景。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::556dc29681cb461be8b36faa\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"综述讨论了FMT、益生菌、噬菌体和纳米技术在癌症治疗中的应用潜力及局限性。例如，FMT在缓解ICI结肠炎和放疗毒性中的初步证据，但样本量小、缺乏机制洞察；益生菌临床试验结果不一致，受个体微生物组和宿主基因组影响大；噬菌体和纳米技术尚处于早期阶段。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c0a4b24151e52eb58609dc77\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"提到F. nucleatum在CRC中的诊断价值（结合FIT提高性能），以及与MSI状态、肿瘤位置、预后的关联。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::984b10a4e42684438bc48144\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"指出小鼠模型与人类生理的差异、抗生素使用的混杂效应、饮食和环境因素的影响、以及病毒组和真菌组的潜在作用。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::91ee4199ed9203bb31c2a3e6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述是2020年发表的，后续可能有新的重大发现，使用时需注意时效性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::054563d2038db64bf6dbf5f8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的许多机制主要基于小鼠模型（germ-free mice, antibiotic-treated mice），在向人类推广时需格外谨慎，因为小鼠和人类的肠道微生物组成及生理存在显著差异。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::189ee075d443a0a8a4076fde\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"对于益生菌和FMT的效果，文中明确指出临床证据有限且存在冲突，不应将其视为已确立的标准疗法。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::788bf004ee45cd5fa0bb13bd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"不同癌症类型（如CRC vs Melanoma vs NSCLC）中微生物的作用可能截然不同，需区分对待，避免过度泛化。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9e22ec4c8c30ff5945d7ac5d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0229\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-30c4d9a86f8c4e63ba33\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-2d4faf2da7bc361a24e6\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"kind\":\"assets\",\"reason\":\"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\"status\":\"missing\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s143\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::da470854082ae3519201c93a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"abstract\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0e392f2741b0f93bae38bcf7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::eef080ffa6526d7f034bb32e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"The study employs a computational modeling approach. It constructs a dynamic model of tumor-immune-gut microbiome interactions. The parameters for gut bacteria dynamics were fitted to clinical data from melanoma patients. Virtual patient data were generated based on clinical survival data. Simulations were then run to analyze the impact of initial bacterial levels and growth rates on therapeutic outcomes, comparing scenarios with manipulated vs. natural bacterial compositions.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::05116375370aabb6ca40490a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Provides a theoretical model linking gut microbiome dynamics to ICI efficacy, offering mechanistic insights into interpatient heterogeneity.\",\"limits\":\"The findings are derived from simulations and model fitting, not direct experimental validation. The specific mechanisms of interaction are inferred through the model rather than empirically proven. The generalizability beyond melanoma or specific model assumptions is not established in this abstract.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::812a29729d0569843ec91062\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"At the initiation of anti-PD-1 therapy\",\"finding\":\"Low initial growth rate and low level of favorable bacteria predict non-responders, while a high level of favorable bacteria predicts responders.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9f9dc46c0fca85bc8c805b82\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Through simulation of bacterial manipulation\",\"finding\":\"It is possible to promote the response rate to anti-PD-1 by manipulating the gut bacteria composition of non-responders, potentially achieving long-term progression-free survival.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::180cd9e0445370625d26cf5c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"theory\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5b574c8eff2c26db3363b047\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"The research investigates why only a subset of patients shows durable clinical responses to ICIs despite their high success in some solid metastatic malignancies. Specifically, it seeks to understand the underlying mechanisms by which favorable and unfavorable gut bacteria modulate anti-PD-1 efficacy and to identify predictive markers for treatment response.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bc2761f49854f8882dead30a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"The study focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome and the efficacy of anti-PD-1 immune checkpoint inhibitors in cancer treatment, specifically using melanoma patient data as a reference for model calibration. The scope is limited to theoretical modeling and simulation rather than clinical trials or wet-lab experiments.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::013530ac89b265b4772bb2e9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"This paper addresses the heterogeneity in patient responses to immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) by exploring how the gut microbiome influences therapeutic outcomes. The authors developed a mathematical model to simulate tumor-immune-gut microbiome interactions. They fitted the dynamics of gut bacteria to clinical data from melanoma patients and generated virtual patient datasets based on survival statistics. The study aimed to identify predictive markers for responders versus non-responders and to evaluate whether manipulating gut bacterial composition could improve response rates. The work provides a computational framework to understand mechanisms that are not fully explained by empirical studies alone.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::17191bc2054009614ecc02ea\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"This paper offers a computational perspective on how gut microbiome composition influences the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors. It provides specific predictive markers (initial bacterial levels and growth rates) derived from modeling, suggesting that microbial modulation can theoretically enhance treatment response. This is valuable for discussing mechanistic hypotheses and predictive biomarkers in the context of microbiome-IICI interactions.\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::be73708f468266ddc0678883\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"These are model-derived predictions fitted to clinical data, not independent prospective validations. The causal link is theoretical within the model structure.\",\"contribution\":\"Identifies specific microbial characteristics (low/high levels of favorable bacteria, growth rates) as predictive markers for anti-PD-1 response in melanoma patients via modeling.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::91197f30babbd6c32cdd1a19\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"The mechanism is simulated; actual biological pathways are not detailed. The claim of achieving long-term progression-free survival is a simulation result, not a clinical observation.\",\"contribution\":\"Proposes a mechanism where the initial state of favorable bacteria determines therapeutic outcome, and suggests that modifying this state can shift non-responders to responders.\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6a8a6a7123af68e7f4e79f93\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"The use of melanoma patient data to calibrate the model and the focus on anti-PD-1 therapy.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d39d3c28cec61e16914b5346\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The results are based on a theoretical model fitted to clinical data, not direct experimental evidence of causality.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b5593bd6e42114fbf96bf247\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The specific findings regarding predictive markers are derived from simulation outputs and may depend on model assumptions.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7245caff3982eb86a32b47d5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The generalizability to other types of solid tumors or different ICI classes is not addressed in the abstract.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::decc20b4febb01d740031b54\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Claims about improving response rates through bacterial manipulation are hypothetical based on simulation, not confirmed clinical outcomes.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::77d026a6cc947cee8b070bee\",\"source_handle\":\"P0525\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"identity\",\"reason\":\"source identity was not independently verified\",\"status\":\"input_attributed\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"no complete research body was indexed\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"html\",\"reason\":\"html_empty\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\"status\":\"partial\"}],\"material_scope\":\"abstract_only\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s205\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ed84bfa0d924f906dce32dbc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::eefefea07d6878b3752fb470\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ed99ee349cf7e2108d0c9964\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用纵向队列设计，纳入HIV感染者和健康对照者。在基线（ART前）、治疗后6个月和治疗后12个月三个时间点收集样本。使用全基因组宏基因组测序技术获取微生物数据，结合生物信息学分析方法解析微生物群落结构（分类学组成）并推断其功能（代谢通路）。通过组间比较和时间序列分析来评估ART干预下的动态变化。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::546dc499ea44116be66a96fd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了HIV感染者在接受ART治疗前后肠道微生物组和代谢通路变化的纵向数据，证实了ART仅能部分恢复微生物失调。\",\"limits\":\"所给材料未交代具体的统计显著性水平、样本量大小、HIV感染者的临床分期/CD4计数等混杂因素控制情况，也未明确说明是否建立了严格的因果关系证据链。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3d287971f46755b7b6042a2b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"ART治疗前 vs HIV阴性对照\",\"finding\":\"HIV感染者表现出显著的肠道微生物失调，特征为促炎微生物的富集以及拟杆菌门（Bacteroidetes）比例的降低。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6147fe50b1a75a1346e5d56b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"ART治疗后6-12个月\",\"finding\":\"随着ART治疗的进行，变形菌门（Proteobacteria）的比例下降并持续至12个月；拟杆菌门比例先升后降。整体失调未完全逆转。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d80efe1c4773c92faac2b3a1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"代谢通路分析\",\"finding\":\"丙酮酸发酵至异丁醇的代谢通路改变在HIV感染者中持续存在，即使经过12个月的ART治疗仍未恢复。该机制的改变与Ruminococcus bromii物种丰度的降低呈相关性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b3c67d6d0fbaa64a990f0530\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::28ae9179302c3f88f8763f49\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"核心问题是：肠道微生物组的失调是否与HIV疾病进程有因果联系，还是仅仅反映了宿主免疫和代谢系统受疾病影响后的继发改变？同时探究ART治疗对这种失调及代谢通路的影响。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9ca0638881caa3424c4c5fb2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"研究对象为HIV感染者（PL-HIV）与健康对照者；研究情境涵盖ART治疗前、治疗后6个月及12个月的时间点；范围聚焦于肠道微生物群落的组成变化及其衍生的代谢通路动态。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1beed5cbe59f1132e3562305\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本研究旨在探讨肠道微生物组在HIV感染及抗逆转录病毒治疗（ART）过程中的作用，特别是区分微生物失调是疾病的原因还是结果。通过全基因组测序和生物信息学分析，比较了HIV阴性人群与接受ART治疗的HIV感染者在治疗前、后6个月及12个月的肠道微生物组成和代谢通路。研究发现，HIV感染者存在显著的微生物失调，表现为促炎微生物富集和特定菌门比例改变。ART治疗虽能部分改善这种失调，但无法完全恢复，且持续影响某些关键代谢通路（如丙酮酸发酵至异丁醇途径），这与Ruminococcus bromii物种的减少相关。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::26f6a19146e4cc66a62c2f5d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文提供了HIV感染背景下肠道微生物组失调的具体表型特征（如促炎菌富集、特定菌门波动）及其代谢后果（异丁醇通路异常）。虽然研究对象是HIV而非实体瘤，但其揭示的“病原体诱导的代谢通路改变”及“ART治疗无法完全修复的代谢缺陷”机制，可作为理解其他慢性炎症或免疫调节状态下微生物-宿主互作的类比素材，特别是关于微生物代谢产物如何可能间接影响宿主免疫环境的讨论。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fa45074ac801c19969563333\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"不能直接回答ICI在实体瘤中的疗效问题。HIV与实体瘤的免疫微环境差异巨大，此处的微生物变化不直接等同于ICI响应相关的微生物标志物。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了慢性病毒感染（HIV）状态下肠道微生物组失调的典型特征，包括特定的菌群失衡（如拟杆菌门减少、变形菌门变化）和代谢通路的持续性异常。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b2e7ffae968b86f2dadae989\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"所给材料未详细阐述该代谢通路具体如何影响免疫系统或肿瘤微环境。不能将此机制直接外推至ICI疗效机制，除非有额外的文献支持HIV模型与ICI模型在该代谢路径上的同源性。\",\"contribution\":\"揭示了微生物代谢通路（异丁醇途径）与特定菌种（R. bromii）之间的关联，暗示了微生物代谢活动可能是介导宿主生理状态改变的重要机制。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d273cae802639736e13992c1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"论文展示了如何使用全基因组测序和生物信息学分析来追踪微生物组随时间（治疗前后）的动态变化，以及将分类学变化与功能代谢通路联系起来的方法。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5c69ca328d17163eb93f2c01\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"指出ART治疗虽有益但会导致持续的代谢通路改变和部分失调，提示药物治疗可能存在长期的微生物副作用。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::eabdcfe14d06e442a537ec12\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"严格区分HIV感染模型与实体瘤/ICI模型的生物学差异，不可直接将HIV相关的微生物标志物视为ICI疗效预测因子。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d9fc3ff47c5be409e71db45e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"注意“相关性”不等于“因果性”，文中提到的代谢通路改变与菌种减少的相关性需结合其他证据谨慎解读。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ac01dd1b97a2cb47cee04edc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该研究主要关注代谢通路和菌群组成的变化，对于具体的免疫细胞浸润、细胞因子水平等直接免疫效应指标，所给材料未提供详细信息。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::144bd64b15ea10bc68fd82d0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0024\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"identity\",\"reason\":\"source identity was not independently verified\",\"status\":\"input_attributed\"},{\"kind\":\"html\",\"known_losses\":[\"headings/tables/math/image pixels are not preserved by this plain HTML projection\"],\"reason\":\"body converted to structured material; headings/tables/math/image pixels may be lost\",\"status\":\"derived\"},{\"kind\":\"html\",\"reason\":\"html_not_scholarly_body\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"html\",\"reason\":\"html_not_scholarly_body\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"html\",\"reason\":\"html_challenge_or_login\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"pdf\",\"reason\":\"full-page text extracted; page positions retained\",\"status\":\"fitz\"},{\"kind\":\"fitz\",\"reason\":\"layout, table relations, formulas, figure pixels, and scanned text may be lost\",\"status\":\"known_gap\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s222\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c0f45620867bb47d8d241b27\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d95556f59f1a5dfeaf412001\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3e18a3ea80bd35dda72e241a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用基于GWAS摘要数据的两样本双向孟德尔随机化设计。暴露变量包括肠道微生物丰度、微生物代谢通路和血浆代谢物；结局变量为8种特定癌症的风险。使用逆方差加权（IVW）作为主要分析方法，辅以MR-Egger、加权中位数和贝叶斯加权MR进行敏感性分析。通过FDR校正控制假阳性，并利用MVMR调整混杂后计算中介效应比例。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0c44cc68e693e76a84a1056e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物、血浆代谢物与8种常见癌症之间的大规模因果关联证据，特别是揭示了微生物-代谢物-癌症轴的中介机制，为精准医疗提供了潜在的生物标志物和治疗靶点。\",\"limits\":\"1. 样本仅来自欧洲人群，限制了在其他种族中的外推性。2. 由于微生物GWAS统计效力较低，使用了较宽松的SNP阈值（P < 1e-5），尽管进行了严格筛选，但仍可能存在弱工具变量偏差和高假阳性率（部分结果FDR极高）。3. MR假设线性关系，无法捕捉非线性效应；结果反映长期累积效应，难以量化特定时间点的干预效果。4. 许多发现的中介比例较小或统计效力有限，需独立队列验证。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1cdc42d4e710b56fbd34e0ac\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"单向MR分析，P_IVW < 0.05且排除不一致方向或显著多效性结果\",\"finding\":\"识别出129种肠道微生物、57条微生物代谢通路和463种血浆代谢物与泛癌存在潜在因果关联。其中15种微生物、8条通路和58种代谢物与多种癌症相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::53f2d8130fcc6defac99679b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"反向MR分析，P_IVW < 0.05\",\"finding\":\"发现结直肠癌与Syntrophorhabdia之间存在名义上的双向因果关系；肺癌与硫酸盐还原通路、甲状腺癌与卟啉生物合成通路也存在潜在双向关系；26种血浆代谢物与癌症存在双向因果关联。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ac2510c5b5936aa4af9cc930\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"MVMR和中介分析，P < 0.05\",\"finding\":\"确认了9条显著的中介通路。例如，Gordonibacter丰度通过调节Palmitoleate (16:1n7)水平介导了15.60%的食管癌保护作用。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::48cca68e27b116e9f350b0ac\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::eae7452630896bd2e34e5212\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"1. 肠道微生物群的改变是癌症发病的因果驱动因素还是继发性后果？2. 微生物群失调与癌症风险之间是否存在双向因果关系？3. 血浆代谢物在微生物-癌症相互作用中发挥多大程度的介导作用？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::26f95f0b97bc5ed89346f58e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"研究欧洲人群（GWAS数据）中肠道微生物群（473种菌属/种、205条代谢通路）、血浆代谢物（1091种代谢物及309种比值）与8种泛癌（乳腺癌、结直肠癌、子宫内膜癌、食管癌、卵巢癌、肺癌、前列腺癌、甲状腺癌）之间的因果关系。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::72c3469b1383e11cd71c06c6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本研究旨在解决肠道微生物群改变是癌症病因还是继发后果的争议，以及两者间的双向因果和代谢介导机制尚不明确的问题。作者利用两样本双向孟德尔随机化（MR）分析，结合多变量MR（MVMR）和中介效应分析，系统评估了肠道微生物、血浆代谢物与泛癌风险之间的潜在因果联系。研究通过筛选遗传工具变量，排除了异质性和水平多效性干扰，识别出具有稳健因果关联的微生物、代谢物和通路，并量化了代谢物在微生物-癌症轴中的中介比例。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8183fbd4e9d66b2855586773\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文通过孟德尔随机化方法，从遗传角度证实了肠道微生物及其代谢产物对多种实体瘤（如食管癌、乳腺癌等）的潜在因果影响，并量化了代谢物的中介作用。对于综述而言，其核心价值在于提供了“微生物-代谢物-肿瘤”这一具体机制路径的因果证据，特别是针对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）疗效相关的炎症和代谢微环境调控，提供了基础生物学层面的支持素材。然而，该研究未直接涉及ICIs疗效的临床终点数据，主要提供的是易感性和病理生理机制的背景证据。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3a7b4f528c7f9b50a18a2cfd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这些中介效应是基于遗传关联推断的，并非直接的实验验证机制。中介比例通常较小，且多数关联仅在名义显著水平，需谨慎解读其临床解释力。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物通过调节特定血浆代谢物（如棕榈油酸、丙酰肉碱等）进而影响癌症风险的因果证据链。具体指出了9条中介通路，例如Gordonibacter通过Palmitoleate影响食管癌。这有助于解释微生物如何不直接作用于肿瘤细胞，而是通过系统性代谢重编程来介导其对宿主的影响。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::81b663c0ae20f274dc44b366\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"研究关注的是癌症发病风险（etiology），而非现有癌症患者接受ICI治疗后的疗效（efficacy/response）。因此，不能直接推断这些微生物对ICI疗效的影响方向或程度。\",\"contribution\":\"识别了与多种实体瘤（包括肺癌、乳腺癌、结直肠癌等ICI主要适应症）有因果关联的特定微生物属（如Ruminococcus D bicirculans, Gluconobacter, Holdemania等）。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::de7a4522c66f7ab6f27feff7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"研究发现8条血浆代谢通路参与多种癌症发展，如氨基酸代谢、嘌呤降解等。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1ccacaa3226821fea88b4ce7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文中提到的与肺癌、乳腺癌、结直肠癌等相关的微生物（如Ruminococcus, Fusobacterium等）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5873b17349430789679f464d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"使用MR方法克服观察性研究的混杂和反向因果偏倚。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0ad4414ed7af54e1e83783b4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该研究仅涵盖8种癌症，未包含所有实体瘤（如黑色素瘤虽在讨论中被提及作为ICI背景，但未纳入MR分析主体）。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d1fb94856315c33c55d973ed\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"结果主要反映癌症发生的遗传易感性，不能直接外推至已确诊癌症患者的治疗反应。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c6e4ff84fd3ce9891a6b9178\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"部分高FDR值的结果应被视为假设生成性质，而非确证性证据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::23ceced867ce2023de5cf4ad\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"所有数据源自欧洲人群，不适用于非欧洲裔群体的直接推断。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::08567a32027e1b861f221b6b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0059\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s053\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::07cd5b2d6202c7ff598866a1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::03706fac74e9ae78cf0cf089\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e4086809617589731824e1dd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"The authors conducted a structured narrative review using an evidence-based approach. They performed an extensive literature search covering peer-reviewed articles, expert reports, book chapters, and conference proceedings published between 1995 and 2025. Keywords included 'microbiome', 'immune checkpoint', 'cancer progression', 'immunotherapy', 'tumour microenvironment', and 'immune regulation'. The material was systematically evaluated and organized into four main sections: 1) Human microbiome and cancer development, 2) Immune checkpoint mechanisms and cancer progression, 3) Challenges of microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitions, and 4) Innovative immune modulation checkpoints for future strategies. The review relies on summarizing existing theoretical discussions and experimental studies rather than conducting new primary research.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::55a02a2dc52e7580d6d66133\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Provides a comprehensive overview of the intersection between microbiome science and immune checkpoint biology, categorizing mechanisms by checkpoint type (PD-1, CTLA-4, LAG-3) and microbial influence.\",\"limits\":\"As a narrative review, it does not present new primary data or a systematic meta-analysis. The exact molecular signaling pathways used by microbes to enhance anti-cancer immunity remain unclear according to the authors, indicating a gap in current mechanistic understanding.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::67c4c3e6af96242f4541dbea\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Highlights the therapeutic potential of combining microbiome modulation (probiotics, prebiotics, diet) with ICIs.\",\"limits\":\"The review notes that most research focuses on the gut microbiome, leaving the roles of lung, skin, and tumor microbiomes underexplored. Clinical translation is still in early stages, and standardized models for studying these interactions are lacking.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::95d22bb66d151b71205145ed\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"General mechanism described\",\"finding\":\"Microbiome dysbiosis is associated with increased inflammation, tumor progression, and reduced efficacy of ICIs, while a balanced microbiome promotes favorable immune responses.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5e29304bf98a9b6bf9a119bc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Specific bacterial species mentioned\",\"finding\":\"Bacteria such as Akkermansia muciniphila, Bifidobacterium, and Faecalibacterium are implicated in promoting T-cell activation and anti-tumor immunity, potentially through the production of short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs) like butyrate and propionate.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a635ddba111bab4d9611550c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Molecular pathway description\",\"finding\":\"PD-1/PD-L1 and CTLA-4 pathways inhibit T-cell activation via SHP-2 recruitment and dephosphorylation of key signaling molecules (ZAP-70, PI3K), leading to T-cell exhaustion. Dual blockade of PD-1 and LAG-3 enhances CD8+ T-cell clonal diversity and IFN-γ production.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::aea122fb269004e049b5e290\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Host factors\",\"finding\":\"Inter-individual differences in HLA heterozygosity and germline mutations (e.g., in TLR genes) significantly influence the response to ICIs and microbiome composition.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3bfbd0dcede79f72a5275257\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a01e8693a7f8797a6b42e997\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"The review aims to address the complex relationship between the microbiome and immune checkpoint mechanisms in cancer, specifically seeking to understand how microbiome composition impacts immune checkpoint expression/function, the challenges limiting anti-tumoral efficacy, and the innovative prospects for future anti-cancer strategies integrating microbiome science with immunotherapy.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1b4d9c3cfeb80380f15a8c54\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"The review covers the interaction between the human microbiome (primarily gut, but also lung, skin, and tumor) and immune checkpoint mechanisms (PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIM-3) in the context of cancer progression and immunotherapy. It spans from basic molecular mechanisms to clinical implications, including dietary and environmental influences.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::93df419f23881e7bb626802e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"This structured narrative review synthesizes current knowledge on how the microbiome modulates immune responses and affects the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) in cancer. The authors outline the biological basis of immune checkpoints, discuss specific microbial species and metabolites that influence T-cell activity, and explore challenges such as inter-individual variability and dysbiosis. The paper highlights the potential of combining microbiome modulation (via probiotics, diet, or FMT) with ICI therapies to overcome resistance and improve patient outcomes, while noting gaps in understanding molecular signaling pathways and the role of non-gut microbiomes.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5181e183b2c10026caf50473\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"This review serves as a high-level conceptual map for linking gut microbiome composition to ICI efficacy in solid tumors. It provides specific examples of beneficial bacteria (Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium), mechanisms of action (SCFA production, T-cell modulation), and host factors (HLA, genetics) that may mediate this effect. It is useful for establishing the background of microbiome-immune interactions and identifying key molecular targets (PD-1, LAG-3) where microbial influence is hypothesized, though it lacks detailed quantitative data on specific tumor types or patient cohorts.\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bafd57110247206857a0e5b8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"The review summarizes associations and potential mechanisms but does not provide specific clinical trial data or hazard ratios for these bacteria in solid tumors. It acknowledges that the exact molecular pathways are understudied.\",\"contribution\":\"Identifies specific microbial taxa (Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium, Faecalibacterium) associated with improved ICI efficacy and explains their general role in promoting anti-tumor immunity through T-cell modulation and SCFA production.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b6347179d994b6c43aa5ab53\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"The connection between specific microbial metabolites and these precise intracellular signaling cascades is stated as 'understudied' and 'unclear' in the text. The review links them conceptually but does not detail the direct causal chain for every bacterium-metabolite-target interaction.\",\"contribution\":\"Details the molecular mechanisms of immune checkpoints (PD-1/CTLA-4 signaling via SHP-2, ZAP-70, PI3K/AKT/mTOR) and how they lead to T-cell exhaustion. Also describes how dual blockade (PD-1/LAG-3) can reverse some of these effects by enhancing clonal diversity and IFN-γ production.\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8315483e27ca8a91fa594278\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"These are presented as general factors influencing variability; specific interactions between particular microbial strains and specific HLA alleles are not detailed.\",\"contribution\":\"Discusses host factors such as HLA heterozygosity and germline mutations (TLR, CTLA-4, PD-1 SNPs) that influence both microbiome composition and ICI response.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::06d348d8542dae49e25ecd4d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Descriptions of PD-1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, and TIM-3 functions, their role in T-cell regulation, and the concept of immune evasion.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2303aa38abbbb294e5728f90\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Mentions of high-fiber/Mediterranean diets promoting beneficial bacteria, and ultra-processed foods/dysbiosis linked to poor outcomes.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::15d644fbea992ad437f01b6f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Explicit statements that the exact molecular signaling pathways of microbes are unclear, and that non-gut microbiomes (lung, skin, tumor) are underexplored.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9b8a1900c0acca7bd3801284\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"This is a narrative review, not a systematic meta-analysis; findings represent synthesized perspectives rather than pooled statistical results.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::aa63729cb0ce9c470294b016\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The review explicitly states that the exact molecular mechanisms by which microbes influence specific checkpoints are 'understudied' and 'unclear'; do not infer direct causal chains where only associative or hypothetical links are made.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5e556766daf1ba1ff970208b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"While gut microbiome is the primary focus, the review acknowledges significant gaps in knowledge regarding lung, skin, and tumor microbiomes; avoid assuming gut findings apply universally to all tissue sites without caution.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8d689bcd3159587560683629\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Claims about specific bacteria (e.g., Akkermansia) improving ICI efficacy are based on emerging evidence summarized here; verify against primary clinical trials for specific solid tumor types if precise efficacy metrics are required.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::148441cdf053ea845666e0f4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0005\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s040\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c63d5fbb47ffa46172f25167\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::360f4d715a1e85a344fd0e8a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::54460fcc9b674b16fa00b8fb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用回顾性队列分析方法。首先从2021年《Science》发表的“饮食纤维和益生菌影响黑色素瘤免疫治疗反应”研究中提取AYA队列（N=23）。随后进行倾向评分或匹配设计，按2:1比例选取50-70岁的老年非AYA患者作为对照组。统计控制变量包括性别、BMI、种族、治疗初治状态、疾病分期（III期/IV期）、吸烟、药物及酒精使用史。利用高通量测序数据进行Alpha和Beta多样性分析，并进行差异丰度分析（Differential Analysis）以识别组间特异性微生物标志物。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a79c95afeb0ce7aea3853d69\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"首次系统性地描述了AYA黑色素瘤患者肠道微生物组的特征，并明确了其与老年患者的关键差异（如Bacteroides stercoris vs Ruminococcaceae/Blautia/Dorea的分布）。\",\"limits\":\"样本量较小（AYA仅23人）；数据来源于二手提取而非独立前瞻性收集；未直接报告微生物组特征与ICI具体临床疗效（如ORR, PFS, OS）的相关性，仅提供了基线特征描述；部分P值报告可能存在格式错误（如Blautia obeum的p值缺失或异常），需谨慎解读统计显著性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c24ca101fe6ac33803d551a3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"AYA (15-39岁) vs. Older non-AYA (50-70岁)，匹配后样本量分别为23和46\",\"finding\":\"Alpha和Beta多样性在两组间无统计学显著差异；但观察到Alpha多样性随年龄增加而增加的趋势。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a7ce9a312d9ed2f1638e875e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"差异丰度分析\",\"finding\":\"老年非AYA患者中Ruminococcaceae科（家族水平）丰度显著更高；AYA患者中Bacteroides stercoris丰度更高。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::597957f0559b74ad71d261ab\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"特定菌种 prevalence\",\"finding\":\"Blautia massiliensia (p=0.010), Blautia obeum, 和 Dorea longicatena (p=0.035) 在老年非AYA患者中显著更常见，这些物种已知与肥胖生物标志物相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::95adf190e53a839c4f66cc2f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4b42c6910a5ab5e3934dd15b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）已改变晚期黑色素瘤的治疗格局，但青少年及年轻成人（AYA）群体在此类治疗中的生存获益历史上低于其他年龄段，且关于该特定人群肠道微生物组对ICI疗效影响的研究匮乏。本研究试图明确AYA患者肠道微生物组的独特特征，以解释潜在的疗效差异并为个性化治疗提供依据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c5ab529a33fc4aa7c0ba1ad7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"研究对象为15-39岁的青少年及年轻成人（AYA）黑色素瘤患者，以及50-70岁的老年非AYA患者。研究情境为接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的晚期黑色素瘤患者。数据来源为2021年《Science》发表的一项研究的回顾性队列数据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::621c238c42151ca1082b6986\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本研究旨在比较AYA与老年黑色素瘤患者在接受免疫检查点抑制剂治疗前的肠道微生物组特征差异。研究从既往大型研究中提取了23名AYA患者，并按2:1比例匹配了46名老年患者作为对照。在控制了性别、BMI、种族、疾病分期等混杂因素后，通过测序数据分析两组间的微生物多样性及特定菌属丰度。研究发现两组间整体多样性无显著差异，但物种组成存在显著不同：老年组中富集了随年龄增长而增加的Ruminococcaceae科及与肥胖相关的Blautia和Dorea属细菌，而AYA组中Bacteroides stercoris丰度较高。结论指出AYA与老年患者的肠道菌群特征存在本质差异，提示针对AYA人群的微生物调节策略需区别于老年人。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fdb5b8888a97a1eebb836436\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文提供了青少年及年轻成人（AYA）黑色素瘤患者肠道微生物组的基线特征数据，并与老年患者进行了对比。对于综述而言，其核心价值在于揭示了“年龄/发育阶段”这一宿主因素如何塑造肠道菌群结构，从而可能影响免疫治疗的响应基础。它不直接回答机制问题，但为解释为何不同年龄段患者对ICI反应不同提供了重要的背景变量和潜在的生物标志物线索。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b90473264289de79142d0882\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"仅描述基线特征，未直接关联临床结局（如生存期或缓解率）。不能直接证明这些菌群差异导致了疗效差异，只能说明存在相关性或潜在风险因素。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了AYA与老年黑色素瘤患者肠道菌群组成的基线差异数据。具体显示AYA患者富含Bacteroides stercoris，而老年患者富含Ruminococcaceae及Blautia/Dorea属。这有助于解释不同年龄组患者微环境的基础差异，进而可能影响ICI疗效。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::91f62d029f6d062893eab747\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制推断较弱。虽然提到B. stercoris与纤维摄入相关，但未在本文中进行因果验证。不能据此断定菌群差异是疗效差异的唯一机制。\",\"contribution\":\"指出了AYA与老年患者菌群结构的显著不同，特别是涉及膳食纤维代谢相关菌种（Bacteroides stercoris与纤维摄入正相关）的差异。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3c26278e9a3f998a24452ba0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"AYA患者（15-39岁）在黑色素瘤流行病学和治疗反应上的独特性，以及当前研究在该群体的缺乏。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fdb042fcd8544ecc1908f039\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"发现AYA患者中Bacteroides stercoris较多，而老年患者中肥胖相关菌（Blautia/Dorea）较多。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::26808b690a8af30833a15b67\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该研究为横断面基线描述，未建立菌群与临床结局的直接因果联系。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fff1a9c3ac39dbe1c9eda1d9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"样本量小（N=23），统计效力有限，尤其是亚组分析结果需谨慎对待。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b18352633f474ecd4cf79305\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"数据源自2021年《Science》论文的二次提取，原始研究的详细方法学细节（如测序深度、生信流程）在本摘要中未完全交代，需查阅原文确认。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::023c913f5bd9899f87bdf664\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"P值报告存在不一致（如Blautia obeum的p值），阅读时需保持警惕，不宜过度强调统计显著性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a1545368d30cd49932a56c4e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0010\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"identity\",\"reason\":\"source identity was not independently verified\",\"status\":\"input_attributed\"},{\"kind\":\"pdf\",\"reason\":\"full-page text extracted; page positions retained\",\"status\":\"fitz\"},{\"kind\":\"fitz\",\"reason\":\"layout, table relations, formulas, figure pixels, and scanned text may be lost\",\"status\":\"known_gap\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s189\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::36aa7c16dd9aa335f125602a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::eec523ebb51b576f83a906d5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::336d3e9f649133c8318edf00\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用前瞻性队列研究设计。纳入标准：组织学确诊的不可切除III期或IV期皮肤黑色素瘤患者，接受抗PD-1单药治疗（纳武利尤单抗或帕博利珠单抗）。对照组为患者的直系亲属（健康人）。主要终点：根据RECIST v.1.1标准评估的治疗反应（完全缓解CR、部分缓解PR定义为响应者；疾病稳定SD、进展PD定义为非响应者）。数据采集：治疗前通过问卷收集社会人口学、临床、生活方式和饮食变量；采集基线粪便样本。实验室分析：使用DNeasy PowerSoil Pro提取DNA，扩增16S rRNA基因V3-V4区进行Illumina MiSeq测序，使用DADA2流程生成ASVs并基于SILVA数据库进行分类；对部分样本进行宏基因组鸟枪法测序以重建MAGs。统计分析：比较各组间的菌群多样性（Alpha/Beta）、相对丰度及临床特征差异，使用Kruskal-Wallis检验、Fisher精确检验及limma线性模型识别差异物种。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7ba2dfedc1eb207addb32c68\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了波兰这一特定欧洲人群背景下，肠道微生物组特征与抗PD-1治疗反应的关联证据，指出了与该人群饮食模式（如高植物摄入）相关的潜在有益菌属（P. copri, B. uniformis）。\",\"limits\":\"样本量较小（尤其是对照组仅10人，且年龄显著小于患者组）；观察性研究设计无法确立因果关系；饮食数据依赖自我报告问卷，可能存在回忆偏倚；未直接测量微生物代谢产物机制；不同研究间关于特定菌属（如Faecalibacterium）作用的矛盾结果提示人群异质性，限制了单一生物标志物的普适性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f3dabf81aac85365acaa0d7d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"波兰黑色素瘤患者队列，基线状态\",\"finding\":\"响应者（n=25）的拟杆菌门/厚壁菌门比值显著高于非响应者（n=32），且响应者的细菌物种丰富度（Richness）显著低于非响应者。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::03ad9e12f07b47f5c940696d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"波兰黑色素瘤患者队列，基线状态\",\"finding\":\"响应者肠道中普雷沃氏菌（Prevotella copri）和均匀拟杆菌（Bacteroides uniformis）的丰度显著升高；非响应者中普拉梭菌（Faecalibacterium prausnitzii）、肠脱硫弧菌（Desulfovibrio intestinalis）及部分未分类厚壁菌显著富集。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::afb811ac51851f8ef1c79e86\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"波兰黑色素瘤患者队列，基线饮食调查\",\"finding\":\"高植物性食物（水果和蔬菜总和）摄入与响应概率增加2.9倍相关；低乳制品摄入（每日≤1份）与响应概率增加2.0倍相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::072e088bef5b876efe98b6a4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"波兰黑色素瘤患者队列，基线状态\",\"finding\":\"响应者的粪便钙卫蛋白水平（炎症标志物）中位数低于非响应者，但组间差异无统计学意义。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b0757ddd3362ddc16e521525\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::19e0ec894f1eb5a1184b3d6d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"在波兰人群中，基线肠道微生物组的组成以及饮食等外在因素是否与黑色素瘤患者对抗PD-1治疗的临床反应（响应 vs. 非响应）相关？是否存在人群特异性的微生物标志物？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::863cf7d94bd87e259d9fdeb2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"波兰人群中的转移性黑色素瘤患者（接受抗PD-1治疗）及健康对照，聚焦基线肠道微生物组组成、饮食模式与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的关联。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ba74aefc5df7bb8b114ac5d3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本研究旨在探讨波兰裔黑色素瘤患者对抗PD-1治疗的反应与其基线肠道微生物组及外在修饰因素（如饮食）之间的关联。研究招募了64名接受抗PD-1治疗的患者和10名健康对照，通过问卷调查收集人口统计学、生活方式和饮食数据，并在治疗前采集粪便样本进行16S rRNA基因测序（metataxonomics）及部分宏基因组鸟枪法测序。结果显示，响应者（R）与非响应者（NR）在肠道菌群结构上存在显著差异：响应者的拟杆菌门/厚壁菌门（Bacteroidota/Firmicutes）比值较高，物种丰富度较低；响应者肠道中普雷沃氏菌（Prevotella copri）和均匀拟杆菌（Bacteroides uniformis）丰度较高，而非响应者则富集普拉梭菌（Faecalibacterium prausnitzii）、肠脱硫弧菌（Desulfovibrio intestinalis）及部分未分类厚壁菌。此外，高植物摄入和低乳制品摄入与更好的治疗反应相关。该研究强调了肠道微生物组和饮食对ICI疗效的影响具有人群特异性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::49cb8db198fa13c507057ec7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文为综述提供了关于肠道微生物组影响免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的人群特异性证据。其核心价值在于揭示了在波兰人群中，特定的微生物组合（P. copri, B. uniformis）和饮食模式（高植物、低乳制品）与治疗响应正相关，这与部分其他队列（如Chaput et al.发现Faecalibacterium有益）的结果形成对比，有助于综述讨论“微生物标志物的人群依赖性”和“饮食-微生物-免疫”交互作用。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::efd525b8d51c8646673bf5ad\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"仅限波兰人群，不能直接外推至其他种族或地理区域；观察性关联，非因果证明。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了波兰人群中与抗PD-1治疗响应正相关的特定微生物类群（P. copri, B. uniformis）和负相关类群（F. prausnitzii, D. intestinalis）的具体数据。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::825c7f4f98b5e07f9c30a0ec\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"基于自我报告问卷，缺乏对具体营养成分或代谢产物的直接测量；混杂因素（如整体生活方式）未完全控制。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了饮食模式（高植物摄入、低乳制品摄入）与ICI治疗响应相关的流行病学证据。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::924f3d1141577180ee5bcbb0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"钙卫蛋白差异无统计学意义；未直接测定免疫细胞浸润或细胞因子水平；机制链条不完整。\",\"contribution\":\"探讨了肠道菌群组成与宿主肠道炎症状态（通过粪便钙卫蛋白衡量）的潜在联系，尽管统计上不显著，但趋势显示响应者炎症水平较低。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0ab239de79b2493b354259b7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"作者指出与其他队列（如中国NSCLC患者中P. copri有益，或某些黑色素瘤队列中Faecalibacterium有益）结果的矛盾，强调单一物种不能作为跨人群的通用生物标志物。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9e01134b66ca5c18493345af\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"研究发现高植物摄入和低乳制品摄入与良好预后相关，并引用文献说明膳食纤维可能通过产生短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）增强T细胞反应。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b9ee09f7293357ceedf2c7af\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该研究的发现基于波兰特定人群，其微生物组特征受当地饮食和文化影响，结果不能直接推广到其他种族或地区。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::089fc94ec405841194913163\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"对照组年龄显著小于患者组，且样本量小，这可能影响基线微生物组比较的解释力，需谨慎对待与健康对照的比较结果。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c90a11b11848cab5e8c2f7f7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"饮食数据来自问卷，存在主观性和回忆偏差，且未量化具体营养素摄入量，仅能反映大致饮食模式。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::854f2417fb331859fb4ff475\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"虽然发现了微生物与响应的关联，但未阐明具体的分子机制（如代谢产物、抗原模拟等），因此不能用于解释确切的生物学通路。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::55c6fd10a6749abc57a112b9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0545\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"identity\",\"reason\":\"source identity was not independently verified\",\"status\":\"input_attributed\"},{\"kind\":\"pdf\",\"reason\":\"full-page text extracted; page positions retained\",\"status\":\"fitz\"},{\"kind\":\"fitz\",\"reason\":\"layout, table relations, formulas, figure pixels, and scanned text may be lost\",\"status\":\"known_gap\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s024\",\"s281\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::661ac39e317c4d00a2d636c4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4dd74fbdc2f421ab931a4cb0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::711d27360533c41d6d2ec36c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用范围综述方法论。使用PICO框架构建指导问题，在PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, Scopus, SciELO, LILACS五个数据库进行结构化搜索。纳入标准为涉及成年癌症患者、接受系统性肿瘤治疗、进行肠道微生物组分析并明确链接到治疗反应/毒性/预后的研究。排除儿科、仅放疗/手术、纯体外实验及2015年前文献。数据提取通过标准化表格进行，涵盖研究设计、人群特征、微生物分析方法、预测模型性能及主要结果。最终通过叙事综合法（narrative synthesis）对数据进行定性汇总，按癌症类型和治疗模式分类，重点区分“定量预测模型”与“微生物特征描述”，并识别知识空白和方法学局限。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::011d8e1b72c422e144efa713\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了2015-2025年间肠道微生物组在肿瘤治疗反应中应用的全面地图，区分了预测模型开发与微生物特征描述两类证据。\",\"limits\":\"作为范围综述，不进行质量评估或因果推断；未提供定量荟萃分析结果；所引用的原始研究多为小样本或回顾性，存在选择偏倚和混杂因素控制不足的风险。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::47aa59edf8e80e7879afe702\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"明确了微生物组预测模型在特定情境下（如尿路上皮癌、直肠癌）超越传统临床标记物的潜力，强调了菌株水平分辨率的重要性。\",\"limits\":\"不同研究的测序技术、生信流程和统计方法高度异质，导致直接比较困难；多数证据仍为关联性而非因果性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b7ee2bfeae4e357feca73e50\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"指出了临床转化的主要障碍：方法学标准化缺失、外部验证不足、机制不明及监管挑战。\",\"limits\":\"未能提供具体的标准化协议建议或成本效益分析的详细数据；对真菌、病毒等非细菌微生物的作用探讨有限。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::83d1af535bb6a4c8baae2ee9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗，多中心队列及荟萃分析\",\"finding\":\"菌株水平的微生物特征比临床因素更具预测力。Gunjur等(2024)发现针对联合ICI反应的菌株特征AUC为0.73，优于临床因素的0.56；但泛癌种通用特征在不同ICI方案间外推性较差（一致方案AUC 0.65 vs 不一致方案0.51）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::aa01327d182b7a35bd738a5f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"新辅助化疗，尿路上皮癌\",\"finding\":\"微生物组预测模型表现优于临床变量。Bukavina等(2024)开发的随机森林模型预测完全缓解（CR）的AUC为0.88，而临床因素仅为0.50；高拟杆菌属丰度与较差反应相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::65ce34ec16ea84186df5a999\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"同步放化疗，鼻咽癌\",\"finding\":\"益生菌干预可降低毒性。Xia等(2021)的II期试验显示，益生菌鸡尾酒将3-4级口腔粘膜炎发生率从47.1%降至25%，并通过调节肠道菌群失调和增强免疫反应发挥作用。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fdaca457d135841bbe395399\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"新辅助免疫放化疗，局部晚期直肠癌\",\"finding\":\"物种水平模型具有高预测准确性。Yang等(2024)开发的SPEED模型在训练集AUC为98.8%，验证集为77.8%，用于预测病理完全缓解（pCR）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cb0b5abe6bd93e8ca5e5c6b5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"多种实体瘤，综述综合\",\"finding\":\"特定菌属与疗效/毒性关联。双歧杆菌、阿克曼氏菌、粪杆菌等通常与ICI良好反应相关；梭杆菌、拟杆菌等在部分研究中与化疗耐药或毒性增加相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::39bf57bd7ec01753d11856ee\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8e3b08f72d596718e9bb782c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"解决的核心问题是：肠道微生物组衍生的生物标志物和预测模型在肿瘤治疗反应实践中具有何种临床潜力？具体动机在于应对癌症治疗的异质性响应、固有毒性及耐药性挑战，寻找能实现更精准患者选择和疗法优化的新型生物标志物。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0c91c85e8effd4baf32727a9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"成人癌症患者（涵盖结直肠癌、黑色素瘤、非小细胞肺癌、食管癌、尿路上皮癌等实体瘤），接受全身性肿瘤治疗（化疗、免疫检查点抑制剂ICIs、靶向治疗及联合方案）。研究范围聚焦于肠道微生物组作为生物标志物在预测治疗反应、毒性及疾病进程中的临床潜力，包括微生物特征识别和预测模型的开发/验证。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::738eff2017d024fc1b01f364\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"这是一篇遵循JBI指南和PRISMA-ScR报告的范围综述（scoping review），旨在系统映射并批判性地描述当前关于肠道微生物组在肿瘤学中作为生物标志物的证据。作者检索了2015年至2025年间发表的20项相关研究，涵盖了观察性队列、临床试验和机制研究。综述重点分析了特定微生物类群如何影响免疫治疗和化疗的疗效，以及它们对治疗相关毒性的调节作用。研究发现，基于微生物组的预测模型在某些情况下优于传统临床标记物（如尿路上皮癌中AUC达0.88 vs 0.50），且特定干预（如益生菌）可减轻毒性。然而，综述也指出，由于方法学异质性、缺乏外部验证和机制理解不完整，这些模型的临床转化仍面临挑战。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b9b4578c05b8f7b07647e479\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为回答“肠道微生物组如何调节实体瘤ICIs疗效及其机制”提供了关键的背景框架和具体证据线索。它汇总了支持微生物组影响ICI疗效的主要菌属（如双歧杆菌、阿克曼氏菌）、展示了微生物预测模型在ICI反应预测中的性能数据（特别是菌株水平特征的优势），并讨论了FMT克服ICI耐药的临床尝试。同时，它指出了当前证据的方法学局限（异质性、缺乏外部验证），有助于在综述中平衡地呈现微生物组 biomarker 的现状与挑战。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::85d4c075f44e0f132e06caed\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"预测模型的性能数据来自特定队列，外推性受限；FMT试验样本量小（n=15）；大多数关联证据来自观察性研究，不能直接证明因果关系。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物组影响ICI疗效的具体微生物特征和预测模型性能数据。包括：1) Gunjur等(2024)的多中心研究显示菌株水平特征对联合ICI反应的预测能力（AUC 0.73）优于临床因素；2) Gazzaniga & Kasper (2025)和Gopalakrishnan等(2018)综述指出的与良好ICI反应相关的菌属（双歧杆菌、阿克曼氏菌、粪杆菌等）；3) Davar等(2021)的临床试验显示FMT可使PD-1难治性黑色素瘤患者获得客观缓解（20%）。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::09a6b7bfdf51f2fbcab58d48\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"该综述主要归纳其他研究的机制发现，本身未提供新的机制实验数据；许多机制仍处于假说阶段，需结合原文献进一步验证；未详细阐述所有可能的代谢途径。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了微生物组调节ICI疗效的可能机制线索和间接证据。包括：1) Gazzaniga & Kasper (2025)和Chrysostomou等(2023)综述提到的免疫调节机制（如激活T细胞、NK细胞、I型干扰素通路）；2) McCulloch等(2022)观察到不利微生物特征与全身炎症（NLR升高）相关；3) Davar等(2021)发现FMT诱导CD8+ T细胞活化；4) 综述指出抗生素使用可能削弱ICI疗效，暗示生态依赖性。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::17e85bdc44e67b65e568505b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"综述指出当前证据的方法学异质性（样本采集、DNA提取、生信流程）、缺乏外部验证、小样本量导致的过拟合风险，以及因果关系的缺失。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2d2018252fd4aee42531eb16\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"综述提到微生物组也影响化疗疗效（如梭杆菌促进耐药，拟杆菌改善某些化疗药效果）和毒性（如益生菌降低粘膜炎，特定菌属预测3-4级毒性）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::93842ba0acb7c1623cffc35d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"综述提到微生物组特征在早期检测（结直肠腺瘤/癌，AUC 96%/87%）和疾病进展预测（如mCRC中乳酸杆菌与反应相关）中的潜力。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::92203afa91a5d08ad9c31eae\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述是范围综述，其结论基于对20项研究的叙事综合，而非定量荟萃分析。因此，其提供的“AUC”等性能指标应视为各独立研究的结果汇总，而非经过严格统计合并的估计值。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f144188f88dd66e6b5199a8c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"综述中引用的机制解释（如免疫激活、代谢产物作用）主要来自被综述的原始文献或评论文章，并非本综述作者的新发现。在引用时需明确来源。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2bdb542a3b579fd596759670\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"综述强调“菌株水平”特征的重要性，但这主要基于Gunjur等(2024)的一项研究，其他多数研究停留在属或种水平。因此，菌株水平的优越性尚需更多证据支持。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a2fa1a7af600d3f8db94c74b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"综述包含了一些非ICI治疗（如化疗、靶向治疗）的研究，在应用于回答ICI相关问题时，需注意区分不同治疗模式的微生物组相互作用差异。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f33418f66f54c2ba117b589d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"综述指出临床转化面临巨大挑战，因此在利用其提供的积极发现（如高AUC）时，必须同时强调其探索性质和缺乏外部验证的局限性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::269a6177926dee975b0abb8c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0026\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s279\",\"s093\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3170d76df87bfb377320ebc6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::833ddf71a11d978e6fce42b3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bce53def04698b2385f517a0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"As a review article, the approach involves a critical appraisal of published literature rather than primary data generation. The authors systematically discuss: 1) Preclinical models identifying key bacterial species; 2) Clinical correlations between stool microbiome composition and ICI outcomes; 3) The impact of antibiotics on survival; 4) Specific intervention trials for prebiotics (dietary fiber), probiotics (CBM588, SER-401), and FMT across different tumor types and lines of therapy. They compare results against historical benchmarks and note limitations such as small sample sizes and heterogeneity in trial designs.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::eb889e487c6bdd1e356372eb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Provides a comprehensive synthesis of current evidence linking gut microbiome composition to ICI efficacy in solid tumors, categorizing strategies into prebiotics, probiotics, and FMT.\",\"limits\":\"The field lacks large, definitive randomized trials; most evidence comes from small phase I/II studies or retrospective analyses. The review acknowledges that widespread adoption is premature and mechanisms are not fully elucidated.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1b772a2563878345157adfe5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Highlights the complexity of microbial effects, noting that both low and excessively high levels of certain bacteria (e.g., Akkermansia) may be suboptimal, suggesting a need for balanced composition rather than single-species enrichment.\",\"limits\":\"Does not provide causal mechanistic proof for all observed associations; many findings are correlative.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d8a1dbcd8a5f17abeac1cf9e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Identifies specific ongoing trials and future directions, such as stratification based on baseline microbiome composition.\",\"limits\":\"Cannot predict the success of future trials or resolve uncertainties regarding universal vs. personalized application of microbiome therapies.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6a77b53a16f1542d379f2044\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Preclinical and observational clinical studies\",\"finding\":\"Specific bacterial taxa (Ruminococcaceae, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) correlate with favorable responses to anti-PD-1 antibodies, while antibiotic use before/during ICI initiation is associated with higher primary resistance and shorter overall survival.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0ee1f89ce9752d4834de52d4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Clinical trials of Probiotics (CBM588)\",\"finding\":\"Small prospective trials in mRCC showed significantly improved progression-free survival and overall response rates when CBM588 was added to ICI-based regimens, though sample sizes were limited (n=30 per arm).\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c04267c3ab6c013d3e805b57\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Clinical trials of FMT\",\"finding\":\"FMT combined with ICIs showed encouraging results in refractory melanoma (ORR 30%) and frontline settings for melanoma (ORR 65%), NSCLC (ORR 77%), and RCC (12-month PFS improved from 35% to 67%). However, benefits were not consistent in all contexts, such as microsatellite-stable colorectal cancer where outcomes were comparable to historical controls without FMT.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0fbe205ee9cf1e2729d24317\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Biomarker development\",\"finding\":\"The TOPOSCORE biomarker, integrating Akkermansia with other microbial groups, showed significant correlation with overall survival in cohorts of mNSCLC, mRCC, and urothelial carcinoma.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c47c382f8fcd311029400a6b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::391636a4ef531dc3e03166fa\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"The paper addresses the growing interest in microbiome modulation as a therapeutic strategy to overcome resistance to ICIs in oncology. It seeks to summarize current evidence regarding which microbial species are beneficial or detrimental, how disruption affects outcomes, and whether specific modulation strategies (prebiotics, probiotics, FMT) show clinical benefit.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d466f3497f07b41883777b89\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"The review focuses on the interplay between the gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) in patients with solid malignancies, specifically advanced melanoma, metastatic renal cell carcinoma (mRCC), and metastatic non–small cell lung cancer (mNSCLC). It covers preclinical evidence, clinical observations of microbial associations, and various modulation strategies including prebiotics, probiotics, and fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT).\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8bf43a9c720757c7c1b29667\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"This article is a narrative review that critically appraises existing studies on how gut microbiome modulation can enhance the efficacy of ICIs in solid tumors. It synthesizes preclinical findings linking specific bacterial taxa to treatment response, discusses the negative impact of antibiotic-induced dysbiosis, and evaluates clinical data from trials involving dietary interventions, probiotic supplementation, and FMT. The authors highlight promising signals but emphasize the lack of large-scale randomized controlled trials needed to establish standard of care.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a96d68b8b3ab3149559fa7a0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"This review serves as a foundational overview for understanding the current state of microbiome modulation in ICI-treated solid tumors. It provides concrete examples of successful and failed interventions, specific bacterial markers associated with response, and the methodological challenges in this field. It is particularly useful for establishing the background of why microbiome matters, summarizing the landscape of clinical trials, and highlighting the gap between preclinical promise and clinical validation.\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::067e4c00a3d6d84463a180d1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Most clinical data are from small, non-randomized, or early-phase trials. Cannot definitively prove causality for all associations. The review itself notes that large RCTs are lacking.\",\"contribution\":\"Summarizes clinical evidence showing that specific gut microbes (Ruminococcaceae, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) are associated with improved ICI outcomes, while antibiotic disruption correlates with poorer survival. Provides ORR and PFS data from FMT and probiotic trials in melanoma, RCC, and NSCLC.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2cbbb1c1818351f5263e174a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"The review is descriptive and does not present new mechanistic experiments. Mechanisms are largely inferred from preclinical models or translational analyses of small cohorts. Does not provide detailed molecular pathway analysis.\",\"contribution\":\"Discusses potential mechanisms indirectly through observed effects: e.g., dietary fiber enhancing postbiotic production, vancomycin preconditioning disrupting immunity, and intratumoral Gammaproteobacteria hindering gemcitabine response. Mentions the role of short-chain fatty acids.\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::193d9a5f14c622a00b8fa4ba\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"The review establishes the rationale for microbiome modulation, citing preclinical discoveries (Sivan et al., Vétizou et al.) and the general interplay between gut microbiome and immunity.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::442c140f14f35073e88fda05\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Contrasting results: FMT worked well in melanoma/RCC/NSCLC but showed no added benefit over historical controls in microsatellite-stable colorectal cancer.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::53f032c1944a751907a8ef5a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Discussion of small sample sizes, lack of standardization in FMT donors (responders vs. healthy volunteers), and conflicting data on single-biomarker utility (Akkermansia levels).\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9e457f01ec0c174b1c1a5c20\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The review is a narrative summary, not a systematic meta-analysis. Do not treat its conclusions as definitive consensus.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2f55750dba533f27c47b404c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Clinical trial results cited are primarily from Phase I/II studies with small sample sizes; avoid overstating efficacy as established fact.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1b246c5f5e588d398b2174b7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Mechanistic claims are largely based on preclinical models or correlational clinical data; distinguish between observed association and proven mechanism.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::895c49a50d8426f8ea373423\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The review explicitly states that large randomized trials are lacking; do not imply that these strategies are standard of care.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b149a9f56e3601f28672e249\",\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s008\",\"s129\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8e24c98ddc10d25e6368e25c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c7751d6078705a8eed77bd20\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b7b7e3472b4df79f76e0d24c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用叙述性综述方法，综合了机制研究（前临床模型与人类观察数据）和临床干预试验证据。具体路线包括：1）梳理微生物组影响ICI的药理学基础（抗原呈递、代谢物耦合、屏障完整性）；2）分类评估三类主要干预手段（FMT、LBPs、定义菌群）的代表性临床试验结果；3）讨论影响可重复性的转化因素（共用药、饮食、定植率）及安全监管问题。未进行系统检索或定量荟萃分析，而是基于现有文献进行逻辑整合与批判性评议。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d823b853e4ac54a493eee6ef\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了关于微生物组工程化干预ICI治疗的最新临床证据综合，特别区分了FMT、LBPs和定义菌群三种模态的优缺点及适用场景。\",\"limits\":\"作为迷你综述，未提供新的原始实验数据；对特定菌株或代谢物的因果机制多基于前临床模型或间接人类证据，缺乏大规模随机对照试验的确证数据。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cdc0eb48bfb3cc26a577a419\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提出了将微生物组干预视为“生态药理学”而非简单附加剂的框架，强调了基线生态、共用药和功能性读出（如代谢物、定植率）的重要性。\",\"limits\":\"对于不同肿瘤类型间微生物组效应的异质性解释有限，主要依赖已发表的小规模试验，难以推断普适性规律。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c698a9fd6f94a8050dbc3115\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"明确了安全与监管优先事项，包括供体筛查、追溯性及报告标准，为未来临床试验设计提供了实用指南。\",\"limits\":\"监管建议基于现有案例和专家共识，尚未形成统一的行业标准，具体实施细节尚待后续研究明确。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::698814d6ffd5131ce300e4d6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"抗PD-1难治性转移性黑色素瘤\",\"finding\":\"来自反应者的粪菌移植（FMT）提供了最强的人类概念验证，部分患者实现了临床再敏感化，并伴随供体型微生物特征和肿瘤免疫重塑。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8fa931de280fc236eee06476\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"使用活体生物制剂（如CBM588）联合ICI\",\"finding\":\"在肾细胞癌中显示出改善临床结果的探索性信号，且能显著改变粪便微生物组特征，但结果具有情境依赖性，需更多大样本验证。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4ccc398d5ad7381abec37394\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"使用定义菌群（如SER-401）及抗生素预处理\",\"finding\":\"一项针对黑色素瘤的Ib期试验因入组不足未能得出效力结论，但揭示了广谱抗生素预处理可能破坏保护性免疫准备，提示“清除后添加”策略存在设计陷阱。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::46a823fe6dc2d69e904ef7b1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"ICI相关的难治性结肠炎\",\"finding\":\"FMT在病例系列和转化研究中显示出修复生态平衡、恢复黏膜免疫耐受的活动，支持其作为毒性管理的潜在手段。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7235049ddd5daa54ae6a8121\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1fc6d62ba3897e0fe7ee791b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管ICIs改变了多种恶性肿瘤的管理方式，但仅对部分患者有效且伴随毒性。现有的组织生物标志物无法完全捕捉宿主层面的决定因素。本研究试图解决的核心问题是：肠道微生物组如何作为可操作的调节器影响ICI的敏感性和毒性？以及目前基于微生物组的临床干预策略（FMT、LBPs、Consortia）的证据基础和转化障碍是什么？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0de486040443081d8ed9cbc1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"聚焦于实体瘤（特别是黑色素瘤、肾细胞癌、非小细胞肺癌等）患者接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs，如抗PD-1/CTLA-4治疗）时的疗效与毒性管理。研究对象为肠道微生物组及其工程化干预策略，涵盖从基础机制到临床转化试验的综合分析。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::08bc0ccb88530457d6c7da11\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇迷你综述，旨在将微生物生态学原理与抗原呈递、T细胞启动及代谢物信号传导等生物学机制联系起来，并系统总结了三种主要干预模式（粪菌移植FMT、活体生物制剂LBPs、定义菌群Consortia）的临床证据。文章指出，肠道微生物组不仅是预测标志物，更是可操作的宿主水平调节剂，能够同时影响抗肿瘤疗效和免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）。通过回顾早期临床试验，作者强调了微生物组干预在重新敏感化难治性肿瘤中的概念验证价值，同时也指出了当前干预措施在可重复性、安全性及标准化方面的挑战。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5cc8704ee17e7dd46325481a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文为综述中关于‘微生物组如何调节ICI疗效’及‘介导机制’提供了结构化的临床证据框架。它不仅汇总了FMT、LBPs和定义菌群三类干预的具体试验结果，还深入分析了影响这些干预效果的生态学和药理学因素（如抗生素使用、饮食、基线菌群状态）。这对于回答用户关于机制和疗效的问题至关重要，因为它将分散的临床试验置于一个统一的‘生态药理学’解释框架下，并指出了当前证据的边界（如难治性 vs. 一线治疗，不同肿瘤类型的差异）。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c38bcef62c8079a6036e37c8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"证据主要来自小规模Phase 1/Ib期试验，样本量小，异质性高。不能直接外推至所有一线治疗场景或所有肿瘤类型。特别是SER-401试验未达效力终点，需谨慎解读。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了三类主要微生物组干预策略（FMT、LBPs、Consortia）在实体瘤中的具体临床证据对比。例如，FMT在难治性黑色素瘤中显示出的概念验证效力，以及LBPs在肾细胞癌中的探索性信号。同时指出了定义菌群试验中因抗生素预处理导致的负面设计教训。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0e83796c6787bdce34f2f296\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"许多机制细节源自前临床模型（小鼠），人类证据多为间接支持（如FMT后的免疫重塑观察）。代谢物水平的因果关系在人类中尚未完全确立，需注意区分观察性关联与因果证据。\",\"contribution\":\"详细阐述了微生物组影响ICI疗效的生物学机制框架，包括：1）通过促进树突状细胞激活和交叉呈递来增强CD8+ T细胞反应；2）通过短链脂肪酸等代谢物调节先天免疫编程和炎症基调；3）通过维持肠道屏障完整性来减少系统性炎症和irAEs风险。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d86b2c26e65d14b0a2de91e0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"讨论了基线生态、共用药（抗生素、PPI、激素）、饮食和定植率对干预结果的影响。强调了‘生态药理学’概念，即干预不是简单的药物添加，而是生态扰动。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8449be79b3a7045e41c5dacb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"提到了耐药大肠杆菌血症、产志贺毒素大肠杆菌以及SARS-CoV-2传播的案例，强调了供体筛查和制造控制的重要性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5c4718a22ebccf62e6d86dfd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该论文主要关注实体瘤（黑色素瘤、肾细胞癌、NSCLC），其结论不一定适用于血液肿瘤或其他癌症类型。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::434f935a5128024bbc9228db\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的‘强概念验证’仅限于抗PD-1难治性黑色素瘤中的FMT，不应过度推广到其他干预模式或肿瘤类型。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::736f594938f6aedd75c4d1dd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"机制部分混合了前临床模型和人类观察数据，需明确区分哪些是已证实的人类因果机制，哪些是基于模型的推测。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b0fe5dc8f31ddf0d2f44a79a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"临床试验结果多为早期阶段（Phase 1/Ib），效力结论往往受限（如SER-401试验），解读时需强调其探索性质。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e325d70a97f845ed6b9630a4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0178\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s010\",\"s039\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9ffb961f33f663bbe3d8758c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"structured_partial\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::39e0ed7f8bbe7249a0cc470d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d1619fdda7516b77df89edca\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用叙事性综述方法，综合了来自临床前研究（动物模型、体外实验）和临床研究（人类队列、病例报告、准实验研究）的证据。作者并未进行系统性的文献检索或定量荟萃分析，而是基于已有文献对微生物组组成、代谢产物、免疫细胞互作以及各类干预手段的效果进行定性描述和机制解释。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c52075ce0089f1f796870060\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"系统梳理了肠道微生物组影响CRC免疫治疗响应的多种机制路径（包括代谢物、免疫细胞招募、屏障功能等），并汇总了益生菌、FMT、饮食及中药等多种干预手段的临床前和部分临床证据。\",\"limits\":\"作为叙事性综述，未进行系统性文献检索或偏倚风险评估；结论受限于所引用研究的异质性（样本量小、设计多样）；部分发现（如A. muciniphila的作用）存在矛盾；缺乏对干预措施直接比较的定量证据；安全性讨论主要基于个案或小规模试验，尚不足以确立常规临床应用的规范。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::84c41d1446ea2fd02ca22186\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"MSS/pMMR CRC模型及临床背景\",\"finding\":\"特定微生物群（如Akkermansia muciniphila, Bifidobacterium, Lactobacillus等）及其代谢产物（如短链脂肪酸SCFAs）可通过促进CD8+ T细胞浸润、抑制调节性T细胞（Tregs）和髓源性抑制细胞（MDSCs），增强抗PD-1/PD-L1疗法的疗效。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0bb6354b1ffa085e58316dd9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"不同菌株作用\",\"finding\":\"部分病原体（如Fusobacterium nucleatum, Porphyromonas gingivalis）通过诱导免疫抑制微环境降低ICIs疗效；而某些益生菌株（如L. paracasei sh2020）可增强抗CTLA-4疗法效果。A. muciniphila的作用存在争议，既有促癌报道也有抑癌报道，但与C. butyricum联用可协同增强疗效。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::eeec402edb49ca9e42b9e1d0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"FMT临床应用\",\"finding\":\"FMT联合ICIs在MSS转移性CRC的II期临床试验（RENMIN-215）中显示出改善生存率和可控的安全性，外周γδ2 T细胞水平升高与响应相关。但FMT存在供体筛选困难、耐药基因转移及感染风险等安全顾虑。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::85a176f85847c29434a827f6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"其他干预手段\",\"finding\":\"中药复方（如清解胶囊、葛根芩连汤）和膳食纤维饮食可调节菌群结构，增加有益菌丰度，抑制肿瘤生长；工程化益生菌和纳米技术递送系统展示了克服免疫耐药的潜力。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c8766415c71f1b0aa83a51c7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::82c1049c351f6660caa30818\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"解决ICIs在大多数结直肠癌患者（尤其是MSS/pMMR型）中疗效有限的问题，探索如何通过调节肠道微生物组来克服免疫治疗耐药性，并识别相关的安全隐患。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::edd6329a6caa52f247dce0af\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"结直肠癌（CRC）患者，特别是微卫星稳定/错配修复 proficient (MSS/pMMR) 亚型；聚焦肠道微生物组对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）疗效的影响及基于微生物组的干预策略。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3e4a05237cb42d6954c814b0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"这是一篇叙事性综述，旨在总结肠道微生物组在结直肠癌发生、发展及免疫治疗反应中的作用机制，并评估益生菌、粪菌移植（FMT）、饮食调节和传统药物等微生物组干预措施作为ICIs辅助治疗的潜力与安全性。文章指出，尽管微生物组调控在临床前模型中显示出增强抗肿瘤免疫的潜力，但现有证据存在不一致性且缺乏大规模临床试验支持，因此强调需要标准化的方法和更严谨的临床验证。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::10989374a21315d00fde5aba\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为理解肠道微生物组如何调节实体瘤（特别是结直肠癌）中的免疫检查点抑制剂疗效提供了详细的机制框架和干预手段清单。它特别强调了MSS/pMMR这一难治亚型的微生物组特征，并区分了不同微生物群（有益菌vs病原体）对免疫微环境的相反作用。对于综述而言，其价值在于整合了从分子机制到临床转化的多层次证据，并指出了当前领域的不一致性和安全挑战，可作为构建“微生物组-免疫治疗”相互作用章节的重要背景素材和机制解释来源。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ebd11b917309870a1c077e6e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"证据主要来自小鼠模型和小规模人类研究，缺乏大规模随机对照试验的直接因果证明；不同研究间结果存在冲突（如A. muciniphila）。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物组影响ICIs疗效的具体微生物物种（如Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium, Lactobacillus, Fusobacterium）及其在MSS/pMMR CRC中的临床前和初步临床证据。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5a7b7c989be4d1458c33014d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"多数机制细节源自动物模型或体外实验，在人体内的确切适用性需结合具体临床数据验证；不同机制可能在不同患者亚群中主导作用不同。\",\"contribution\":\"详细阐述了微生物组调节免疫反应的机制，包括：1) 代谢物介导（SCFAs, 4-HPA, 胆汁酸）；2) 免疫细胞招募与极化（CD8+ T cells, DCs, M1/M2 macrophages）；3) 炎症通路激活（TLR4, NF-κB）；4) 屏障功能维持。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9f19d718b8beb25ba0a72627\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"临床证据等级参差不齐，多为II期试验、病例报告或准实验研究；缺乏长期安全性和标准化方案的数据。\",\"contribution\":\"总结了非抗生素类微生物组干预策略（益生菌、FMT、饮食、中药）在增强ICIs疗效方面的潜在应用和现状。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::84acd6806e0eec333e74652d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"MSS/pMMR CRC对ICIs天然耐药的特征，以及肠道微生物组作为关键影响因素的背景介绍。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e018458bdb969bec348e179c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"肿瘤微环境中微生物生态位（microniches）的概念，以及微生物-宿主-免疫系统三角关系的图示化描述。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4ae3f21e24e49d1344657963\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Akkermansia muciniphila在CRC中既被报道促癌又被报道抑癌的矛盾发现。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::64c10cff9d71226f6df3ca15\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"FMT在临床应用中面临的供体筛选、耐药基因转移和感染风险等安全挑战。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::264cce889a5056e1b23ca71b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"本文是叙事性综述，非系统性综述，其结论反映作者对现有文献的选择性解读，可能存在发表偏倚或选择偏倚。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::43b95aac20cf5e0952d064de\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中引用的许多机制证据来自动物模型（小鼠），不能直接外推至人类患者的全部生理病理过程。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bc41e0e7d6ac4add9ec6afd1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"关于特定益生菌株（如A. muciniphila）的作用存在相互矛盾的文献，需谨慎对待单一方向的概括。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b4fcee3819520eb2e476d1c2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"临床干预效果多基于小规模研究或观察性数据，尚未形成标准治疗方案，不应视为已证实的常规临床指南。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::755083fdbe007a675d60e15b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0439\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"html\",\"reason\":\"html_not_scholarly_body\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"html\",\"known_losses\":[\"headings/tables/math/image pixels are not preserved by this plain HTML projection\"],\"reason\":\"body converted to structured material; headings/tables/math/image pixels may be lost\",\"status\":\"derived\"},{\"kind\":\"html\",\"reason\":\"html_not_scholarly_body\",\"status\":\"partial\"}],\"material_scope\":\"structured_partial\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s001\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::47320b778a94a3f6e1bba0ee\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s061\",\"s286\",\"s214\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5b9018b036f8b7172a084833\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s061\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s214\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::eab85e6bee9c4b2fed5a5534\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the impact of gut microbiota/metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction followed STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: mechanisms of ICIs, heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, microbial metabolites as mediators, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and microbiome-based interventions.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e2c9835b96f8fc6dc09ac52b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut taxa and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, highlighting context-dependent biomarkers rather than universal signatures.\",\"limits\":\"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review does not establish causal relationships for all proposed mechanisms due to observational data dominance.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4f4f27ebf49eb4765b4072a3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Anti-CTLA-4 therapy; Melanoma patients and mouse models\",\"finding\":\"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for therapeutic efficacy via Th1 responses and dendritic cell activation.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a1803946bf15951d555dd21c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Metastatic melanoma patients\",\"finding\":\"Responders exhibit higher alpha-diversity and enrichment of Faecalibacterium and Ruminococcaceae; however, only a fraction of human taxa successfully colonize murine models.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0698d1c77cb0d200e790e2f0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Advanced NSCLC patients\",\"finding\":\"Relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila is prognostic; low abundance (<4.8%) correlates with superior overall survival compared to high abundance, challenging the binary 'good/bad' bacteria concept.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::633e7982644fd55dc1491f2b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Various ICI regimens; Preclinical and clinical cohorts\",\"finding\":\"Microbial influence is context-dependent: Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes associations with irAE risk invert across cancer types (protective in melanoma but linked to severe colitis in hepatobiliary malignancies).\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7401efb4116390e74b3c0d15\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Mechanistic pathways; In vivo and in vitro models\",\"finding\":\"Specific microbes enhance efficacy via distinct pathways: LGG and B. fragilis activate cGAS-STING; Enterococcus expresses SagA to activate NOD2; Alistipes finegoldii uses CXCL16-CXCR6 axis. Metabolites like SCFAs and indoles protect against toxicity via AhR/PPARα/NF-κB modulation.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c4c101d96abe914328c6abdc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s061\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s214\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5e3f0657dbc810fb682a25e8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"To systematically characterize the complex interplay between the gut microbiome, its metabolome, and ICI outcomes (efficacy and toxicity), addressing the clinical heterogeneity in patient responses and the lack of reproducible predictive models or intervention strategies.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f3675d08d336269e9d5f7b86\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome (specific taxa and metabolites) and the efficacy/toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), including PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 targets. It covers preclinical mechanistic studies and early-phase clinical trials across various solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, gastric/colorectal cancer).\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1bc1f290c28d78622ffb8469\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and their metabolic byproducts regulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It delineates specific microbial taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::487a265dc168c8a0c9af82f3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"This review offers a structured framework for understanding how gut microbiota and metabolites modulate ICI efficacy and toxicity in solid tumors. It provides detailed mechanistic insights into specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO), along with an evaluation of clinical interventions like FMT and probiotics. It is particularly useful for mapping mechanistic pathways and identifying context-dependent biomarkers, while cautioning against universal generalizations due to cohort and methodological heterogeneity.\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e4fe0aec77d9cea7ccfbcb3b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Associations are often based on small cohorts or preclinical models. The review explicitly notes that findings are not universally reproducible and depend heavily on study methodology and cohort characteristics.\",\"contribution\":\"Identifies specific microbial taxa associated with ICI response across different cancer types and ICI regimens (e.g., Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1, Akkermansia abundance levels for NSCLC). Highlights that microbial roles are context-dependent and vary by tumor type and host factors.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bee8d56ffb923bd61271c4b9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or in vitro studies. Human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are often undefined. The review cautions that these mechanisms may not directly translate to clinical efficacy without further validation.\",\"contribution\":\"Details molecular mechanisms by which microbes and metabolites modulate immunity: cGAS-STING activation by LGG and B. fragilis; NOD2 activation by Enterococcus; AhR-mediated barrier protection and cardiotoxicity mitigation by indoles and SCFAs; PERK-GSDME pyroptosis induction by TMAO.\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2653a9eca08d3e9b4aabdd40\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Overview of CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 mechanisms, and the clinical challenge of interpatient heterogeneity and irAEs.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6f7f1819fb2b6498ee2e73b4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Discussion of FMT trials (responder-derived vs. healthy donors), probiotic encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition strategies.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::246f46b2e4daa7c0826508a1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Critique of current study heterogeneity, sample processing issues, and the need for standardized multi-omics approaches.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::01a4eaf6f9130e6df88a4449\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The review emphasizes that microbial biomarkers are highly context-dependent (tumor type, ICI regimen, host genetics). Do not generalize findings from one cancer type (e.g., melanoma) to others (e.g., hepatobiliary) without considering this variability.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c302f1d1ebc15fb248ecf95b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models. Clinical translation is still in early phases (Phase I/II trials). Avoid overstating the clinical applicability of specific microbial interventions.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::297962d07c0123503e761a0c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide statistical meta-analyses or formal quality assessments. Treat the synthesized evidence as indicative rather than definitive proof of causality.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4677960f83a51b4866588b1e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"supplement_material\"],\"value\":{\"auxiliary_material\":\"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\",\"evidence\":[],\"gap_id\":\"case_E_phase3_rct\",\"judgment_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\"limitations\":[],\"material_ready\":true,\"material_usefulness\":\"supporting\",\"outline_action\":\"State that no completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in ICI-treated patients was identified in this material. Note that the study is a narrative review summarizing preclinical and early-phase (I/II) evidence. Highlight that the authors explicitly call for future large-scale randomized controlled trials to validate findings, confirming the absence of such completed Phase III data in the current literature reviewed.\",\"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"remaining_gap\":\"The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.\",\"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"status\":\"unmet\",\"useful_material\":\"The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s061\",\"s286\",\"s214\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::368f88790e7cd7be69d3482e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"supplement_materials\"],\"value\":[{\"auxiliary_material\":\"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\",\"evidence\":[],\"gap_id\":\"case_E_phase3_rct\",\"judgment_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\"limitations\":[],\"material_ready\":true,\"material_usefulness\":\"supporting\",\"outline_action\":\"State that no completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in ICI-treated patients was identified in this material. Note that the study is a narrative review summarizing preclinical and early-phase (I/II) evidence. Highlight that the authors explicitly call for future large-scale randomized controlled trials to validate findings, confirming the absence of such completed Phase III data in the current literature reviewed.\",\"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"remaining_gap\":\"The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.\",\"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"status\":\"unmet\",\"useful_material\":\"The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies.\"}],\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8d402e4e4dd606e12c0dadf8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-0c71639dc3330990d568\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-2c047b67f79872fa4042\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-2d4faf2da7bc361a24e6\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"kind\":\"assets\",\"reason\":\"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\"status\":\"missing\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::782ec3f7244d0ab076658c3c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science Core Collection, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the effects of gut microbiota or metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction was guided by STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: first covering ICI mechanisms, then the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, followed by specific metabolite classes, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and finally microbiome-based interventions.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d7e9648a9d3a228b80acd4f6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut microbes and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, categorizing interventions by their molecular targets (STING, NOD2, AhR, etc.).\",\"limits\":\"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review acknowledges significant methodological heterogeneity across studies and notes that many proposed biomarkers and interventions require validation in large-scale, standardized longitudinal studies.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f6e33ef85bc9029ac9138418\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Melanoma patients treated with anti-CTLA-4 (ipilimumab)\",\"finding\":\"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (e.g., B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for antitumor efficacy.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::69bf00aad7ea27d8d011a5f9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"NSCLC patients treated with anti-PD-1\",\"finding\":\"High relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila (Akk-high) was associated with worse overall survival compared to Akk-low groups, challenging the binary 'good vs bad' bacteria concept and highlighting cohort/cancer-type dependency.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d3b8e49c5165f6a25f200eab\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Various ICI regimens\",\"finding\":\"Microbial influence is context-dependent; different ICIs rely on distinct microbial signatures (e.g., Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1 vs. Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4).\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f5a2ef1b4e9581d3a710c521\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Tryptophan metabolites (3-IAld, IPA)\",\"finding\":\"3-IAld alleviates colitis and enhances efficacy via AhR/IL-22; IPA provides cardioprotection via AhR/PI3K/AKT signaling.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::361feac329a052a7d78f53b7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"SCFAs (Butyrate, Propionate, Acetate)\",\"finding\":\"Butyrate protects against cardiotoxicity via PPARa-CYP4X1 and enhances antigen presentation via HDAC inhibition; Propionate/Acetate promote Treg homeostasis and memory CD8+ T-cell differentiation.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::120f673d74db8c5732a0396e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"TMAO\",\"finding\":\"Triggers immunogenic tumor cell death (pyroptosis) via PERK-GSDME pathway, recruiting CD8+ T cells.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1b3cf17eff823e01454721f6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Probiotics (LGG, BF839, Akk)\",\"finding\":\"LGG and BF839 activate cGAS-STING axis in dendritic cells to enhance CD8+ T cell infiltration; Akk produces c-di-AMP which directly activates STING.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0b0761c9932abc9ab5a5874d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"FMT interventions\",\"finding\":\"FMT from long-term responders to PD-1 therapy showed higher efficacy than healthy donors; response correlated with loss of deleterious baseline species rather than just engraftment of donor strains.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6c7424e735d637988d2eced9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"The clinical utility of ICIs is limited by interpatient variability in efficacy and the occurrence of systemic toxicities (irAEs). The review aims to systematically delineate the microbiome-metabolite-immune axis to understand these variations and optimize the balance between therapeutic gain and toxicity, ultimately guiding the development of precise microbial interventions.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b70d300ebe4f7a632702a5f0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"The review focuses on the gut microbiome and its metabolic byproducts as systemic regulators of immune function, specifically in the context of cancer immunotherapy using immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It covers mechanisms of ICI action (PD-1/PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, TIM-3), the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions across different cancer types and cohorts, microbial metabolites (tryptophan derivatives, SCFAs, TMAO, inosine, bile acids, polyamines) as mediators of efficacy and toxicity, and microbiome-based interventions including probiotics, FMT, postbiotics, and dietary fiber.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e3b528b07174c7f2c4e9b9b5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and microbe-derived metabolites regulate the efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs) of ICIs. It highlights specific taxa like Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, and Akkermansia muciniphila that potentiate therapeutic responses via pathways such as cGAS-STING and NOD2. The review also details how microbial metabolites protect organs like the heart and colon from inflammation while enhancing anti-tumor immunity. It evaluates emerging interventions like FMT and next-generation probiotics, noting that while preclinical and Phase I trials show feasibility, substantial hurdles remain regarding cohort heterogeneity, methodological standardization, and the need for large-scale longitudinal studies to establish reproducible predictive models.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7a16470a938828a019a65473\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Critiques the reliance on single-taxa abundance, advocates for topology-based approaches, and highlights logistical barriers like metagenomic turnaround times for precision nutrition.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bf0ea10d71d03a741315fcbb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Describes FMT from responders vs. healthy donors, encapsulation technologies for probiotics, and the double-edged nature of antibiotic preconditioning and high-fiber diets.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0cebf65ae6c2fb3a2b3291c3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Findings are based on a synthesis of various studies with differing methodologies; causal relationships are often inferred from preclinical models or observational data rather than definitive clinical trials.\",\"contribution\":\"Details the context-dependent nature of microbiome-ICI interactions, showing that beneficial taxa vary by cancer type and ICI regimen (e.g., Bacteroides for CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium for PD-1, variable role of Akk). It also discusses the trade-off between efficacy and toxicity, noting that some microbes protective in one context may be detrimental in another.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a2d90e74ef12c1e1106eacf6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Many mechanisms are described from murine models or in vitro studies; human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are noted as undefined.\",\"contribution\":\"Provides specific molecular mechanisms linking microbes/metabolites to immune modulation. For example, it describes how LGG and BF839 activate the cGAS-STING pathway, how tryptophan metabolites act via AhR, and how SCFAs influence T-cell function and barrier integrity through epigenetic and receptor-mediated pathways.\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::86223da55d78e8184ad44dcf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"This review offers a structured framework for understanding the 'gut-metabolite-immune' axis in the context of solid tumor immunotherapy. It provides detailed mechanistic insights into how specific microbial taxa and metabolites modulate ICI efficacy and toxicity, serving as a valuable resource for explaining biological mechanisms and contextualizing clinical heterogeneity. It also summarizes the current state of microbiome-based interventions, highlighting both promising strategies and translational barriers.\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::74ec76742b9f6daf3762643e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide quantitative meta-analytic results; effect sizes and statistical significance should not be inferred from this text alone.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::995110f30544c2be6aece91c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models (mice) or small clinical cohorts; extrapolation to broader human populations requires caution.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b16eb73c69f940a7edbd13bf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The role of specific microbes (e.g., Akkermansia) can be context-dependent and even contradictory across studies; avoid treating any single taxon as universally beneficial or detrimental.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8d7b3fab2b1cb1884ae2d02d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Claims about the efficacy of interventions like FMT or probiotics are primarily based on early-phase trials or preclinical data; robust clinical validation is still needed.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::de02bcabb5761d1a2aab77da\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A_variants\"],\"value\":[{\"approach\":\"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the impact of gut microbiota/metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction followed STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: mechanisms of ICIs, heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, microbial metabolites as mediators, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and microbiome-based interventions.\",\"contribution_and_limits\":[{\"contribution\":\"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut taxa and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, highlighting context-dependent biomarkers rather than universal signatures.\",\"limits\":\"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review does not establish causal relationships for all proposed mechanisms due to observational data dominance.\"}],\"key_findings\":[{\"conditions\":\"Anti-CTLA-4 therapy; Melanoma patients and mouse models\",\"finding\":\"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for therapeutic efficacy via Th1 responses and dendritic cell activation.\"},{\"conditions\":\"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Metastatic melanoma patients\",\"finding\":\"Responders exhibit higher alpha-diversity and enrichment of Faecalibacterium and Ruminococcaceae; however, only a fraction of human taxa successfully colonize murine models.\"},{\"conditions\":\"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Advanced NSCLC patients\",\"finding\":\"Relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila is prognostic; low abundance (<4.8%) correlates with superior overall survival compared to high abundance, challenging the binary 'good/bad' bacteria concept.\"},{\"conditions\":\"Various ICI regimens; Preclinical and clinical cohorts\",\"finding\":\"Microbial influence is context-dependent: Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes associations with irAE risk invert across cancer types (protective in melanoma but linked to severe colitis in hepatobiliary malignancies).\"},{\"conditions\":\"Mechanistic pathways; In vivo and in vitro models\",\"finding\":\"Specific microbes enhance efficacy via distinct pathways: LGG and B. fragilis activate cGAS-STING; Enterococcus expresses SagA to activate NOD2; Alistipes finegoldii uses CXCL16-CXCR6 axis. Metabolites like SCFAs and indoles protect against toxicity via AhR/PPARα/NF-κB modulation.\"}],\"paper_kind\":\"review\",\"problem_or_question\":\"To systematically characterize the complex interplay between the gut microbiome, its metabolome, and ICI outcomes (efficacy and toxicity), addressing the clinical heterogeneity in patient responses and the lack of reproducible predictive models or intervention strategies.\",\"research_scope\":\"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome (specific taxa and metabolites) and the efficacy/toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), including PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 targets. It covers preclinical mechanistic studies and early-phase clinical trials across various solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, gastric/colorectal cancer).\",\"work_summary\":\"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and their metabolic byproducts regulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It delineates specific microbial taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\"}],\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1431bb03ae021761d8f92368\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B_variants\"],\"value\":[{\"broader_review_uses\":[{\"connection_to_review\":\"Sets the stage for why microbiome modulation is a critical area of research in overcoming ICI limitations.\",\"material\":\"Overview of CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 mechanisms, and the clinical challenge of interpatient heterogeneity and irAEs.\",\"purpose\":\"Contextual background on ICI mechanisms and limitations\"},{\"connection_to_review\":\"Provides evidence on the feasibility and challenges of translating microbiome science into clinical practice, highlighting the gap between preclinical success and clinical implementation.\",\"material\":\"Discussion of FMT trials (responder-derived vs. healthy donors), probiotic encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition strategies.\",\"purpose\":\"Evaluation of microbiome-based interventions\"},{\"connection_to_review\":\"Offers a critical perspective on the current state of the field, suggesting areas where future research needs to improve reproducibility and causal inference.\",\"material\":\"Critique of current study heterogeneity, sample processing issues, and the need for standardized multi-omics approaches.\",\"purpose\":\"Methodological considerations and future directions\"}],\"facet_contributions\":[{\"boundaries\":\"Associations are often based on small cohorts or preclinical models. The review explicitly notes that findings are not universally reproducible and depend heavily on study methodology and cohort characteristics.\",\"contribution\":\"Identifies specific microbial taxa associated with ICI response across different cancer types and ICI regimens (e.g., Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1, Akkermansia abundance levels for NSCLC). Highlights that microbial roles are context-dependent and vary by tumor type and host factors.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\",\"possible_uses\":\"Can be used to support arguments about the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions and the lack of a universal 'good' microbiome signature. Provides specific examples of taxa to discuss in the context of patient stratification.\"},{\"boundaries\":\"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or in vitro studies. Human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are often undefined. The review cautions that these mechanisms may not directly translate to clinical efficacy without further validation.\",\"contribution\":\"Details molecular mechanisms by which microbes and metabolites modulate immunity: cGAS-STING activation by LGG and B. fragilis; NOD2 activation by Enterococcus; AhR-mediated barrier protection and cardiotoxicity mitigation by indoles and SCFAs; PERK-GSDME pyroptosis induction by TMAO.\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\",\"possible_uses\":\"Provides mechanistic depth for explaining how the gut microbiome influences ICI efficacy and toxicity. Useful for discussing specific signaling pathways (STING, NOD2, AhR, NF-κB) and their role in remodeling the tumor microenvironment and protecting distal organs.\"}],\"planning_summary\":\"This review offers a structured framework for understanding how gut microbiota and metabolites modulate ICI efficacy and toxicity in solid tumors. It provides detailed mechanistic insights into specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO), along with an evaluation of clinical interventions like FMT and probiotics. It is particularly useful for mapping mechanistic pathways and identifying context-dependent biomarkers, while cautioning against universal generalizations due to cohort and methodological heterogeneity.\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\":[\"The review emphasizes that microbial biomarkers are highly context-dependent (tumor type, ICI regimen, host genetics). Do not generalize findings from one cancer type (e.g., melanoma) to others (e.g., hepatobiliary) without considering this variability.\",\"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models. Clinical translation is still in early phases (Phase I/II trials). Avoid overstating the clinical applicability of specific microbial interventions.\",\"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide statistical meta-analyses or formal quality assessments. Treat the synthesized evidence as indicative rather than definitive proof of causality.\"],\"topic_handles\":[\"gut microbiome composition and diversity\",\"immune checkpoint inhibitors (PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT)\",\"microbial metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO, bile acids)\",\"immune-related adverse events (irAEs)\",\"fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT)\",\"probiotics and postbiotics\",\"precision nutrition and dietary fiber\",\"cGAS-STING pathway\",\"NOD2 signaling\",\"aryl hydrocarbon receptor (AhR)\"]}],\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bd2a31924b2f1b7a5c0db505\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2088384ebad86f83dd115cc2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s060\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::182a456925359bd5e4cb6b24\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"local_passages\"],\"value\":{\"external_calls\":0,\"passages\":[{\"best_sentence\":\"The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed.\",\"card_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\"limits\":[],\"match_terms\":[\"粪菌移植\",\"益生菌\",\"机制\",\"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\",\"mechanisms mediate effect\",\"ici\",\"i\",\"ii\",\"iii\",\"nsclc\",\"rct\"],\"material_depth\":\"fulltext\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:290154100\",\"pool_action\":\"already_in_pool\",\"reading_path\":\"\",\"score\":120.720283,\"section_path\":[\"Supplementary question reading\"],\"segment_kind\":\"directed_content\",\"source_handle\":\"P0584\",\"text\":\"{\\\"auxiliary_material\\\": \\\"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": [], \\\"gap_id\\\": \\\"case_E_phase3_rct\\\", \\\"judgment_path\\\": \\\"F:\\\\\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\\\\\outputs\\\\\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\\\\\03_external_closure\\\\\\\\runs\\\\\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\\\\\source_units\\\\\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\\\", \\\"limitations\\\": [], \\\"material_ready\\\": true, \\\"material_usefulness\\\": \\\"suppor…\",\"title\":\"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"usable_fields\":[],\"year\":\"2026\"},{\"best_sentence\":\"The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\"card_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\"limits\":[],\"match_terms\":[\"粪菌移植\",\"益生菌\",\"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\"],\"material_depth\":\"fulltext\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:290154100\",\"pool_action\":\"already_in_pool\",\"reading_path\":\"\",\"score\":17.613751,\"section_path\":[\"general understanding\",\"work summary\"],\"segment_kind\":\"card_work_summary\",\"source_handle\":\"P0584\",\"text\":\"taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. m, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\"title\":\"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"usable_fields\":[],\"year\":\"2026\"}],\"question\":\"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect? 微生物干预策略的临床转化现状 系统评估粪菌移植（FMT）、活体生物药（LBPs）、益生菌及饮食干预在实体瘤 ICI 治疗中的临床试验数据，区分初治与难治人群的疗效差异，明确证据等级（I/II 期 vs III 期），并分析供体选择、安全性及标准化挑战。 涵盖人体临床试验（I-III 期），聚焦实体瘤（黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC、CRC 等）。包括 FMT（供体来源、给药途径）、定义菌群（如 CBM588、MRx0518）、益生菌及饮食干预。明确排除纯临床前研究（除非用于解释机制背景）及非 ICI 背景的微生物干预。严格区分观察性关联与干预性因果证据，标注试验设计类型（单臂 vs RCT）及人群特征（初治 vs 经治）。\",\"reading_mode\":\"focused_local_search\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d2eba37acde2103b14529835\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"abstract\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::04eaac683222de8ca9070df9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::06a06e3788b228f652f2234d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"这是一项前瞻性、跨机构的多中心转化研究。研究对象为接受新辅助治疗的早期乳腺癌、直肠癌或食管癌患者。排除标准包括既往同种异体组织/实体器官移植史及既往接受过抗癌治疗。数据采集包括在新辅助治疗前、完成后以及完成后六个月进行粪便采样。微生物组分析采用16S rRNA测序。病理反应在手术时评估，分为应答者（pCR）和非应答者。主要终点是检验GM多样性与病理反应的关联。探索性分析包括cf-DNA与GM多样性的关联，以及基线cf-DNA与pCR的关联。统计方法计划使用Shannon指数分析Alpha多样性，Jaccard相似性指数计算Beta多样性，并使用PCA和随机森林进行分类和聚类分析。主要终点的关联将通过调整潜在混杂因素的逻辑回归分析进行评估。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4335ab0b84254bb1619de1a5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了关于在爱尔兰特定医疗体系下开展大型多中心肿瘤-微生物组转化研究的可行性和方法论框架；确立了研究设计和预期分析路线。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代最终的研究结果、GM多样性与pCR之间的具体关联、任何机制解释或统计学显著性结论。由于研究尚未完成，无法评估其实际科学贡献或外部有效性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3b6b5d30ce92296b3fd3c4eb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"研究进行中，仅基于招募可行性验证\",\"finding\":\"证明了在爱尔兰开展此类转化研究的可行性，并优化了筛选和招募流程以提高招募数量。目前已招募14名患者。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::320fb9443b29f631a256d1d4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::41aeb07965852bce86ea4e11\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管已知肠道微生物组可能通过调节免疫通路影响宿主免疫及对免疫检查点抑制剂的反应，但关于GM多样性如何影响胃肠道和乳腺癌新辅助治疗后的病理完全缓解尚不清楚。本研究旨在解决这一知识空白。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ff38897831fd6a0ec9f1ff49\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"爱尔兰多中心前瞻性转化研究，针对早期乳腺癌、直肠癌和食管癌患者，在开始新辅助治疗（化疗、免疫治疗或放化疗）前及治疗后不同时间点收集粪便样本。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f72f8d50d6728b9c9231a8ea\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文介绍了一项正在进行的爱尔兰多中心转化研究，旨在探讨基线肠道微生物组（GM）多样性与新辅助治疗后病理完全缓解（pCR）之间的关联。研究假设基线GM多样性更高将导致更好的病理反应。目前招募仍在进行中，已纳入14名患者，预计2025年初得出结果。摘要主要描述了研究设计、可行性验证及初步招募情况，未提供最终的统计分析结果或发现。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d98bcf3fa54abee781c2fe1a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该材料为一项正在进行中的研究摘要，主要价值在于其研究设计的描述和可行性报告，而非实证结果。对于综述而言，它提供了关于“肠道微生物组多样性”与“实体瘤新辅助治疗反应”之间关联的研究背景和方法论参考，特别是涉及爱尔兰人群的数据收集策略。由于缺乏具体发现，它不能直接回答F1或F2的具体机制或效应大小问题，但可作为背景信息说明该领域正在进行的努力和研究缺口。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c4920cf42f919cbcc228f58e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"该研究尚未提供结果，因此不能用于支持或反驳GM多样性对疗效的影响。仅能作为“正在进行的研究”或“研究缺口”的背景提及。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了关于肠道微生物组多样性与实体瘤新辅助治疗反应之间关联的研究背景和待检验假设。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1c4d84fb7c3a7fd7ceb4eed5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"摘要仅提到GM可能通过调节免疫通路影响宿主免疫，但未在本研究中验证具体机制。\",\"contribution\":\"未提供具体的机制证据。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c317d477bfa68247450db74d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"研究设计细节：多中心、前瞻性、爱尔兰人群、16S rRNA测序、Shannon/Jaccard指数、逻辑回归分析。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a2d7c14d865c1772f5c9db60\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"摘要明确指出“little is known about how the GM diversity influences complete pathological response”，且研究预计2025年出结果。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::05743daab7f9a70950e809cd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该论文仅为研究方案/进展报告，无最终结果。切勿将其假设或计划当作已证实的发现。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::28f4868d4c01ef55c8555742\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"研究人群限定为爱尔兰早期乳腺癌、直肠癌和食管癌患者，结果外推需谨慎。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4de22e3bb2306b19cff594fe\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"研究关注的是“多样性”而非特定菌群组成，这与某些关注特定菌属的研究不同。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2df6782f572a20b2e37854aa\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"新辅助治疗类型多样（化疗、免疫治疗、放化疗），结果可能因治疗方式而异，需区分看待。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a13e11aec07c79c3b5d5ac28\",\"source_handle\":\"P0045\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"identity\",\"reason\":\"source identity was not independently verified\",\"status\":\"input_attributed\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"no complete research body was indexed\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\"status\":\"partial\"}],\"material_scope\":\"abstract_only\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s206\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a19c959f8a2acc29636f119b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7b89231969a054b4a89c2a48\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c823cde6fd7be8f3503cb7e3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"系统性文献回顾。作者检索了EMBASE、Web of Science、MEDLINE等数据库，关键词包括(gut microbiota OR gut microbiome) AND (cancer OR oncology) AND (paediatric OR children)。文章结构上先介绍一般背景，再分章节讨论致癌机制、全身治疗相互作用、儿科特异性（发病率、治疗诱导的变化、急慢性并发症）、干预措施，最后总结局限性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::304fdc7a467cbc5937eb2a85\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"系统梳理了儿科肿瘤中微生物组研究的现状，特别区分了血液恶性肿瘤和实体瘤的证据差异。\",\"limits\":\"主要基于观察性研究和小型试点研究，缺乏大规模前瞻性试验；无法确立因果关系（是原因还是结果）；实体瘤数据极度匮乏。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::31af98e275ea3928cfba54b1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提出了微生物组作为预测生物标志物和个性化治疗靶点的潜力。\",\"limits\":\"目前尚无标准化的干预方案（如益生菌、FMT）在儿科肿瘤中的确切疗效和安全性数据，部分干预存在潜在风险（如菌血症）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ff2cfcc604793b53a9d59566\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"成人免疫检查点抑制剂治疗\",\"finding\":\"抗生素使用可能降低免疫治疗反应；Akkermansia muciniphila丰度高的患者预后更好。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e426c7e2e3a8cb7610cfe635\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"儿童急性淋巴细胞白血病(ALL)\",\"finding\":\"诊断时粪便DNA含量较低；双歧杆菌、乳酸杆菌丰度降低；化疗后微生物多样性显著下降，恢复缓慢。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3b249c424838c10c3f3f76f3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"儿童实体瘤（横纹肌肉瘤）\",\"finding\":\"小样本研究显示，治疗前微生物多样性较低的患者对放化疗反应较好，但结论受限于样本量。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::46682478facb5aaa26af0904\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"化疗副作用\",\"finding\":\"特定菌群（如肠球菌科、链球菌科）的高丰度与中性粒细胞发热、腹泻等急性并发症相关；Faecalibacterium减少可能与长期肥胖和代谢综合征风险相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f6196f1a51bb8d17a7355dca\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9a8c8c84055f2f5ec45e2efd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管成人研究中微生物组对肿瘤免疫治疗的影响已较明确，但在儿科人群中，由于病例数少和治疗复杂，其具体作用、对疗效的影响机制以及对副作用的贡献仍不清楚。本文旨在梳理现有文献，填补这一知识空白。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5698c6861547b14b692a5ea1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"儿科肿瘤（特别是急性淋巴细胞白血病和实体瘤）与肠道微生物组的关系，涵盖发病机制、治疗反应及副作用。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fa48e8593af165fb2b6abbf5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"这是一篇2022年的综述文章，旨在总结肠道微生物组在儿科肿瘤发生和治疗中的最新研究进展。文章首先概述了微生物组的一般生理作用及其通过免疫调节影响癌症的机制，随后重点讨论了儿科特异性，包括分娩方式、喂养方式对微生物组的影响，以及化疗和放疗引起的微生物组变化。研究发现，微生物组的变化与治疗反应和毒性相关，但目前证据多来自成人或小型儿科队列，且因果关系尚不明确。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::27021dceb70692ec254a2259\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述提供了儿科肿瘤中微生物组作用的宏观背景和具体临床关联素材。虽然它不直接回答“机制”层面的分子细节（这是其局限），但它提供了关键的临床表型关联（如菌群变化与疗效/毒性的相关性）、不同肿瘤类型的证据强度对比（ALL vs 实体瘤），以及关于抗生素使用对免疫治疗影响的成人证据外推提示。对于综述而言，它是构建“儿科特异性”章节和讨论“当前证据局限性”的重要基础材料。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::16e154198afee70b84b0d829\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"该综述明确指出儿科实体瘤数据极少，且多数关联未证实因果。不能将此视为儿科ICIs疗效的确切机制解释，仅作为假设生成的来源。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了儿科肿瘤中微生物组与治疗反应关联的临床观察数据。例如，指出ALL患者化疗后多样性降低，且某些菌群丰度变化与疗效相关（尽管主要是描述性关联）。同时引用了成人研究中Akkermansia与ICIs疗效正相关的证据，为儿科可能的类似机制提供类比支持。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9bda68f2ddae3b446d9d8f89\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这些机制大多基于成人模型或体外研究，儿科特异性验证不足。综述本身未提供新的机制实验数据，而是汇总现有理论。\",\"contribution\":\"概述了微生物组影响治疗的潜在生物学途径，包括：1）细菌酶解药物代谢（如伊立替康）；2）免疫调节（如双歧杆菌促进T细胞反应）；3）屏障损伤导致细菌易位引发炎症。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::28d3e1b6a2d3d74bf0d52e22\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"提到儿科病例数少、治疗复杂（联合化疗/放疗/抗生素）、样本收集困难，导致高质量研究稀缺。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::eb54daf7521fc7faadeaef52\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"剖宫产增加ALL风险，母乳喂养降低ALL风险，涉及微生物组建立的关键窗口期。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e496368c2da663bee84e959f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"提及益生菌可能导致造血干细胞移植患儿菌血症，FMT在儿童中的应用尚不成熟。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::dde97d1799340db7c2a03104\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述主要关注儿科，但其引用的关键机制（如ICIs疗效）多基于成人研究，使用时需明确区分人群差异，避免直接将成人结论套用于儿科。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6253ea41b94d1e85c041082c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的许多关联（如菌群与毒性）多为观察性结果，不能推断为因果关系。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8d8cc5c422e1531f2b8f99c1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"对于实体瘤部分，证据非常薄弱，仅有个案或小样本报告，不应过度解读其普遍性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::73000960b882ef64134393a6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0008\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s211\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::48b1ccff373340eac78f8870\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f5e29d134f6ae2f02fed940a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fe8a34ad7e972c4f4e598847\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用单臂、前瞻性、II期临床试验设计。纳入标准为BCLC A–B期HCC、ECOG评分0–1、器官功能良好且在TACE后2周及MWA后1周影像学评估均达到mRECIST完全缓解的患者。排除既往接受过其他免疫调节剂、存在活动性感染或严重合并症者。所有患者在接受TACE和MWA后2周内开始接受特瑞普利单抗治疗，持续6个月。随访直至复发、死亡或研究结束。统计分析计划包括Kaplan-Meier估计RFS和OS，Cox比例风险模型计算HR，以及描述性统计次要终点。样本量计算基于历史数据预期中位RFS从15.5个月提升至27个月（HR=0.57），需30名参与者以检测显著差异。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b75b6c531806168ee3c5a352\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了针对特定亚群（BCLC A–B期，TACE+MWA后CR）的辅助免疫治疗标准化方案细节，包括药物剂量、疗程（6个月短程）、评估时间点及安全性监测流程。\",\"limits\":\"作为方案文件，缺乏实际临床结局数据；单臂设计无法提供因果推断证据，依赖外部历史数据进行比较；样本量较小（n=30），可能限制对罕见不良反应的检测能力及结果的普遍适用性；随访时间较短，无法评估长期“尾部效应”。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f516c5d011fc341d938ec983\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"当前材料为临床试验方案阶段\",\"finding\":\"所给摘要未交代实际疗效数据、安全性结果或统计学结论。文中仅包含基于历史数据的预期结果（如预期RFS改善）和研究设计的理论依据。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0f17851423c5158ded11696c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"methods\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6ac9ad2bebc7059ddafc25a8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"针对早期至中期HCC患者在接受TACE联合MWA等根治性局部治疗后面临高复发率（5年内高达70%）且缺乏标准化辅助治疗的问题，探究短程辅助PD-1抑制剂（特瑞普利单抗）是否能有效降低复发风险并改善预后，同时评估其安全性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2c32d64fd11413e8e7d895d8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"研究对象为巴塞罗那肝癌临床分期（BCLC）A–B期肝细胞癌（HCC）患者；情境为经动脉化疗栓塞（TACE）联合微波消融（MWA）局部治疗后达到完全缓解（CR）的高复发风险人群；范围聚焦于评估短期辅助免疫检查点抑制剂（特瑞普利单抗/Tislelizumab）的疗效与安全性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8830c3ef754ce06dd585ec36\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇单臂、前瞻性、II期临床试验方案，旨在评估在TACE联合MWA治疗BCLC A–B期HCC并确认完全缓解后，使用6个月短程辅助特瑞普利单抗（200 mg，每3周一次）的疗效和安全性。研究主要终点为无复发生存期（RFS），次要终点包括局部肿瘤进展、肝内远处复发、肝外疾病时间、总生存期及不良事件。该研究基于TACE诱导免疫原性细胞死亡与MWA协同作用产生有利免疫微环境的理论假设，试图验证短程辅助免疫治疗的可行性。由于这是一份试验方案（Protocol），目前尚未报告实际的患者入组数据或最终结果。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a62f5b9e638b3cf768bce014\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文作为临床试验方案，虽无结果数据，但详细定义了“介入治疗（TACE/MWA）+ 辅助免疫”这一特定干预组合的操作规范、患者筛选标准及评估体系。对于综述而言，其价值在于明确该联合疗法的具体实施路径、潜在的理论机制（免疫原性细胞死亡与抗原释放）以及当前证据等级的局限性（单臂、小样本、无对照）。可用于说明该领域正在进行的探索方向及现有证据的缺口。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7b77312891d3e4cc2ea696c0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"仅提供方案设定，不提供疗效对比数据；不能证明该方案优于其他方案或观察性研究中的效果。\",\"contribution\":\"明确了TACE联合MWA后辅助使用PD-1抑制剂的具体给药方案（特瑞普利单抗 200mg q3w x 6个月）及适用人群（BCLC A-B, CR状态）。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0a3f8d22a54c5b8ceceaa816\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这是基于文献引用的理论机制阐述，而非本研究实测的机制数据；不同介入方式（如RFA vs MWA）的效果可能存在差异，需注意外推限制。\",\"contribution\":\"阐述了TACE和MWA通过诱导缺血、化疗毒性及热损伤导致免疫原性细胞死亡，释放肿瘤新抗原，从而重塑肿瘤免疫微环境并增强T细胞反应的机制假设。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0c606f0b8f28a6531283f01e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文中指出目前尚无标准化的辅助治疗方案，IMbrave050等III期研究结果存在长期获益不维持的情况，且多数研究聚焦于手术切除而非消融/介入治疗后的辅助治疗。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c09f082a0637e3742ebb9436\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文中提到近期研究表明6个月的维持免疫治疗可提供与连续治疗相当的疗效，同时具有良好的安全性和依从性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::dc42c1b1a9a199905719b905\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该研究为单臂试验方案，无对照组，因此任何关于疗效的声称均为预期值或基于历史数据的推测，不能作为确证性证据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1d752c6ac999e16ec53adf54\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"研究对象限定为BCLC A-B期且经TACE+MWA达到CR的患者，结果不可直接外推至其他分期、其他局部治疗方式（如单纯TACE或RFA）或未达CR的患者。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::03c28017ae4db0bbc863d9c7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"机制部分主要引用自其他研究，本研究本身未进行生物标志物或机制层面的实证分析。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2a0bc2e4ae20db7e5e41da89\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"所给材料未交代实际入组进度、脱落情况及最终安全性数据，无法评估真实世界的耐受性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::142a0121960c84ba03086ed3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0030\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-4dcc7c19ae5301df5638\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-24f387f49005f46578a2\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"missing\"},{\"kind\":\"assets\",\"reason\":\"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\"status\":\"missing\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s183\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fa917863b42b865823617a1e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"abstract\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4f68bc3c0e51d3eab948fccf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ad5a28fe0d2f3d68b7b8e60f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"1. 数据收集：使用公开可用的418名NSCLC患者基线肠道微生物组物种谱数据。2. 模型构建：训练机器学习模型预测ICI响应（R vs NR），固定参数，在保留测试集上验证（AUC=0.62，OS曲线差异显著p<0.0001）。3. 筛选子集：聚焦于模型预测价值良好的257名患者。4. 模拟干预：在模型中模拟健康供体FMT和治疗性菌群组合添加到患者基线微生物组中的过程，考察不同定植比例（exposure-dependent）对预测响应概率的影响。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8dd8758eb8f26ba40de0493c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了一个基于基线微生物组预测ICI响应的机器学习框架，并证实了在特定患者亚群中，通过模拟FMT或定制菌群可提升预测响应率。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代具体的机器学习算法类型、特征选择细节、治疗性菌群的具体组成成分、菌株分离的具体进展以及临床转化的时间表。仅基于回顾性数据的模拟，非前瞻性临床试验结果。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::89e7cfb984cc8f88cb8a9ce6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"基于418名NSCLC患者数据的机器学习模型，在从未见过的测试集上\",\"finding\":\"模型平均AUC为0.62，能显著区分总生存期（OS）曲线（p<0.0001）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::93a5dccbe3d93c3c7257faa4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"在模型预测价值良好的257名患者子集中，模拟健康供体FMT添加\",\"finding\":\"FMT提高了模型预测的响应率，且效果依赖于暴露量（即FMT物种定植并替换患者基线微生物组的比例）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a54ca17131fe904ae7af49e9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"在相同子集中，模拟候选治疗性菌群组合添加\",\"finding\":\"候选治疗性菌群组合同样提高了响应率，且结果也呈现剂量/定植依赖性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::679f65a7a246700078865033\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b5b1d19764f6694dbdc7af78\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"现有研究中单个微生物物种与ICI响应的关联往往不可重复且统计效力不足；虽然FMT显示有益，但药物开发多集中于简单菌群组合。本研究试图在模型中复制FMT的治疗益处，并设计能够增强ICI响应的治疗性微生物组合。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ae8542404f12e8b138fd3320\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"基于418名非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者的基线肠道微生物组数据，构建机器学习模型以预测免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）的响应情况；并在模拟环境中评估粪菌移植（FMT）及设计型活细菌疗法对ICI疗效的影响。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4ae34442850db6176f0dc26c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"该研究旨在解决个体微生物物种与ICI响应关联缺乏统计稳健性的问题，并探索通过微生物组干预改善ICI疗效的策略。作者利用418名NSCLC患者的基线微生物组数据训练了一个区分响应者（R）与非响应者（NR）的机器学习模型（AUC=0.62）。随后，在具有良好预测价值的子集（n=257）中，通过模拟实验评估了健康供体FMT和自定义治疗性菌群组合的效果。结果显示，增加FMT或治疗性菌群的定植比例可依赖性地提高模型预测的响应率。结论认为这些候选疗法有潜力改善ICI患者响应，目前正进行菌株分离培养以开发联合疗法。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::52690f071bd7b697f8226c7c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文提供了关于“微生物组介导ICI疗效”的一个具体计算生物学视角。它不侧重于单一机制的发现，而是提供了一个从微生物组特征到临床响应预测的建模流程，并展示了通过恢复“响应者样”微生物组特征（通过FMT或合成菌群）来改善预后的概念验证。这对于综述中讨论“如何通过调节微生物组增强ICI疗效”以及“预测生物标志物的开发”部分具有直接参考价值。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8ac1b1eac700149a344ed443\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"模型性能中等（AUC 0.62），且仅在NSCLC队列中验证，外推至其他实体瘤需谨慎。所给摘要未交代模型的可解释性（即哪些具体菌群驱动了预测）。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了基于全谱微生物组而非单一物种的ICI响应预测模型构建方法，并量化了模型性能（AUC 0.62）。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a23aef9604c65bbc592eb585\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这是基于计算机模拟的结果，非体内或体外实验验证。所给摘要未交代具体的分子机制（如抗原呈递、炎症调节等），仅停留在表型预测层面。\",\"contribution\":\"提出了通过“恢复响应者样微生物组特征”来克服ICI无响应的设计策略，并通过模拟证明了FMT和定制菌群的潜在有效性。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9427443eb0fa7c8aa3845ea9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"418名NSCLC患者的基线微生物组数据及其与ICI响应的统计关联分析。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::caf5e2a920fd8e6427e41f2c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"候选治疗性菌群的设计逻辑（围绕供体FMT和ICI响应相关物种及机制）及菌株分离培养的进展。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::107cddc181c0ebe6140204b3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该研究仅为摘要级别，所有关于“治疗性菌群”的具体成分、作用机制及临床前/临床数据均未知，不得推断其具体功效或安全性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::32be3241aa6be5e4aa9c6909\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"模型基于回顾性数据，模拟结果不代表真实临床疗效，需明确区分“预测模型中的响应率提升”与“实际患者生存获益”。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1b85f9454a1366e32d8300b8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"研究对象限定为NSCLC，其微生物组特征可能与其他实体瘤不同，跨癌种推广需谨慎。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4c5791d22681d874f3bce1ab\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"作者声称的“promise”为初步概念验证，尚处于菌株分离和培养阶段，距离实际应用仍有距离。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::674ce0ddf3f79ba2358a5d60\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"identity\",\"reason\":\"source identity was not independently verified\",\"status\":\"input_attributed\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"no complete research body was indexed\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\"status\":\"partial\"}],\"material_scope\":\"abstract_only\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f42355f065d836e3bfa3b47e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"abstract\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a5d09754fe44a730fc9e13b8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0cd9ce6812b543c46a2b0b3e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"文献综述与理论模型构建。作者通过总结现有文献中关于衰老相关微生物变化的研究，并结合已知的与ICIs响应相关的微生物标志物，进行对比分析。在此基础上，作者提出了一个概念性模型来解释观察到的广泛水平上的变化，并梳理了当前正在进行的针对老年群体的相关临床试验。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e6783c48b9261e1c8c710173\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了将衰老微生物组变化与ICIs疗效联系起来的综合视角，提出了衰老可能通过改变微生物组导致ICIs疗效降低的假设性机制框架。\",\"limits\":\"作为综述，其核心贡献在于总结和提出模型，而非提供新的实验证据或因果验证。所提出的机制和模型需要后续研究验证。材料未提供具体的微生物菌株列表或详细的分子机制细节，仅概括为“潜在机制”。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::723be181544673725c3485d9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"基于现有文献的综合分析\",\"finding\":\"衰老相关的微生物组变化倾向于使微生物组组成向“无响应者”样状态偏移，即缺乏那些被证明能支持治疗反应的微生物。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3af563cf55f97e70ec3fc77a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"临床背景\",\"finding\":\"在导致治疗批准的临床试验中，老年患者的代表性不足，尽管他们在癌症人群中不断增长且是 understudied 群体。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8fc2629fed14aefc065b8a36\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::dfb23f0ab88414ec82177b23\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"随着人口老龄化，老年癌症患者在接受新兴的免疫疗法时往往缺乏代表性数据。已知衰老会导致微生物组发生已知转变，但这些转变如何影响ICIs疗效？特别是，衰老引起的微生物组变化是否导致了该人群疗效降低？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::dba6e9c1035507d6509ff592\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"老年癌症患者、肠道微生物组、免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）疗效\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4270f4bc1c3973a0df4a4095\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇综述，旨在探讨肠道微生物组随年龄变化的特征及其对老年癌症患者接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）治疗反应的影响。文章总结了与衰老相关的微生物变化文献，并将其置于ICIs疗效的背景下进行解读，提出了一种解释这些广泛变化的模型，并讨论了针对这一未被充分研究人群的临床试验现状。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::70a25591cd37a6e5c9bad9d7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为理解老年癌症患者ICIs疗效差异提供了一个重要的微生物组学视角。它直接关联了“衰老”这一宿主因素与“微生物组”这一环境/共生因素，解释了为何老年人群可能对ICIs反应较差。对于综述而言，它是连接宿主年龄、微生物组构成与治疗结局的关键桥梁，特别适用于解释疗效异质性中的宿主-微生物交互作用部分。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3a12281019419049fa737cd8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这是基于文献总结的推论，非直接干预实验结果。未提供具体的微生物物种名称或丰度数据，无法用于定量预测。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了关于老年人群微生物组组成趋向于“无响应者”特征的定性描述。指出这种组成缺乏支持ICIs疗效的微生物，从而解释了该人群疗效降低的可能原因。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::09ea2d04b82d833ef20840b9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"摘要中称“review the potential mechanisms... and posit a model”，但未列出具体机制路径（如炎症、代谢产物等）。因此只能作为机制探索的指引，不能替代具体的机制证据。\",\"contribution\":\"回顾了衰老引起微生物组变化的潜在机制，并提出了一个解释这些变化的概念模型。虽然具体机制细节在摘要中未展开，但指出了方向：衰老导致的微生物组改变可能介导了疗效差异。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7a3447126c6e157188a24eb6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"指出老年人在ICIs获批临床试验中代表性不足，但该群体正在增长且未被充分研究。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::591ae31111114ee05e9b490d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"提到微生物组可作为区分ICIs响应者的生物标志物，且前体模型显示补充单一菌株或代谢物可改变治疗反应。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::898892fa672da4975217f7a8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"本文是综述性质，其“发现”是基于对已有文献的综合解读和模型构建，而非原始实验数据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b7941f28565f11c0bd8304cb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的“demonstrate that these age-related changes tend to shift...”是作者对文献趋势的总结性陈述，应视为一种合理的科学推断或假设框架，而非确凿的因果证据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::acb8875d49af6a65afcf6b3d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"未提供具体的微生物分类群或代谢物名称，使用时需结合其他提供具体菌株信息的论文。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e0b015fe0b4612ce34503aa7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"主要关注老年人群，结论外推到年轻人群时需格外谨慎。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::97c50b7b2f2680d78ead1ba2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0484\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"identity\",\"reason\":\"source identity was not independently verified\",\"status\":\"input_attributed\"},{\"kind\":\"html\",\"reason\":\"html_not_scholarly_body\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"html\",\"reason\":\"html_challenge_or_login\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"html\",\"reason\":\"html_challenge_or_login\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"html\",\"reason\":\"html_empty\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\"status\":\"partial\"}],\"material_scope\":\"abstract_plus_snippets\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s082\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5f1aaf404afa62661d66b17f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::624421c50bf0330615999b98\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::98aeff8a1cc25ec30c221b66\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"横断面意见调查（Survey）。设计包含Likert量表、多选题和开放式问题的问卷，覆盖特定临床情境。通过电子邮件和社交媒体分发，限制每个IP地址一次有效回答，并要求受访者具备一定临床经验（>20例ICI治疗NSCLC患者）以确保数据质量。使用描述性统计方法分析计数和百分比。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3a53d08ff4d0e3d27fa021a7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了关于ICI单药治疗NSCLC临床实践中主要知识空白的全球专家共识视图，特别是针对被排除在关键试验之外的患者亚群。\",\"limits\":\"样本存在选择偏差（由作者网络发起，虽经多渠道扩散但仍可能偏向特定群体）；自我报告的意见主观性强，不一定代表广泛的实际经验；定义可能缺乏共识；仅反映观点而非客观临床结果。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::58cec9b865f75116325cab3c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"老年患者（>70岁）\",\"finding\":\"74%的医生认为ICI在老年患者中的安全性和有效性等同于年轻患者；但承认该领域仍有重要证据缺口。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6980f2c5b915fb7b596040f9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"ECOG PS 0-2 vs PS 3-4\",\"finding\":\"94%同意治疗PS 0-2患者；36%同意治疗PS 3患者；仅6%认为PS 4合理。多数（63%）认为PS 2-3患者缺乏证据。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::60341f6cf52d4d3f131b80f3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"无症状 vs 有症状脑转移\",\"finding\":\"81%相信ICI对无症状脑转移有效；仅30%同意治疗有症状脑转移。后者被视为第二大研究优先级。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::63c21e6923221667803db965\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"自身免疫疾病（AIDs）\",\"finding\":\"77%仅在低严重程度情况下治疗；74%认为安全性较差，但65%认为疗效相似。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5b0aaf48f0f8d7206265fb06\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"HIV感染\",\"finding\":\"近60%认为控制良好的HIV患者ICI安全有效；对于未控制HIV，约50%医生不确定或认为存在差异。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6cf8b3e8698f6301f7a11732\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"实体器官移植\",\"finding\":\"大多数拒绝治疗心脏（69%）、肺（67%）或肝脏（59%）移植患者；肾脏移植拒绝率较低（42%）。医生表现出防御性行为，承认缺乏知识。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bb4aee60aad6b4020e4c26e6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"糖皮质激素剂量阈值\",\"finding\":\"医生对降低ICI效力的激素剂量阈值意见不一：37%认为是0-10mg，34%是11-30mg，11%是>30mg，15%不知道。48%认为抗生素可能降低ICI效力。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fe5c195d98e0415447c69124\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"肠道微生物组\",\"finding\":\"61%相信调节肠道菌群可能增加ICI疗效；认为这是一个重要的未来挑战。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::101d88dd7f159d723f94da6e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"超进展（HPD）与假性进展（PPD）\",\"finding\":\"62%报告诊断过HPD，81%报告过PPD。讨论指出医生可能低估HPD高估PPD，且机制尚不明确。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6777267f4ce927960eca6281\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"治疗持续时间\",\"finding\":\"90%同意治疗持续时间是重要挑战；大多数医生即使达到完全缓解也不会在24个月前停药。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::180740df6c1985892130b93e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"疗效预测因子\",\"finding\":\"被63%的医生投票为最重要的未来研究挑战。目前PD-L1预测价值有限，TMB争议大，其他生物标志物正在研究中。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e0942a3f99d4c2c0070f179f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::122ca4b0f3810fb148bbb794\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管ICI改变了NSCLC的治疗格局，但关键临床试验排除了许多真实世界常见患者群体（如老年人、脑转移、合并症患者），导致临床证据存在缺口。本研究试图明确医生在实际操作中遇到的主要挑战，并确定哪些领域最需要前瞻性临床研究来填补证据空白。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::88701ff49db3112307221f93\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者使用免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）单药治疗的临床实践挑战；调查对象为有ICI治疗经验的肿瘤科医生，重点关注老年人群、体能状态（PS）、脑转移、合并症（自身免疫病、HIV、器官移植）、伴随用药（激素、抗生素）、肠道微生物组影响、疗效预测因子、治疗持续时间及不典型反应等情境。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::60a2f20875af05d3fe99a0bc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本研究旨在评估肿瘤科医生在NSCLC临床实践中使用ICI单药治疗时面临的主要挑战和知识空白。通过Oncodistinct跨国研究网络发起了一项在线问卷调查，涵盖18个具体主题和一个开放性问题。问卷经过两轮专家试点测试验证。数据收集于2019年9月至2020年2月，采用雪球法传播。最终分析纳入106名完全填写问卷且自报治疗过至少20名NSCLC患者的医生的回答。结果以描述性统计呈现，识别了临床决策中的不确定性领域和优先研究方向。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cfac5899880e3cc0c32dd898\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文通过调查肿瘤科医生的意见，量化了ICI单药治疗NSCLC中未被充分研究的临床场景的重要性排序。对于综述而言，它提供了关于哪些临床情境（如脑转移、合并症、伴随用药）被认为最具挑战性且急需证据的专家视角，并指出了当前生物标志物预测能力的不足。特别地，它确认了肠道微生物组和抗生素使用作为潜在疗效调节因素的临床关注度。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7a0d2c48407b62f03e6e40c9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这是基于医生意见的调查数据，而非直接的微生物组机制研究或临床干预结果。未提供具体的微生物种类或代谢产物数据。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了临床医生对肠道微生物组影响ICI疗效的认知现状：61%的医生认为调节肠道菌群可增加ICI疗效，且将其列为重要挑战。同时提到质子泵抑制剂也可能通过影响微生物组降低ICI疗效。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::efc7e397075ef5d4d8a3d1e9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"主要引用回顾性研究和观察性研究的相关性，未阐明具体的分子或免疫学机制。机制部分（如HPD/PPD的生物机制）明确指出尚未完全理解。\",\"contribution\":\"讨论了抗生素可能通过改变肠道微生物组导致菌群失调（dysbiosis），进而与较低的ICI结局相关。提及粪菌移植（FMT）和活体生物疗法正在临床试验中被探索以增强ICI疗效。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e916c605e8ffda8e1c358b7d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"医生将疗效预测因子（63%）、脑转移治疗（第二高优先级）、治疗持续时间（90%认为重要）列为最关键的未满足需求。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3431ae98da9ff498b694c975\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"揭示了临床试验证据（如CheckMate系列）与真实世界临床决策之间的差距，例如医生对PS 3患者、有症状脑转移患者的治疗态度与指南推荐的差异。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::28881b85a91dc1d14c0920bf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"指出HPD和PPD的定义缺乏共识，医生感知与文献报道的发生率存在差异。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a48c95293a076d6755ab8849\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"本材料反映的是医生的主观意见和感知，而非客观的临床结果或机制证据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5a9e3521a341ed8771bca03d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"样本主要来自欧洲（80%），可能存在地域文化或医疗体系带来的偏差。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f7b963187b0476e625b6c1d6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"关于微生物组和抗生素的内容主要是关联性观察和医生信念，不能直接推导因果关系。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f0436439012b08a4563f16c6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"未提供具体的微生物组测序数据或机制实验细节，仅作为临床需求的背景。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f0a93a43126b46cd5b6dfe65\",\"source_handle\":\"P0524\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s119\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0be2b85ecad3848b4b6bd3bb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d75f9e2f8d75e5d4121db45c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a61414ebf37d6e26fb25c8ab\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用系统性文献回顾与综合的方法。作者梳理了关于肠道微生物群组成、功能及其与宿主免疫互作的现有研究，重点归纳了从分子机制（信号通路、代谢途径）到临床前模型证据，再到早期临床试验数据的多层次信息。文章按机制分类（特定菌株、代谢物、生物活性成分、昼夜节律）和组织治疗策略（饮食、FMT、LBPs等）进行逻辑编排，未提供新的原始实验数据，而是对已有证据进行分类、解释和综合评议。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7989217ee9a26ec028a34cad\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"系统整合了肠道微生物群调节ICI疗效的多维机制，包括菌株特异性效应、代谢物介导的信号通路及昼夜节律维度；提供了从基础机制到临床转化策略的全面图谱。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代具体的文献检索策略、纳入排除标准及质量评估方法；主要依赖已发表文献的综合，缺乏对异质性的大规模定量Meta分析；部分结论基于动物模型，临床验证尚处于早期阶段。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bf373bb67b77ec20f45b7a31\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"基于小鼠模型及部分人类队列观察\",\"finding\":\"特定益生菌株（如LGG、B. breve JCM92、C. butyricum）可通过激活DCs、促进CD8+ T细胞浸润或减少Tregs来增强ICI疗效；而某些病原体（如F. nucleatum的不同存在形式）可能通过代谢物介导免疫抑制或局部激活适应性抵抗。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a6217b254e21a2974b6c3c63\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"体外及动物实验机制研究\",\"finding\":\"微生物代谢物（丁酸盐、ICA、肌苷、UB）通过表观遗传修饰、受体激活（AHR, A2aR）等途径直接调节T细胞功能和分化；但某些代谢物（琥珀酸、4-HPA、脱氧胆酸）可诱导MDSCs浸润或Treg积累，导致ICI耐药。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::41de4893349e5dda8838775b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"跨学科理论推导与初步临床观察\",\"finding\":\"肠道微生物群和免疫细胞均具有昼夜节律，干扰节律可能导致代谢紊乱和免疫抑制；同步ICI给药时间与免疫/微生物节律高峰可能提高疗效（时间免疫治疗概念）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::40c304f2af6e24d9727997ce\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2dc8864454dd12af0d85f50c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"解决结直肠癌中大多数MSS患者对ICI治疗原发性耐药的临床困境，探索通过调节肠道微生物群来增强ICI疗效的潜在机制和治疗策略。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::94e811e66263ba6df8d78a76\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"结直肠癌（CRC），特别是微卫星稳定型（MSS）患者对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）的耐药问题；聚焦肠道微生物群及其代谢产物、生物活性成分在调节ICI疗效中的双重作用，以及昼夜节律的影响。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::afe7ad26d480688d4c9f3392\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇综述，旨在阐明肠道微生物群如何通过特定菌株、代谢物和生物活性成分调节宿主免疫系统，进而影响结直肠癌中ICIs的疗效。文章首先分析了有益菌和致病菌通过抗原呈递、T细胞浸润及免疫抑制细胞调控等机制对ICI反应的双向影响；其次探讨了微生物代谢物（如短链脂肪酸、色氨酸代谢物、肌苷等）作为免疫调节信使的作用；接着引入了肠道微生物群与宿主免疫细胞的昼夜节律交互概念，提出时间免疫治疗的潜力；最后综合了饮食干预、粪便微生物移植（FMT）、益生菌/益生元补充及靶向抗生素等临床转化策略，并评估了其成熟度与挑战。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::45e4d9250c21caec00f4a3d1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为“肠道微生物群如何调节实体瘤ICI疗效”这一核心问题提供了详尽的机制分类框架和临床策略评估。其价值在于将分散的菌株、代谢物和节律研究整合为一个连贯的解释体系，特别适用于构建关于微生物-免疫互作机制的综述章节，并为评估不同干预手段（FMT vs LBPs vs 饮食）的临床证据等级提供参考。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::adea10aba1e36bb84bfa3998\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"多数机制证据来自小鼠模型，人类临床相关性多为相关性研究或早期试验，因果链条在人体内的确证程度不一。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物群影响ICI疗效的具体生物学路径：包括通过DCs成熟、CD8+ T细胞招募/活化、Treg/M2 TAM抑制来增强抗肿瘤免疫，以及通过代谢物诱导MDSCs/Treg来抑制免疫。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b404ca97dff2ff1c948e1bcf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制描述多基于体外或动物实验，部分通路在人体肿瘤微环境中的确切角色尚需更多临床数据支持；不同菌株/代谢物的效应具有高度情境依赖性。\",\"contribution\":\"详细描述了介导效应的具体分子机制：如cGAS/STING通路、HDAC抑制、AHR/A2aR受体信号、TLR4/NF-kB通路等；并区分了不同代谢物（如丁酸盐vs琥珀酸）的相反作用。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::42f9bb5ec25209a85ca2ee7e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"该领域研究处于起步阶段，人体内的具体节律同步策略尚未标准化，证据多为理论推导或小规模观察。\",\"contribution\":\"提出了昼夜节律作为调节微生物-免疫互作的新维度，指出节律紊乱可能导致代谢异常和免疫抑制，而时间给药可能优化疗效。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7122c492de11ff5cd5a81b4e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"综述中Table 1总结了饮食、FMT、益生菌/益生元、靶向抗生素四种策略的原理、代表物质、临床成熟度（Level 0-2）及挑战。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::002d0d635179c80da9c8da0d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文中提到商业益生菌在黑色素瘤患者中可能与较差的ICI反应相关，强调菌株特异性和定植失败风险。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::073ee8d1f69f6dce1f884a1b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"讨论了厌氧菌的储存、胃酸耐受、制剂技术（包埋、冻干、孢子）等转化障碍。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::731261fac8e7206de02c3682\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述主要聚焦结直肠癌（CRC），虽然提及黑色素瘤等其他实体瘤作为类比，但其核心机制和临床数据主要源于CRC研究，外推至其他实体瘤时需考虑肿瘤微环境的差异。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::07a304c9811c3d5e2bf7ad29\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的许多机制（如特定菌株的作用）主要基于小鼠模型，人类体内的复杂生态系统和个体差异可能导致结果不同，需谨慎解读因果性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e29c6b7635fa985315443e61\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"昼夜节律部分多为理论探索和初步证据，尚未形成标准化的临床治疗方案，不应视为既定事实。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::365380f2d431637a3205386a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"对于“超级供体”等概念，综述指出其存在性尚未完全证实，应避免将其作为确定的科学结论引用。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7c5d3e0d3bfbb9f3b3c2811f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-4dcc7c19ae5301df5638\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-d48cd64bd12b302ad2ba\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-1c552864f10e55d2639d\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-76a4a344a1a9861e53c5\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-57c86dec56d8ae37b5be\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"kind\":\"assets\",\"reason\":\"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\"status\":\"missing\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f41de8a0023f3ed5dc879900\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e09ecaeff3665610ee375bfa\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b27d11a4cf958b094b9096a4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"作为一篇综述，本文采用概念扩展与多组学综合路线。首先，通过类比宇宙学中的“暗物质”，提出并定义“癌症暗物质”的新内涵，将其从单纯的癌细胞内在异常扩展到整个肿瘤微环境的复杂相互作用。其次，分章节详细论述不同层面的“暗物质”：1) 病毒模拟（VM）及其引发的免疫反应；2) 非编码RNA（T-UCRs）和非规范蛋白（ncORFs）的作用；3) 多组学技术（基因组、转录组、蛋白质组、代谢组、离子组、微生物组）在识别这些要素中的应用；4) 人工智能在多组学数据整合与分析中的作用。最后，探讨针对这些“暗物质”的治疗策略，如液体活检监测、基于ncORF的免疫疗法及微生物组调节。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e27bbd4e1149741c27e65033\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提出了“癌症暗物质”的扩展定义，将研究视角从单一的癌细胞内在突变扩展到包含微生物组、代谢物和离子平衡在内的整个TME生态系统。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代具体的实验验证数据，主要为理论框架和文献综述；对于某些机制（如特定ncORF的功能）的详细分子路径描述可能依赖于引用而非本研究原创数据。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::52c38d7e3a9d69f7fec13c01\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"系统总结了多组学技术（特别是质谱、单细胞测序、宏基因组学）在揭示癌症免疫学隐藏层面上的应用潜力和方法论进展。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代各技术在实际临床转化中的具体成功率、成本效益分析或标准化程度；部分技术应用仍处于早期阶段。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8d0dc0277036cb1f22c8130d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"强调了“病毒模拟”作为连接表观遗传异常与固有免疫反应的关键桥梁，为增强免疫治疗敏感性提供了新的机制解释。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代VM在不同癌症类型中的普遍性差异及个体间变异的具体量化数据；VM诱导的细胞死亡与免疫原性细胞死亡（ICD）的重叠机制尚需更多实证支持。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6dba659dc8e8f1a92e6f3d8a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"在癌症细胞中，特别是在存在表观遗传失调或DNA损伤的情况下\",\"finding\":\"内源性逆转录病毒（ERVs）的激活导致双链RNA（dsRNA）积累，引发“病毒模拟”（VM），进而激活干扰素刺激基因（ISGs），招募并激活CD8+ T细胞，形成免疫排斥常数（ICR）特征。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::196a97718b5b6019ccd08b7d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"在非编码基因组区域\",\"finding\":\"非规范开放阅读框（ncORFs）和转录超保守区域（T-UCRs）可产生非规范肽段或调控性RNA，这些产物在正常组织中不表达，因此被视为“外来”抗原，具有高度免疫原性，可作为个性化免疫治疗的靶点。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::704d0e893ed1e1ad020b1e48\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"在肿瘤微环境（TME）中\",\"finding\":\"肠道和肿瘤驻留微生物群通过代谢产物、免疫细胞信号和表观遗传修饰调节宿主免疫反应，特定细菌物种（如Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia muciniphila）与免疫检查点抑制剂（CPI）疗效正相关，而其他物种（如Fusobacterium nucleatum）则促进免疫逃逸。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::49d5d9b1b4a08dd42cbb901a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"应用多组学和人工智能时\",\"finding\":\"整合基因组、转录组、蛋白质组和代谢组数据，结合AI/ML算法，能够识别传统方法遗漏的低丰度生物标志物和非规范抗原，提高预测免疫治疗响应和患者生存率的准确性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::23e2dbdd103ad4a082674b6a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ff1549e2dd006e44224958c5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"传统的癌症研究主要关注编码区的基因突变和信号网络，但许多肿瘤生物学现象无法用此解释。作者试图解决的核心问题是：如何利用高通量技术和多组学整合，揭示那些被忽视的、类似病原体感染的“暗物质”机制（如病毒模拟、非规范肽段、微生物互作等），以阐明癌症免疫原性的真正驱动因素，并为克服免疫治疗耐药性和实现精准医疗提供新的理论框架和治疗靶点。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::48614036d2e2bbe827611111\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"肿瘤免疫学中的“暗物质”（cancer dark matter），涵盖癌症细胞内在的遗传、表观遗传和代谢异常，以及影响宿主在肿瘤微环境（TME）中反应的多种因素。重点讨论病毒模拟（VM）、非规范开放阅读框（ncORFs）、转录超保守区域（T-UCRs）、微生物组、离子组和代谢组等未被传统方法充分探索的领域。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9a4d94abf42b8e9761236bdb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"这是一篇综述文章，旨在重新定义并扩展“癌症暗物质”的概念，从仅指代癌细胞内在的非编码RNA和蛋白质，扩展到包括影响肿瘤微环境中细胞网络的更广泛元素。文章系统梳理了多组学技术（基因组、转录组、蛋白质组、代谢组、微生物组等）如何揭示这些隐藏的生物机制，特别是通过“病毒模拟”现象增强癌症细胞的免疫原性。它探讨了这些发现对理解免疫介导的癌症排斥、免疫逃逸及治疗耐药性的意义，并提出了利用这些新靶点开发个性化免疫疗法（如基于ncORF的疫苗和CAR-T细胞疗法）的策略。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bff525444300dffc8e973e17\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为理解肠道微生物组如何影响实体瘤免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效提供了重要的背景机制和概念框架。虽然它不是专门针对微生物组与ICI相互作用的原始研究，但它明确指出了微生物组是“癌症暗物质”的重要组成部分，并通过代谢产物、免疫调节和表观遗传修饰影响TME。它为后续深入探讨具体菌种（如Akkermansia）如何通过特定分子途径增强ICI疗效提供了理论支撑和多组学整合的研究思路。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::149d1d98058273f16a39f845\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"该论文未提供具体的因果机制细节或定量比较数据，仅列举了观察到的关联；不能直接用于证明某一特定菌株的确切作用机制，需结合其他原始研究。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物组作为癌症免疫治疗关键调节因子的宏观视角，指出特定细菌物种（如Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia muciniphila）与改善抗PD-1疗法反应相关，而另一些（如Fusobacterium nucleatum）则与免疫逃逸相关。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e37f99a06ddd2fc825d185b2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"所述机制多为概括性描述，缺乏针对特定微生物-ICI互作的详细分子实验证据；部分机制（如表观遗传交互）尚处于探索阶段，需谨慎推断其直接因果关系。\",\"contribution\":\"阐述了微生物组通过多种潜在机制影响宿主免疫的通路，包括：1) 微生物代谢产物（如短链脂肪酸）调节免疫细胞功能；2) 微生物信号与宿主免疫细胞信号的对话；3) 微生物组对化疗药物代谢的影响；4) 微生物组与表观遗传修饰的交互作用。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0168a5e7a0c7c39c21c5d7be\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"提出“癌症暗物质”的扩展定义，将微生物组、代谢物、离子平衡等纳入TME的整体调控网络，强调这些因素共同决定了免疫治疗的成败。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::114eba977f8a058e7bf20372\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"介绍了多组学技术（特别是宏基因组学、代谢组学、蛋白质组学）和人工智能在解析癌症复杂生物学中的应用，包括使用长读长测序进行微生物鉴定、ESI-MS检测代谢物等。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c0c46d51241b28d8acf09b38\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"讨论了通过饮食干预、粪便微生物移植（FMT）或益生菌调节微生物组以增强抗肿瘤免疫和改善治疗结果的潜力。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::88ab281331bd879e67fba058\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述侧重于概念扩展和技术综述，而非提供针对特定微生物株与ICI互作的因果实验数据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f320044833c2da13b318a824\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的微生物组与ICI疗效的关联多为观察性研究结果的汇总，具体机制仍需结合其他原始研究进行验证。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::062a089660836db946f94896\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"“癌症暗物质”是一个比喻性概念，实际涵盖范围广泛且部分机制尚未完全阐明，使用时需注意其不确定性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::24eccba0024aefdfcb90564b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"不同癌症类型中微生物组的作用可能存在显著差异，本综述未对所有实体瘤进行区分讨论，外推时需考虑癌种特异性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ec59dba3f443126c53d99a55\",\"source_handle\":\"P0323\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s099\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3ac3ba8f4cc6d753cbb83a54\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3d30e7b52b199af3a1391367\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ef0a5c9b57613de70521df55\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"As a review article, the approach involves a structured synthesis of literature rather than new empirical experimentation. The authors systematically: 1) Summarize clinical trial data associating specific gut microbiota profiles with ICI response in solid tumors; 2) Compare the advantages and limitations of traditional 2D cell lines, animal xenografts, and emerging 3D organoid models; 3) Detail the methodologies for generating immune-reactive organoids (endogenous retention vs. autologous co-culture); 4) Review selected studies demonstrating the application of these organoids in testing microbial metabolites and immunotherapies; 5) Discuss future perspectives and challenges in integrating microbiome components into organoid cultures.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::117625916b47e68f4be38c99\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Provides a comprehensive synthesis of clinical evidence linking gut microbiota to ICI response in solid tumors, identifying key taxa and metabolic pathways involved.\",\"limits\":\"Does not present new primary data; relies on summarizing existing heterogeneous clinical studies where biomarkers are not yet standardized.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c2848590accd421eb41647f2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Critically evaluates the limitations of current preclinical models (2D and animal) and advocates for immune-reactive organoids as a bridge between reductionist models and complex in vivo systems.\",\"limits\":\"The discussion of organoid capabilities is largely prospective or based on a limited set of recent proof-of-concept studies; widespread validation and standardization of these models are still ongoing challenges.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5a9f8b2e79b6779dd60b553c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Outlines specific methodologies for creating immune-reactive organoids (endogenous vs. co-culture) and highlights their potential for personalized medicine and mechanistic dissection of microbiome-immune interactions.\",\"limits\":\"Technical challenges such as maintaining viable immune cells and live bacteria in long-term culture, as well as the cost and scalability of patient-derived organoids, are acknowledged but not fully resolved within the scope of this review.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::552be2a15f5e9f0d75dbb07c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Clinical association studies across melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, and other solid tumors treated with ICIs\",\"finding\":\"Higher gut microbiome diversity and richness are generally associated with improved clinical response to ICIs. Specific taxa such as Akkermansia muciniphila, Bifidobacterium spp., Prevotella spp., and Ruminococcaceae are enriched in responders, while Proteobacteria and certain Firmicutes are often higher in non-responders. However, no single biomarker is consistently predictive across all cohorts.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1ca066ac33678ae8661177bc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Mechanistic studies involving microbial metabolites and immune modulation\",\"finding\":\"Microbial metabolites like short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs) and inosine can modulate systemic immunity, promoting T-cell differentiation and enhancing the efficacy of checkpoint inhibitors. For example, Bacteroides pseudolongum-derived inosine enhances anti-PD-1 efficacy via UBA6 inhibition.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cbeb57c141c65478bbb24358\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Evaluation of immune-reactive organoid platforms\",\"finding\":\"Immune-reactive organoids preserve patient-specific heterogeneity and allow for the study of spatial immune infiltration and drug response. Co-culture systems with autologous immune cells have shown high predictive accuracy (e.g., 85% in melanoma) for clinical ICI outcomes compared to 2D cultures or animal models.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3b59456e52104772902d3506\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0f20a9beca06842928086873\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"The review addresses the gap between clinical observations of microbiome-ICI associations and the lack of robust, human-relevant preclinical models to mechanistically dissect these interactions. It questions how current models fail to capture the complexity of the tumor-immune-microbiome axis and proposes immune-reactive organoids as a solution to predict patient-specific responses and understand underlying mechanisms.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::67a86efa0ce7593078af701a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"The review focuses on the intersection of cancer immunotherapy, specifically immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) in solid tumors, and the gut microbiome. It evaluates various preclinical models, with a primary emphasis on immune-reactive tumor organoids as a platform to study these interactions.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f7fca2ab6a28ec9acd7cc403\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"This paper is a narrative review that argues for the utility of immune-reactive tumor organoids in deciphering how the microbiome influences cancer immunity and response to immunotherapies. It begins by outlining the clinical evidence linking gut microbiota composition to ICI outcomes in solid tumors, summarizing key findings from multiple clinical trials regarding specific bacterial taxa and metabolites. The review then critiques existing modeling systems (2D cultures and animal models), highlighting their limitations in capturing human-specific immune-microbiome-tumor dynamics. It proposes immune-reactive organoids—created either by retaining endogenous immune cells or co-culturing autologous immune cells with tumor organoids—as a superior ex vivo platform. The authors discuss recent experimental data using these organoid systems to test microbial metabolites and checkpoint blockade efficacy, assessing their validity for personalized medicine and mechanistic insight.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::710160eba78c40d56ceac34b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"This review serves as a critical background source for understanding why advanced in vitro models like immune-reactive organoids are necessary to study microbiome-ICI interactions. It provides a curated summary of clinical associations between specific gut bacteria/metabolites and ICI efficacy in solid tumors, which helps contextualize the biological phenomena that these novel models aim to replicate. It also offers a comparative analysis of modeling platforms, justifying the shift towards organoid-based approaches for mechanistic studies.\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::da420b78163a0f5db3eb844c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"The review notes that biomarkers are cohort-dependent and no single species is universally predictive. It does not provide causal proof for all observed associations, only correlations and some mechanistic hypotheses.\",\"contribution\":\"Summarizes clinical evidence showing that specific gut microbiota profiles (e.g., Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and higher diversity are associated with better response rates to ICIs in solid tumors like melanoma and NSCLC. It details interventions like FMT that restore responsiveness.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bb61b58fb0d1d6804d9ba48d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"The mechanistic explanations are largely derived from cited studies or theoretical frameworks; the review itself does not perform new mechanistic experiments. The link between specific metabolites and specific immune cell subsets in organoids is presented as an emerging capability rather than a settled consensus.\",\"contribution\":\"Describes proposed mechanisms such as antigen mimicry, pattern recognition receptor activation, and metabolite-mediated immune modulation (e.g., SCFAs promoting T-cell differentiation). It highlights how immune-reactive organoids can be used to test these mechanisms ex vivo.\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7a8fdebea3aa34093c9f5dbc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Comparison of 2D cell lines, animal xenografts, and organoids, highlighting that animal models lack human-specific immune/microbiome structures and 2D cultures lack tissue context.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f5c6b6a9c205447afedaced3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"References to FMT, probiotic administration (Bifidobacterium), and dietary changes improving ICI outcomes in clinical and preclinical settings.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::29fb8b81d3fe12b1957c0a8c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Discussion of difficulties in culturing live bacteria with tissues, oxygen gradients, and maintaining immune cell viability in organoids.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a997799b6cb6d22bb2bcb0cb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The review is a narrative synthesis, not a systematic meta-analysis; clinical associations should be treated as reported trends rather than definitive causal rules.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e1126cdad0578d28fd60410c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Organoid data cited are from specific proof-of-concept studies; generalizations about organoid performance should acknowledge the variability and ongoing development of these platforms.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::924c1f351a832727b6a0ce44\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The term 'immune-reactive organoids' encompasses different methodologies (endogenous retention vs. co-culture); distinctions between these approaches should be maintained when applying findings.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a7dbfe07425aaf9fdc7d2b33\",\"source_handle\":\"P0416\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s133\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::06ed26dcdd1079324f495536\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d2a864b8d839638970ff124b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0ce1b951dbdb5d2b97b5edac\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"作为一篇综述，本研究通过系统性梳理现有文献，归纳了ICI耐药的多组学机制（第2节），分类总结了不同癌症类型中AI整合多组学的代表性研究及其性能指标（Table 2, 第3节），分析了AI在临床决策支持（如组合疗法推荐、影像病理工作流嵌入）中的具体应用案例（第4节），并评估了从实验室到临床转化的现实挑战（数据标准化、隐私、伦理、成本）及新兴技术趋势（第5节）。未进行新的原始实验或系统检索流程报告。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5060ee12ac9d77c757e11b38\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了ICI耐药机制的多组学全景图，并将AI技术定位为整合这些复杂数据的关键工具；总结了当前AI多组学模型在不同癌症类型中的性能表现和应用模式。\",\"limits\":\"作为综述，其结论依赖于所引用的原始研究的质量和设计；大多数被引用的AI模型基于回顾性队列，缺乏大规模前瞻性随机对照试验（RCT）的最终验证；作者未提供新的实证数据来证明所述模型的普适性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4dfc07039e516d5ef86ad422\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）、黑色素瘤、肾细胞癌（RCC）等多种实体瘤\",\"finding\":\"多组学整合模型（结合基因组、转录组、影像或微生物组）的预测性能（AUC通常0.70-0.85）普遍优于单一标志物（如PD-L1或TMB，AUC约0.6-0.7），能更准确区分响应者与无响应者。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::87abb19ba45c4ce814542c99\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"肠道微生物群分析\",\"finding\":\"特定菌群（如Bacteroides, Prevotella）丰度与ICI疗效正相关；抗生素使用或菌群失调导致疗效下降；粪菌移植（FMT）在部分研究中显示出逆转耐药的潜力。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7cecb6d0693e3c6ac5332efd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"AI模型可解释性应用\",\"finding\":\"SHAP和Grad-CAM等方法能将黑盒模型的预测结果映射回具体的生物学特征（如CXCL9表达、特定突变、组织形态区域），增强了临床信任并为机制假设提供依据。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::48aaab455fe838ba03e358ca\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"临床转化场景\",\"finding\":\"AI不仅用于预测疗效，还能指导联合治疗策略（如针对高干细胞特征肿瘤推荐EGFR靶向药，针对高乳酸产生肿瘤推荐代谢抑制剂），并在新辅助治疗和液体活检监测中展现潜力。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2faae73a5abbb524cdb5d353\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::24426b4854770279981b458a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"单一生物标志物（如PD-L1、TMB）在预测ICI疗效方面存在局限性，无法全面捕捉肿瘤-免疫相互作用的复杂性。如何整合多维度的多组学数据，并利用AI技术从中提取具有临床实用价值的预测性生物标志物和机制见解，以优化ICI治疗策略？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::406ebe1accda247117c3612d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）治疗背景下的肿瘤-免疫系统相互作用，涵盖基因组、转录组、表观基因组、代谢组、微生物组及影像组学等多组学数据；重点讨论人工智能（AI/ML）在整合这些数据以预测疗效、指导联合治疗及临床转化中的应用。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ac9389505740129b9be6d70f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇综述，旨在总结AI驱动的多组学生物标志物在免疫检查点阻断治疗中的作用。文章首先梳理了ICI疗效与耐药性的生物学基础，包括谱系可塑性、抗原呈递缺陷、代谢-表观遗传抑制、微生物群调节及干细胞特性等机制。随后，阐述了如何利用机器学习（如LASSO、随机森林、深度学习CNN）和深度学习方法整合异构多组学数据，构建复合预测模型，并强调可解释性工具（如SHAP、Grad-CAM）在连接模型输出与生物学机制中的重要性。最后，讨论了这些工具在患者分层、联合疗法选择、新辅助治疗指导及纵向监测中的临床应用，并指出了数据异质性、前瞻性验证不足、隐私限制、模型漂移及公平性等转化障碍，提出了单细胞/空间多组学整合、联邦学习及生成式建模等未来方向。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0d964473f3bf7109a81da614\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为理解肠道微生物群如何影响固体瘤对ICI的疗效提供了丰富的机制背景和临床关联证据。它详细描述了微生物组成分（如特定菌属）与免疫反应状态的关联，以及通过FMT或益生菌干预的潜在因果路径。同时，文中提到的AI模型如何识别微生物特征并将其与其他组学数据整合以预测疗效，为回答“机制”和“效应”问题提供了方法论视角和具体实例。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::80b156784a5f17ec10ed3cf2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"主要基于回顾性研究和小型试点试验；FMT效果存在个体差异且可能引入抑制性代谢物；未提供大规模确证性因果关系证据。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物群组成（如Bacteroides和Prevotella物种的富集）与ICI疗效改善之间的观察性关联证据；指出抗生素使用导致的菌群破坏与较差预后相关；提及FMT在部分研究中将耐药转化为响应的初步概念验证。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::385432c46d26b970b5c3ca3e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制描述多为推论性或基于动物模型/小规模人类研究的汇总；具体代谢物介导的详细分子通路在本综述中未深入展开，需参考原文引用的具体研究。\",\"contribution\":\"阐述了微生物群通过全身免疫调节影响ICI疗效的潜在机制：有益菌群促进Th1相关反应和树突状细胞激活，增强T细胞 priming；不利菌群则促进调节性T细胞（Tregs）或髓系抑制细胞（MDSCs）。还提到微生物代谢物（如短链脂肪酸等，虽未详述但暗示代谢联系）的影响。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::27a8f0d788828c3de3b22824\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"AI模型（如随机森林、深度学习）用于识别与良好预后相关的微生物物种；多模态集成优于单模态预测。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::004369712d2190eb43167187\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"不同中心的数据异质性、联邦学习的潜力、模型漂移风险、少数族裔代表性不足的问题。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::268cbb026203d1c9c6a3a3fd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述涵盖多种癌症类型，包括血液恶性肿瘤（如DLBCL），但在回答针对“固体瘤”的问题时，需仔细筛选仅适用于固体瘤的证据（如NSCLC, HCC, Melanoma, RCC等），排除仅基于血液瘤的研究结果。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7c9ca5b7bdf45baf4cdfb729\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的微生物组与ICI疗效的关联多为观察性研究或小样本试点，不能直接推断为因果必然性；FMT的效果并非在所有患者中一致。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2b90b5f072d0f34b0c7a5405\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"AI模型的性能指标（如AUC）来自不同研究，可能存在过拟合或验证不充分的情况，需谨慎解读其泛化能力。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1acbfe405aeaeafd19c2b9dd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0050\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s083\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::be5433584228331fa9932c6c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ef502cfdbea7a131b714b757\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::afae07208eb7b402094ef87d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"作为一篇综述，本研究采用定性综合的方法。作者检索并筛选了关于AI在多组学分析中应用的文献，按主题分类：1) ICI响应的生物学机制（基因、表观、代谢、微生物）；2) AI算法在数据处理和特征提取中的应用；3) 预测模型的构建与性能评估；4) 临床转化挑战与未来方向。通过归纳不同癌症类型（如NSCLC、黑色素瘤、HCC等）的研究案例，总结AI-多组学集成的模式、优势及局限性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::45e2edd4cbc10440b9d83ce3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了AI-多组学在ICI研究领域的全面框架，涵盖了从生物学机制到临床应用的完整链条，特别强调了微生物组和代谢组的作用。\",\"limits\":\"作为叙事性综述，未进行定量荟萃分析；所引用的研究多为回顾性或早期临床试验，缺乏大规模前瞻性随机对照试验的证据支持；不同研究间的模型性能和数据预处理方法差异较大，难以直接比较。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b1cd20585f97af6ed463ce8f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"多种实体瘤（如NSCLC, HCC, 结直肠癌等）\",\"finding\":\"AI整合多组学数据（如影像+基因组+转录组）能显著优于单一生物标志物（如TMB或PD-L1），在预测ICI响应方面表现出更高的AUC（例如DenseNet模型在NSCLC中AUC>0.80）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2dfae72d584f66d8e321a1a6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"肠道微生物组分析\",\"finding\":\"特定菌群（如Bacteroides caccae, Prevotella copri）丰度与ICI响应正相关，抗生素使用导致的菌群失调与耐药相关；AI可识别这些微生物特征并预测疗效。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::913de4464db2b6d75d05700f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"肿瘤微环境与干细胞特性\",\"finding\":\"高干细胞评分（如MKI67/STMN1表达）和冷肿瘤微环境（免疫排斥）与较差的ICI预后相关；AI模型可识别这些特征并建议联合治疗（如化疗或靶向药）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f561d9e9ae6058249436548e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"解释性AI应用\",\"finding\":\"SHAP和Grad-CAM等工具可将AI预测结果映射到具体的生物学特征（如突变、组织形态区域），提高了模型的可解释性和临床信任度。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f1dd7e88ce14b4cd43719acd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ff55ae9f543d103b6be31e83\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"传统单一生物标志物（如PD-L1、TMB）对ICI疗效预测准确性有限，无法全面捕捉肿瘤异质性和动态免疫逃逸机制。如何利用AI整合多维多组学数据，以更精准地预测ICI响应、揭示耐药机制并指导个性化治疗？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1ebcb1344cda6182f0de3e02\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）在实体瘤及血液肿瘤中的应用，重点聚焦于AI驱动的多组学整合技术。涵盖基因组、转录组、表观基因组、代谢组、微生物组、病理学和影像组学等多维度数据，旨在解决ICI疗效预测和耐药机制不明的问题。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::631594cd50887263f619a56f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇叙事性综述，系统梳理了人工智能与多组学技术在预测免疫检查点抑制剂响应和耐药方面的最新进展。文章首先阐述了ICI疗效差异的生物学基础，包括肿瘤异质性、干细胞特性、微环境重塑及微生物组调控；随后介绍了AI算法如何整合异构多组学数据以发现生物标志物、构建预测模型并进行患者分层；接着讨论了这些模型在指导联合治疗、实时监测和毒性预测中的临床转化潜力；最后分析了实施障碍（如数据异质性、黑盒性质、缺乏前瞻性验证）并展望了单细胞/空间多组学、联邦学习和生成式AI等未来方向。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::426e08a68a7581bf4fd33ed9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为理解肠道微生物组如何调节实体瘤中ICI疗效提供了丰富的背景信息和机制线索。它汇总了微生物组特征（如特定菌属丰度、抗生素影响）与ICI响应之间的关联，并指出了AI在解析这种关联中的作用。虽然它不直接提供因果证据，但为综述中关于“微生物组调节机制”的部分提供了关键的假设来源和现有研究的概览，特别是关于菌群失调导致耐药的观察性证据。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1e3ef3ec2ff1e21321a4b09f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"仅为相关性观察，未证明因果关系；主要基于回顾性队列和小型干预研究，外推至所有实体瘤需谨慎。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物组组成（如Bacteroides, Prevotella）与ICI响应之间关联的观察性证据，以及抗生素使用对疗效的负面影响。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::82748b8529f7768537d88a94\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制多为推测性或基于动物/小样本研究，缺乏在大样本人群中验证的详细分子通路证据；具体介导分子（如短链脂肪酸的具体作用）需结合其他原始研究确认。\",\"contribution\":\"提出了微生物组通过调节全身免疫状态（如T细胞活性）和代谢产物影响ICI疗效的潜在机制，并指出FMT可能作为一种干预手段。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d620ad21cf0e985c0a988d2d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"综述中关于AI算法整合多模态数据的流程和挑战的描述。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cf6f8f8f1c8c69b7859dd22a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"关于肿瘤异质性、干细胞特性和乳酸化修饰的讨论。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9c3df0e28beb6af3be145e7b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述是叙事性的，其结论依赖于对所引用文献的选择性综合，可能存在发表偏倚。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3bfb0a1804ed3f4b4dc06a79\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"提到的微生物组关联多为观察性研究，不能直接推断因果；抗生素的影响也是间接证据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b6103fdb96b50522dc3225d1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"不同癌症类型的微生物组效应可能存在差异，不应将所有实体瘤的结果泛化为统一规律。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e28a5fa69ac8cb733bf41414\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"AI模型的性能指标（如AUC）在不同研究中不可直接比较，因为训练集、验证集和预处理方法各异。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ea97ab02cf3d96a0cc2456ce\",\"source_handle\":\"P0054\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s254\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5e9b2083132c1c3c4a13de1c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1cec54c74c4d18e12b8810fe\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::225847e797c5848ab97bbe8b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"作为一篇综述，本文采用了概念框架梳理与实证研究综合相结合的方法。首先，从宿主内在因素（年龄、性别、遗传）和外在因素（地理、生活方式、饮食、药物、疾病状态）多维度界定“健康”与“失调”的复杂性。其次，系统评估了用于检测和量化菌群失调的工具箱，包括粪便/血清生物标志物（如钙卫蛋白、SCFA、胆汁酸、sMAdCAM-1）、传统多样性指标、肠型、微生物群落（guilds）以及基于机器学习的多组学评分模型（重点介绍TOPOSCORE）。最后，综合了关于菌群失调干扰免疫通路（如胆汁酸代谢、屏障功能、T细胞 trafficking）的机制证据，并总结了正在进行的临床试验和国际合作倡议（ONCOBIOME）。文中引用了大量已发表的研究结果进行论证，而非报告新的独立实验数据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e6b4ec3536bfed5569957e0a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提出了一个整合性的框架，将菌群失调定义为生态韧性/抵抗力的破坏，而非简单的多样性丧失。引入了TOPOSCORE这一具体的、基于机器学习且可床旁转化的评分工具，用于个体化评估菌群失调程度。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代该综述是否进行了严格的文献质量评估或系统性检索流程。TOPOSCORE虽经回顾性验证，但 prospective validation（前瞻性验证）仍在进行中，其普适性需进一步确认。部分机制（如特定菌株的作用）主要基于动物模型或观察性研究，因果链条在人类中尚未完全确立。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::200c001346fd8431eea9af0a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"跨多种癌症类型（NSCLC, RCC, UC, CRC）及健康对照的宏基因组数据分析\",\"finding\":\"识别出两个拮抗的物种相互作用组（SIGs）：SIG1（含37种菌，与较差生存期相关，包括口腔来源菌和产胆汁酸厌氧菌）和SIG2（含45种菌，与较好预后相关，主要为丁酸盐产生菌）。TOPOSCORE基于SIG1/SIG2比例计算，能有效预测ICI疗效。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e8cd3bc0897a301a1d370642\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"不同宿主和环境因素对肠道微生物的影响\",\"finding\":\"年龄、性别、遗传、地理、饮食和药物均显著塑造微生物组。其中，药物（特别是抗生素、PPIs）和饮食是主要的可调节驱动因素。抗生素使用与ICI治疗后的无进展生存期和总生存期缩短相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c8bfa4f0c1c8726428d0c9a5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"菌群失调对免疫系统的机制性影响\",\"finding\":\"菌群失调通过多种途径影响免疫：1) 胆汁酸代谢改变导致MAdCAM-1下调，促进抑制性Tr17细胞迁移至肿瘤；2) 肠道屏障受损导致内毒素血症和全身炎症；3) 色氨酸代谢异常影响T细胞活性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1e3908ba4f68f0fdec14c7bd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"生物标志物的临床应用潜力\",\"finding\":\"sMAdCAM-1被提出作为癌症患者菌群失调的“肠道检查”生物标志物，低水平预示较差结局。粪便和血清中的代谢物（SCFA, BA, LPS衍生物）可作为功能性失调的指标。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0520404a962eeeeb652448cc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::abd31b01ef7c997eae560a3a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"当前微生物组科学向临床转化的主要障碍是什么？如何更准确地定义和测量肿瘤治疗中的“菌群失调”，以及其背后的机制和干预手段有哪些？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a011da2fafed15a190fa0d42\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"肿瘤学背景下的肠道微生物组，特别是其与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效及耐药性的关系；涵盖定义、生物标志物、机制及干预策略。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ea0ab8e9068f33e190fdea70\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"这是一篇综述论文，旨在解决肠道微生物组在临床转化中因“菌群失调”定义不一致、生物标志物框架不足及机制理解有限而面临的障碍。文章综合了现有知识，阐述了肠道微生物组成和功能如何影响ICI疗效，区分了相关性与因果证据。作者讨论了基于α-多样性或分类丰度的计算方法，并主张采用更具功能和临床信息量的模型（如TOPOSCORE）。通过回顾性分析数千名患者和对照组的宏基因组数据，研究了区分响应者和非响应者的微生物模式。此外，探讨了菌群失调如何干扰免疫调节通路（如胆汁酸代谢、肠道通透性和黏膜免疫调节），评估了纠正微生物功能障碍的 emerging 治疗策略（饮食、细菌联合体、FMT），并介绍了ONCOBIOME倡议及其全球Atlas平台。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::507d7c5b52fb8f5862d91d0f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为理解肠道微生物组如何调节实体瘤中ICI疗效提供了全面的机制背景和临床转化视角。它特别有价值地提供了关于“菌群失调”多维定义的证据，详细列举了关键的生物标志物（特别是sMAdCAM-1和代谢物），并深入解析了胆汁酸代谢、屏障功能和T细胞迁移等具体机制。此外，它还提供了关于微生物群落在ICI响应中的动态变化（SIGs）以及ONCOBIOME等大型倡议的最新进展，有助于构建综述中关于机制复杂性和临床挑战的部分。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::663d7149925b6ae8ef095827\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"主要基于回顾性分析和已发表的临床试验数据，因果关系需结合其他研究确认。不同癌种的微生物特征可能存在差异。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物组特征（如SIG1富集、低多样性、特定菌属缺失）与ICI疗效（响应vs非响应）之间的关联证据。指出了微生物组构成随时间变化的动态性，以及基线多样性不足以预测长期疗效，强调了纵向稳定性和功能群的重要性。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::89a7d1fe76dc83b7726264ec\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"许多机制细节来自小鼠模型或体外研究，在人体内的确切作用强度和普遍性尚待更多临床验证。某些机制（如TMAO的作用）具有情境依赖性。\",\"contribution\":\"详细阐述了菌群失调影响ICI疗效的具体机制路径：1) 胆汁酸代谢异常导致MAdCAM-1表达降低，进而允许抑制性Treg17细胞从肠道迁移至肿瘤微环境；2) 肠道屏障受损导致内毒素（LPS）易位，引发全身炎症和免疫抑制；3) 色氨酸代谢产物对T细胞活性的调节。还提到了Akkermansia muciniphila的双刃剑效应（适量有益，过量或缺失可能有害）。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::338f6f094d8db6441037f710\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"讨论了健康微生物组的定义困难，涉及年龄、性别、遗传、饮食、药物等多重因素。指出“eubiosis”不仅是缺乏病原体，而是生态韧性和抵抗力的体现。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::51f1209d3349e11e5d957d72\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"总结了FMT、饮食调整、益生菌/后生元等干预措施在临床试验中的进展，特别是IMMUNOLIFE2试验。指出FMT效果依赖于受体生态系统的接受度，且长期效果未知。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::61c0901c9746d99f0f358d64\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"介绍了ONCOBIOME倡议和Seerave Global OncoBiome Atlas，旨在标准化协议、整合多组学数据并开发诊断工具。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b33b090552e5c1063a528cfc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述主要关注实体瘤（肺癌、肾癌、尿路上皮癌、结直肠癌），其结论可能不完全适用于血液肿瘤或其他类型的癌症。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2b025d03013f2288e3c4b740\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"TOPOSCORE是基于特定队列开发的回顾性评分，其前瞻性验证结果未在本文中完全呈现，使用时需注意其验证阶段。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c11a7b1c3af9a72939daec25\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的许多机制（如Tr17细胞迁移、胆汁酸作用）主要基于动物模型或初步临床研究，在人类患者中的普遍性和重要性需谨慎解读。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4c274a2e97b6ee50f0686577\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"作者对Akkermansia muciniphila的描述提示了其作用的非线性（三态关系），避免简单将其视为单一的“有益菌”。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f34e94256a6cf11457a0aba8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0574\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s006\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::dd62b72099edd7c2ee1b6953\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8570782bc7b96368ab122840\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::255c1ac5573e1e3e404d5afb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"The authors conduct a narrative review by systematically categorizing existing literature on organoid-based microbiome-TME research. They structure the analysis around: (1) classification of organoid models and their comparative advantages; (2) specific mechanistic insights gained from organoid studies (e.g., inflammation, genotoxicity, metabolite effects); (3) technological integrations (multi-omics, organ-on-a-chip); and (4) clinical translation potential (drug screening, biomarkers). The approach involves summarizing findings from cited empirical studies, highlighting methodological trends, and providing critical commentary on the limitations of current organoid platforms.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::34fbab3b6c26d35b56f750aa\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Provides a comprehensive classification of organoid models (PDOs, ASC-derived, PSC-derived, etc.) and their specific applications in microbiome-TME research.\",\"limits\":\"Does not present new primary experimental data; relies on summarizing existing literature which may vary in quality and standardization.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::38b6482c083cd363f95fe98a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Critically evaluates the limitations of current organoid models, such as the absence of full immune/stromal components and difficulties in maintaining complex microbial communities.\",\"limits\":\"The assessment of limitations is based on general consensus in the field rather than a systematic meta-analysis of model performance metrics.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f08b54a40f1d8db4de67d102\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Highlights the potential of organoid-on-a-chip and multi-omics integration to overcome current physiological gaps.\",\"limits\":\"These advanced technologies are described as emerging trends with preliminary validation stages; their widespread clinical applicability remains unproven.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bcb64443b2bb8ea8ce0bd0ff\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"In organoid co-culture systems simulating chronic inflammation\",\"finding\":\"Microbial dysbiosis accelerates neutrophil infiltration and induces epithelial-mesenchymal transition (EMT), creating an immunosuppressive environment. Specific pathways like TNFR1/2 targeting TLR5-positive cells have been identified.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fd273960962ef4feb451eefa\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Using organoids exposed to specific bacterial strains or metabolites\",\"finding\":\"Certain bacteria (e.g., pks+ E. coli) induce mutation signatures in organoids consistent with colorectal cancer patients, demonstrating direct genotoxic effects. Metabolites like SCFAs and secondary bile acids modulate signaling pathways (e.g., Wnt/beta-catenin, NF-kB).\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::852f9fee4ba7fa3447ad9000\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"In PDO models with low alpha-diversity communities\",\"finding\":\"Low microbial diversity correlates with reduced MHC-I expression and decreased CD8+ T cell infiltration, suggesting a mechanism for immunotherapy resistance.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4c2d8085d15cf828fc2599fd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"When integrating organoids with multi-omics and AI\",\"finding\":\"Multi-omics integration reveals molecular drivers of host-microbe interactions but faces challenges in causal inference due to data heterogeneity and noise. AI can enhance analysis but requires dual validation.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4744c6b636c79a91192d6fdf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c393de2ae93d94a910b62657\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"To address the gap between conventional experimental models and the complex, dynamic reality of human tumor microenvironments, specifically regarding how gut microbiota influence cancer progression, immune response, and therapeutic efficacy. The review aims to evaluate the utility of organoids in capturing these interactions and identify remaining bottlenecks in translating these findings to precision medicine.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::57eb466c11cee4074bef8508\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"The review focuses on the application of intestinal organoids (including patient-derived, stem cell-derived, and cancer cell line-derived models) as in vitro tools to study the interactions between the gut microbiota and the Tumor Microenvironment (TME), particularly in colorectal cancer. It covers mechanistic insights into microbial dysbiosis, metabolite regulation, immune modulation, and clinical translation scenarios such as drug screening and biomarker discovery.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6f23f085b1ffa8ce1ede256a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"This review article synthesizes current research on how intestinal organoids serve as a bridge for understanding host-microbiota crosstalk within the tumor microenvironment. It details the technical advantages of organoids over traditional 2D cultures and animal models, classifies different types of organoid models, and discusses their applications in deciphering carcinogenic mechanisms driven by microbial dysbiosis, validating tumor-specific microbial features, and exploring bidirectional regulatory mechanisms of microbial metabolites. The paper also addresses the integration of multi-omics technologies and organ-on-a-chip systems to enhance physiological relevance, while critically evaluating limitations such as the lack of complete immune/stromal components and challenges in clinical translation.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c851f80fa6574a66fedb3577\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"This review provides a structured overview of how organoid models are used to investigate the impact of gut microbiota on solid tumors (specifically colorectal cancer) and their response to therapies. It offers valuable context on the mechanistic links between microbial metabolites, immune regulation, and tumor biology, which is relevant for understanding how the microbiome might modulate treatment efficacy. However, it primarily serves as a background resource on model capabilities and limitations rather than providing direct evidence on specific immune checkpoint inhibitor responses.\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0fb4c21263d13151340601ad\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"The review summarizes general associations and platform capabilities; it does not provide specific quantitative data on ICI efficacy modulation by distinct microbial taxa in solid tumors beyond colorectal cancer contexts implied by the focus.\",\"contribution\":\"Discusses how organoid models reveal that microbial dysbiosis and low alpha-diversity correlate with reduced MHC-I expression and CD8+ T cell infiltration, potentially contributing to immunotherapy resistance. It also mentions the use of organoids for screening immunotherapy drugs and evaluating microbiota-targeted modulation.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c217cf68944c1693aa81a2e7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Mechanisms are largely derived from in vitro organoid studies or animal models cited in the review; direct causal evidence in human ICI-treated solid tumors is not established by this source alone. The review notes controversies and incomplete elucidation of epigenetic regulation pathways.\",\"contribution\":\"Details mechanisms by which microbial metabolites (e.g., SCFAs, tryptophan catabolites, indole-3-acetic acid) regulate immune responses via receptor activation (e.g., AhR) and cytokine expression. It outlines pathways involving NF-kB, Wnt/beta-catenin, and PD-1/PD-L1 remodeling through stromal components.\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8eb8b18d1eb66f4d79bf43a9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Classification of organoid types (PDOs, ASC-derived, PSC-derived, cancer cell line-derived) and their respective advantages/limitations in modeling TME complexity.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::87ca3a987643b797d205c089\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Discussion of 'organ-on-a-chip' technology and its ability to simulate fluid flow, mechanical forces, and spatial gradients.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::767918fffb42fc0092043b18\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Mention of AI integration with low-biomass microbiome analysis and multi-omics data interpretation.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ceeec32b7353a2937b49cad2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The review focuses heavily on colorectal cancer and intestinal organoids; extrapolation to other solid tumors should be done with caution as the TME and microbiome composition differ significantly across cancer types.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ebe0cc71c6bcd5001050b0cf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Many mechanistic insights are derived from in vitro organoid models or animal studies cited within the review; these do not constitute direct clinical evidence from human ICI trials.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0c14d18e270937674dbe4e5a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The review emphasizes limitations such as the lack of full immune component reconstitution in standard organoids, meaning findings on immune modulation may underestimate the complexity of systemic immune responses.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5e2cdcb660a4282a1d40663d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Claims about 'personalized medicine' and 'clinical translation' are presented as potential or ongoing efforts, not as established clinical practices validated by this review.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0184c45c29f04c6a97b7f31b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0172\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-30c4d9a86f8c4e63ba33\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-8e42bf7b639e54875284\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-3163dd5592daeae30981\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"kind\":\"assets\",\"reason\":\"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\"status\":\"missing\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s252\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b41a6b145397ba4985cc8f23\",\"source_handle\":\"P0532\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s171\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::720a1b1f135db6f60292f895\",\"source_handle\":\"P0532\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s171\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::27849e2682f5ca0e4d6edbc7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0532\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用叙述性综述方法。作者系统检索并整理了近年来关于肠道微生物与各类癌症治疗相互作用的研究文献。结构上，先按治疗类型（放疗、化疗、靶向、免疫、中药、康复）分类讨论微生物的影响；再按生物学机制（代谢、免疫、生物物理、胞内定植、DNA损伤）归纳深层原理；最后评估临床转化现状与挑战。文中引用了大量动物模型实验、临床试验结果及体外研究数据，并通过图表（Figure 1, 2, 3; Table 1, 2）可视化关键微生物、治疗方式及机制之间的联系。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s171\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::10955ca45dfa3dfb1db68a2f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0532\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物影响多种癌症治疗模式的系统性框架，将分散的机制（代谢、免疫、生物物理等）与治疗类型（放化疗、免疫、靶向等）进行了交叉关联。\",\"limits\":\"作为综述，主要汇总已有观察性研究和部分临床前/临床证据，缺乏原创性的因果验证实验。所引用的机制多为相关性发现或动物模型结果，其在人类中的普适性和因果链条尚需更多功能性研究证实。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s171\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e29eef617749cc8ea9ecb1b0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0532\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"识别了关键的微生物标志物（如Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia, Fusobacterium）及其在不同治疗背景下的双向作用（增强疗效或导致耐药/毒性）。\",\"limits\":\"许多微生物-治疗关联仅在特定肿瘤类型或特定实验条件下观察到，存在显著的异质性。综述未提供具体的预测模型或标准化的临床干预方案。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s171\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c12092fd56c97aaaa22d771f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0532\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"强调了微生物干预的临床转化挑战，包括个体差异、安全性（如FMT风险）、标准化缺失及AI应用的潜力。\",\"limits\":\"对于如何解决这些挑战的具体技术路径（如AI模型的具体架构、工程菌的安全阈值）仅做概念性探讨，未提供实证数据支持。\"},\"role